\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone's use up to seven weeks in a pregnancy in 2000 and later extended that to 10 weeks. PHOTO: Natalie Behring for the Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 A new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  battle is moving to the courts, this time over a pill for ending pregnancies.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents sued the Food and Drug Administration and Health and Human Services department in federal court in Amarillo, Texas, on Friday, seeking to undo the approval of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -inducing pill }}}\uc2  called mifepristone as well as subsequent agency decisions easing access to the drug.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit argued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  exceeded its authority to approve the drug because the agency used a process meant for treatments of serious or life-threatening illnesses, and there wasn't scientific evidence to support the approval and other decisions.\par \par \uc2 Four doctors from Texas, who said they have treated patients harmed by the drug, and four antiabortion medical organizations filed the new lawsuit. They were represented by the \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  , a conservative legal group that helped challenge federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the Supreme Court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization case }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 FDA\uc2  has not followed the science, reversed course, or fixed its mistakes\u8212\'20\'14all to the detriment of women and girls. Instead, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has doubled down on its actions and removed the few safeguards that were in place," the lawsuit said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  approved mifepristone "more than 20 years ago based on a thorough and comprehensive review of the scientific evidence presented and determined that it was safe and effective for its indicated use\u8212\'20\'14medical termination of early pregnancy," an agency spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 HHS\uc2  spokeswoman said mifepristone was a safe and effective option for women seeking essential healthcare. "Denying women access to any essential care they need is downright dangerous," the spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers who specialize in the \uc2 FDA\uc2  and laws concerning administrative agencies couldn't recall any similar lawsuits by an outside group to remove a drug from the market.\par \par \uc2 The lawyers, who hadn't read the lawsuit, said that they expected a court to find that the plaintiffs had standing to bring the lawsuit, but that the challenge may be difficult to win because the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has appeared to move carefully on mifepristone and judges tend to defer to agencies.\par \par \uc2 "If they handle it well, \uc2 FDA\uc2  should prevail," said Daniel Kracov, an \uc2 FDA\uc2  lawyer at \uc2 Arnold & Porter\uc2  , which joined an alliance of other law firms this summer seeking to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Activists who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and lawyers said they expect more lawsuits over mifepristone, including on whether the \uc2 FDA\uc2  's power to regulate drugs overrides, or pre-empts, states' oversight of the practice of medicine.\par \par \uc2 "If the \uc2 FDA\uc2  pre-emption argument can win, it provides a lot more protection for the individuals taking the medication," said Ann O'Leary, a lawyer at \uc2 Jenner & Block\uc2  who heads the firm's task force to find legal strategies to defend \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
