\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Georgia's  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban After Six Weeks Is Blocked; State judge says portions of law, signed by Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  in 2019, were clearly unconstitutional when enacted\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 840 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2022\par 00:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Georgia judge permanently blocked enforcement of the state's ban on most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, ruling that it was clearly unlawful at the time the state legislature passed it in 2019.\par \par \uc2 Judge Robert McBurney of the Superior Court of Fulton County noted Tuesday that there has been a sea change in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law because of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling in June that overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  and ended federal constitutional protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the judge said that if Georgia wants to impose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, the legislature would need to revisit the issue and pass a new law.\par \par \uc2 The ban on most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy took effect in Georgia in July, about a month after the Supreme Court's decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization. The high court's ruling shifted questions about the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to the states.\par \par \uc2 Georgia Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-gov-brian-kemps-re-election-overcame-attacks-from-democrats-and-trump-11668076204"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Republican who was re-elected  }}}\uc2  last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-law-11557266086"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed the ban into law  }}}\uc2 . Georgia was one of several states to pass so-called "heartbeat bills" around that time. The law was previously blocked in federal court in proceedings that took place before the Supreme Court's June decision.\par \par \uc2 Judge McBurney's decision is a victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates in a state that could be an access point for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the south, but it rests on a provision of Georgia law that doesn't guarantee long-term protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The judge didn't rule on whether an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban passed in the future would violate the state's constitution. After the Dobbs ruling, a ban "may someday become the law of Georgia, but only after our legislature determines in the sharp glare of public attention" whether "the rights of unborn children justify such a restriction on women's right to bodily autonomy and privacy," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Following the ruling, Georgia \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, who had stopped performing abortions after six weeks of pregnancy, said they would resume appointments.\par \par \uc2 "We will have to keep fighting in Georgia to hold our legislators accountable, but this ruling proves we have the power to keep winning," said Monica Simpson, executive director of SisterSong Women of Color Reproductive Justice Collective, the case's lead plaintiff.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Georgia Attorney General's office\uc2  on Tuesday appealed the ruling to the state's Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Zemmie Fleck, executive director of Georgia Right to Life, said her organization has been pushing for legislators in the state to convene to adopt a so-called personhood amendment that would, in effect, ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She has criticized the 2019 law for not going far enough.\par \par \uc2 "This is the time to do the things to tighten the law," said Ms. Fleck.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere on Tuesday, Kentucky's highest court heard arguments on whether the state's constitution contains a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a week after voters in the Republican-leaning state rejected a bid to make explicit that its constitution contains no such right.\par \par \uc2 The Kentucky Supreme Court is considering whether to temporarily block enforcement of the state's ban while litigation proceeds. Last Tuesday, Kentucky voters rejected by 52% to 48% a proposed antiabortion constitutional amendment.\par \par \uc2 During the hearing, Deputy Chief Justice Lisabeth Hughes asked Kentucky Solicitor General Matthew Kuhn whether the court should ignore that vote. "It strikes me that a ballot initiative is the purest form of democracy," she said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kuhn said the vote didn't change the language of the constitution, which he said still contains no explicit protection for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He said the closeness of the vote underscored that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a divisive issue in the state, one better left up to the legislature to decide.\par \par \uc2 Last week's vote "does not add words to our constitution, does not change the meaning of the words that are already there," Mr. Kuhn said.\par \par \uc2 Heather Gatnarek, a lawyer with the American Civil Liberties Union of Kentucky who is representing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, argued that a provision of the Kentucky constitution that protects liberty encompasses the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Kentucky has a long and proud history of jealously guarding the liberty rights enshrined in our constitution," Ms. Gatnarek told the court.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What do you think lies ahead for the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kentucky? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 About a dozen states have banned many or most abortions since the Dobbs decision, but in many places the law remains in flux as courts consider whether state constitutions afford protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Lawmakers in at least a handful of states also still haven't settled on whether and to what extent to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgias-abortion-ban-after-six-weeks-is-blocked-11668540794"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia's \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban After Six Weeks Is Blocked  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221115eibf0063h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
