\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 In Races for Governor, Few States Change Control; Democrats fend off strong opponents in Wisconsin and New York, while Republicans \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Greg Abbott win big\b0\par\par\uc2 By Elizabeth Findell and Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 1,317 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2022\par 08:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gubernatorial elections }}}\uc2  resulted in few changes of control on Election Day, as Democrats held off challengers in several races that polls showed could be close including Wisconsin, New York and Michigan, while Republican incumbents won decisively in Florida and Texas, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Democrats also prevailed in the only two states to flip, Maryland and Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 One of the most hotly contested races in the nation was in Wisconsin, where incumbent Democrat \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  fended off Republican businessman \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2 , the AP projected. Mr. Evers ran on a platform of investing in education and infrastructure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-tight-wisconsin-governors-race-gerrymandering-takes-center-stage-11667730884"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposing gerrymandering }}}\uc2  and supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, while Mr. Michels said he would do more to fight crime and touted his support from former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In New York, incumbent Democratic Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  defeated Republican U.S. Rep. \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , according to the AP. Mr. Zeldin gained on her in recent polls, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lee-zeldin-targets-new-york-city-crime-as-polls-show-tightening-governors-race-11666357206"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which gave Republicans hope }}}\uc2  he could become the first candidate from their party to win statewide office in two decades as he focused on voter concern about rising crime. Ms. Hochul campaigned on her record from her year in office, including new gun-control laws, Covid-19 pandemic management and rebate checks for taxpayers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/ron-desantis-hails-win-in-florida-saying-i-have-only-begun-to-fight--KSknjATOE2wp5DHoW3RR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robust victories }}}\uc2  for Florida's \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Texas' Greg Abbott put the two men in strong positions as they prepare for possible presidential runs in 2024, according to political analysts. Both have focused on issues that appealed to their party's base.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Abbott, who defeated former U.S. Rep. \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2 , a Democrat, devoted much of his second term to immigration and border security. Mr. DeSantis, who won over Democrat \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , a former governor and U.S. representative, emphasized his stances on culture issues and his decision to reopen businesses in his state early in the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Michigan Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  defeated conservative political commentator Tudor Dixon, who criticized the incumbent for the length of Covid-19 shutdowns and pledged to expand the state's economy and stop the teaching of critical race theory in schools. Ms. Whitmer focused on her record repairing roads and increasing education spending.\par \par \uc2 New Mexico Democratic Gov. \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2  defeated former television meteorologist Mark Ronchetti, a Republican, according to the AP, in a race focused on issues including crime and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 In Maine, Democratic Gov. \uc2 Janet Mills\uc2  won re-election over former Republican Gov. Paul LePage, the AP said. Mr. LePage hammered the incumbent over energy costs, while Ms. Mills touted her efforts to diversify the state's energy sources.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania Democratic Attorney General \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  beat Republican State Sen. \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , according to the AP. After focusing his campaign on law-and-order issues and protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, Mr. Shapiro will succeed departing Democratic Gov. \uc2 Tom Wolf\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republican Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  defeated former State House Minority Leader \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , a Democrat, the AP projected. Mr. Kemp largely ignored attacks from Mr. Trump over President Biden's win in the state in 2020 and focused on his efforts to promote business development, loosen gun laws and open the state quickly following Covid-19 lockdowns.\par \par \uc2 California Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  easily won re-election in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/democrat-gavin-newsom-re-elected-as-california-governor-5bhSr5YimlgCaUjXOUIH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nation's most populous state }}}\uc2 , according to the AP, after a campaign in which he spent much of his time feuding with Republicans including Messrs. Abbott and DeSantis and promoting liberal positions on such issues as climate change and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Races that were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/midterm-senate-house-governor-races-to-watchhour-by-hour-11667870727"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 too close to call }}}\uc2  in the early-morning hours Wednesday included Kansas and Nevada, where Democratic incumbents sought to keep their seats, and Alaska, where a Republican governor is campaigning for reelection.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Which gubernatorial races are you watching most closely? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The AP also didn't declare winners in the campaigns to succeed GOP Gov. \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  in Arizona and Democratic Gov. \uc2 Kate Brown\uc2  in Oregon, both of whom are leaving office because of term limits.\par \par \uc2 There are currently 28 states with Republican governors and 22 with Democratic governors. Twenty of the states that held elections Tuesday have GOP governors and 16 are led by Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Results from the AP showed Republicans holding on to the governorships in 16 states but not flipping any, while Democrats held on to 13 in addition to the two they flipped. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
