\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Supporters Prevail in Midterm Ballot Measures; Constitutional amendments pass in Michigan, California and Vermont and antiabortion proposal is defeated in Kentucky\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,066 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2022\par 23:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Voters supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in a politically diverse mix of states on Tuesday, delivering victories to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates on ballot measures in Michigan, California, Vermont and Republican-leaning Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/livecoverage/latest-updates/midterms-elections-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 midterm elections }}}\uc2  provided the first national temperature-taking on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-features-prominently-in-midterm-elections-after-demise-of-roe-v-wade-11667826002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voter attitudes toward \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  in late June, ending federal constitutional protections for the procedure. The decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returned \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  policy to the states }}}\uc2 , creating a host of new battlegrounds.\par \par \uc2 Voters in five states considered ballot measures on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. Democrats also made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  central to their campaigns in an array of races and notched victories in a number of them, including contests for governor in Michigan and Pennsylvania.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-is-on-the-ballot-in-five-states-in-midterm-elections-11667921098"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Results of \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ballot Measures }}}\par \par \uc2 Michigan voters passed a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/gretchen-whitmer-wins-second-term-as-michigan-governor-AwIv6Q60TibTj9hXAl96"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 re-elected }}}\uc2  Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 . Democrats also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/michigan-becomes-bluer-as-voters-give-democratic-party-a-governing-trifecta-DZ0FDvUcyCk5lezHM4lo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took control of the state's legislature }}}\uc2  for the first time in four decades.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Whitmer's Republican opponent, Tudor Dixon, had called the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measure a radical proposal.\par \par \uc2 Michigan's referendum {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigans-abortion-tensions-reflect-uncertain-future-in-battleground-states-11651834802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed to amend the state's constitution }}}\uc2  to specify that "every individual has a fundamental right to reproductive freedom." The measure nullifies a 1931 state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that was largely dormant for the past 50 years. Since the Supreme Court overturned Roe, state courts have been considering whether the Michigan law could be reinstated.\par \par \uc2 Michigan was a major focus for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters because it is poised to serve as a destination for patients from nearby states, including Ohio, Indiana and Missouri, where lawmakers are seeking to ban the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Voters in California and Vermont overwhelmingly passed similar amendments to their state constitutions to include \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Vermont's initiative passed with 77% of the vote with nearly all votes counted, according to the AP. With 42% of California's votes counted as of Wednesday, 65% were in support.\par \par \uc2 Both initiatives had been expected to pass in states where there are already limited restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky, with 98% of votes counted, 52% of voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-Tfw0WrHeOVu4J8kI2Xit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a ballot measure }}}\uc2  that sought to amend the state constitution to explicitly say that it doesn't contain a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The proposal failed even as Republicans won most congressional races in the state.\par \par \uc2 The measure's failure won't have an immediate practical effect, but its rejection leaves open the door for the state's Supreme Court to decide that its Constitution includes a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The court is expected to hear arguments later this month in a case challenging the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky voters also declined to elect a vocal Republican \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponent who was running for the state Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 The defeat of the ballot measure in Kentucky is likely to boost \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups that hope direct appeals to voters can help them win Roe-like protections in at least some states where Republican supporters outnumber Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The results tell a similar story to what happened in Kansas in August, where voters in the conservative-leaning state soundly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a proposed state constitutional amendment }}}\uc2  that would have ended protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups said they are discussing options for ballot initiatives in other states in the coming years.\par \par \uc2 "When we can take this issue out of the hands of politicians and let the people decide directly, we can get some really exciting results," said Rachel Sweet, the campaign manager for Protect Kentucky Access, who worked to defeat the Kentucky proposal and previously led efforts to defeat Kansas' proposed amendment.\par \par \uc2 According to an AP VoteCast survey of more than 90,000 voters, roughly seven in 10 said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an important factor they considered, while one quarter said the issue was the single most important factor in their vote.\par \par \uc2 For voters who rated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their top issue, roughly 70% voted for Democrats, according to the national survey, conducted Oct. 31 through poll close on Nov. 8 by the AP-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research for The Wall Street Journal, the Associated Press and Fox News.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents cautioned against reading too much into the referendum results, saying they were significantly outspent by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups on the ballot questions.\par \par \uc2 "The pro-life movement has to do better," said Frank Cannon, a political strategist for Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America. "The political element of the pro-life movement has to step up and that is true in every area. Without that, we're going to be in trouble."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How might the elections shift the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  landscape? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Campaigning on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights didn't help some Democrats, including Georgia gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , who lost her challenge to Republican incumbent Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, Republicans swept three races for the state's Supreme Court. The GOP candidates had taken the position that life begins at fertilization, in response to a questionnaire from a group that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A vote in Montana on a narrower \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measure was still too close to call Wednesday. The measure raises the possibility of criminal charges for healthcare providers unless they take "all medically appropriate and reasonable actions to preserve the life" of a fetus born alive, including after an attempted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14a rare occurrence, according to the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Before the midterms, no state had adopted a constitutional amendment that enshrines protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Sixteen states and Washington, D.C., have written \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into state statutes. A constitutional amendment further protects \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, supporters say.\par \par \uc2 Alabama, Louisiana, Tennessee and West Virginia have adopted constitution amendments in recent years explicitly saying their state constitutions don't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an Election Issue\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become a much bigger motivating issue among Democrats since the Supreme Court ruled that there is no constitutional right to the procedure, according to a survey of about 115,000 voters, compiled by the Associated Press. See the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-different-groups-voted-in-the-2022-midterm-elections-11667955705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 full results of the AP VoteCast survey here. }}}\par \par \uc2 Chad Day contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-supporters-prevail-in-midterm-ballot-measures-11667986139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Rights Supporters Prevail in Midterm Ballot Measures  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221109eib9001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
