\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Frustrated Republicans Try to Explain Lack of Midterm 'Red Wave'; GOP lawmakers, strategists point to former President Trump's role, candidate quality,  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalie Andrews, Siobhan Hughes and Lindsay Wise \par \uc2 1,416 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2022\par 23:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Weaker-than-expected results in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/livecoverage/latest-updates/midterms-elections-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the midterm elections }}}\uc2  for Republicans set off a wave of second-guessing of the party's approach in a campaign seen as a prime opportunity to pick off dozens of seats from weakened Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The GOP still appeared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-inches-closer-to-expected-narrow-house-majority-senate-still-a-toss-up-11668076201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on track to win the majority }}}\uc2  in the House, though with a much smaller margin than many election analysts and party officials had predicted, amid concerns over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/voters-cast-ballots-as-inflation-and-social-issues-weigh-on-americans-11667917985"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflation }}}\uc2  and crime under Democratic control of Washington. In the Senate, the margin will likely be tight, and could once again\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-senate-race-headed-to-runoff-for-second-time-in-two-years-11668022680"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 come down to a Georgia runoff }}}\uc2  as it did in 2020, puncturing party hopes of winning a comfortable majority.\par \par \uc2 The uncertainty over the result contrasts with the party's giddy optimism of a possible "red wave" headed into Election Day\u8212\'20\'14and brought to the surface {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/some-key-trump-backed-candidates-struggled-in-midterms-as-his-party-rivals-sailed-to-victories-11668014249"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 simmering fears and disagreements }}}\uc2 , particularly over the makeup of the GOP's lineup.\par \par \uc2 "As it turns out, candidates and campaigns matter," said \uc2 Kevin McLaughlin\uc2 , an ally of Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) and a former executive director of the National Republican Senatorial Committee.\par \par \uc2 Mr. McConnell had aired concerns over some candidates earlier in the cycle, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/republicans-want-focus-on-retaking-senatenot-leaders-feud-11662664847?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taking public a fight }}}\uc2  with former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Sen. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  (R., Fla.), the head of the Republicans' Senate campaign arm. He felt their actions to shape the field were advancing Republican candidates who were too extreme or unappealing to win in a general election, potentially costing the party winnable Senate seats. Mr. Scott {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mitch-mcconnell-rebukes-rick-scott-for-tax-proposal-11646173769"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected }}}\uc2  Mr. McConnell's comments, and Mr. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-criticizes-mcconnell-in-lengthy-statement-calling-him-a-political-hack-11613513959"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has called to replace him }}}\uc2  as party leader.\par \par \uc2 In a social media message early Wednesday, Mr. Trump called the results "A GREAT EVENING" and said Democrats and media outlets were "doing everything possible to play it down."\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans said Mr. Trump had undercut the GOP's chances.\par \par \uc2 "I'm very disappointed," said Sen. \uc2 Pat Toomey\uc2  (R., Pa.), who is retiring after this term. His seat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/john-fetterman-wins-key-senate-race-in-pennsylvania-defeating-mehmet-oz-oW3cFfkuo97s4Fa2Q9Sl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was won }}}\uc2  by Democrat \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2  over Republican Mehmet Oz, whom Mr. Toomey supported.\par \par \uc2 "I think a huge factor in all of this was the disastrous role of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in this whole process," he said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Toomey pointed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/democrat-josh-shapiro-wins-pennsylvania-governor-race-over-doug-mastriano-rdDSLqwHlckU7Q5yZYF2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the poor showing }}}\uc2  by Trump-endorsed GOP candidate \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2  in the Pennsylvania governor's race, which he said dragged down the state's other Republicans including Mr. Oz. "All across the country we see that the hard-core MAGA candidates dramatically underperformed more conventional Republicans, so that's a big reality that we have to recognize," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The party needs to make some decisions on Trump," said Sarah Chamberlain, head of the Republican Main Street Partnership\u8212\'20\'14an alliance of GOP lawmakers, some of which represent competitive seats. She said Mr. Trump and the party's response to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had hurt them among independent voters.\par \par \uc2 In competitive House and Senate races, many candidates that Mr. Trump endorsed were short on political experience and emerged bruised from competitive primaries, potentially hurting their chances. House candidates J.R. Majewski and Madison Gesiotto Gilbert in Ohio and Bo Hines in North Carolina said they would be standard bearers for the former president, but lacked money and weren't able to appeal to enough voters needed to win tough seats. They faced a barrage of ads from Democrats painting them as too extreme for independent voters.\par \par \uc2 "Trump picked sure losers in winnable races," Gregg Nunziata, a former adviser to Sen. \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  (R., Fla.), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/greggnunziata/status/1590218085008805890"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on Twitter }}}\uc2 . "He picked weak candidates in otherwise slam dunk races requiring the party to spend tons of money we'd rather spend elsewhere," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Some Trump-backed candidates spread conspiracy theories about the 2020 election. Mr. Majewski was at the Stop the Steal rally on Jan. 6. Mr. Hines called for a 10-year moratorium on immigration and said he would support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a case-by-case basis for government review.\par \par \uc2 National Republican groups swept in to buy television ads to help them. House Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy (R., Calif.) campaigned and fundraised with them, trying to pull them across the finish line, but all failed to do so.\par \par \uc2 Mr. McCarthy had confidently predicted last year that Republicans could win dozens of seats, and consistently expanded the target list. In recent days, he was campaigning with Republican Hung Cao, who was running against Rep. \uc2 Jennifer Wexton\uc2 , a Democrat, in a challenge both parties thought was a long shot for the GOP. Ms. Wexton won the race in Northern Virginia 53% to 47%.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  also was seen as reining in GOP gains, as defending access to the procedure was a potent motivator for many independents and Democrats, according to polling and members of both parties. During the primaries earlier in the year, many Republican candidates made comments in debates and interviews about limiting or outlawing abortions. Later, after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned the right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , Democrats had ready-made clips for negatives ads.\par \par \uc2 "Most people thought the economy being not very good, and with the vote being extremely heavy that more Republicans would do well," said former Republican Sen. \uc2 Judd Gregg\uc2  of New Hampshire. People voted on three things, he said: "Trump, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and rejection of Republicans who bought into this cult theory of conspiracy."\par \par \uc2 One example was in Ohio, where Rep. \uc2 Steve Chabot\uc2  (R., Ohio) said that voter concerns over high inflation hadn't been enough to send him back to Congress. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/democrat-greg-landsman-flips-ohio-house-seat-beats-republican-rep-steve-chabot-Gxx2B7Zx3H8PqhFXWK1o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost to }}}\uc2  Democrat Greg Landsman in a district that became unfavorable to Republicans in redistricting.\par \par \uc2 "We certainly emphasized the economy and inflation, and they were beating me over the head on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "That's the thing that beat me," said Mr. Chabot, an antiabortion candidate who had authored a 2003 law known as the partial-birth \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 With many races still uncalled and majorities still in reach, some Republicans were wary of explicit finger pointing. But the outcome was likely to hurt Minnesota Rep. \uc2 Tom Emmer\uc2 's bid to ascend to House majority whip, several GOP aides said, as he led the House Republicans' campaign arm this cycle.\par \par \uc2 "I don't know how. We delivered," Mr. Emmer said when asked if it would complicate his leadership ambitions. He declined to discuss candidate quality or Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 Democrats pushed hard on attacks saying Republicans would limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, seeing it as a way to pull in independent voters. Many were elated when Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lindsey-grahams-abortion-bill-gets-cold-shoulder-from-some-republicans-11663098886"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced a bill limiting abortions }}}\uc2  after 15 weeks of pregnancy, putting the issue back on the front burner just as many Republicans were seeking to focus on inflation and crime, which they saw as more favorable for attracting swing voters. The bill drew the ire of Mr. McConnell, who said any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations should be left up to the states.\par \par \uc2 "I don't really know how to account for all of this," Mr. Graham said Wednesday of Republicans' weaker-than-expected showing. "Pro-life people did well," he said, pointing to GOP Senate and governor candidates like \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2  in North Carolina, Sen. \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  in Florida and J.D. Vance in Ohio. Still, said Mr. Graham, "I'm sure \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was an issue in some places."\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of Susan B. Anthony List, which opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said some Republican candidates didn't have good responses to criticism from Democratic candidates on the issue\u8212\'20\'14and singled out Mr. Oz in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Some candidates "were not prepared and took the ostrich strategy: burying their heads in the sand and running from the issue, allowing their opponents to define them," she said in a memo sent Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Kevin Brady\uc2  (R., Texas), the top Republican on the House Ways and Means Committee, said President Biden's late criticism of Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/biden-social-security-attacks-may-have-helped-democrats-top-gop-lawmaker-says-lo3J8Z3rvgtuy1aoFfX3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over Social Security and Medicare may have helped Democrats }}}\uc2 . Some Republicans have called for changes in the programs, such as changing the eligibility age, to extend their long-term solvency.\par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately, some of that fear mongering works, so that may have had an impact," said Mr. Brady. "I always worry that it's awfully easy to scare seniors."\par \par \uc2 Richard Rubin contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Natalie.Andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Natalie.Andrews@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 siobhan.hughes@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221109eib9007vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
