\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Few State Governor Races Result in Change of Control; Democrats fend off challenges in Wisconsin, New York, Kansas and Michigan; Republicans hold Florida and Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 By Elizabeth Findell and Jimmy Vielkind \par \uc2 1,262 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 November 2022\par 20:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Gubernatorial elections resulted in few {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/livecoverage/latest-updates/midterms-elections-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 changes of control on Election Day }}}\uc2 , as Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-different-groups-voted-in-the-2022-midterm-elections-11667955705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held off challengers }}}\uc2  in several races that polls showed could be close including Wisconsin, New York, Kansas and Michigan, while Republican incumbents won decisively in Florida and Texas, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Election Updates\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/election/2022/general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Live Results }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/livecoverage/latest-updates/midterms-elections-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Latest News }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-different-groups-voted-in-the-2022-midterm-elections-11667955705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Different Groups Voted }}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats also prevailed in the only two states to flip, Maryland and Massachusetts.\par \par \uc2 One of the most {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/election/2022/general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hotly contested races }}}\uc2  in the nation was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/tony-evers-wins-second-term-as-governor-in-wisconsin-aPlnAc7LbxwlHk10nkfq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Wisconsin }}}\uc2 , where incumbent Democrat \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  fended off Republican businessman \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2 , the AP projected. Mr. Evers ran on a platform of investing in education and infrastructure, opposing gerrymandering and supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, while Mr. Michels said he would do more to fight crime and touted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/some-key-trump-backed-candidates-struggled-in-midterms-as-his-party-rivals-sailed-to-victories-11668014249"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his support from }}}\uc2  former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In New York, incumbent Democratic Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  defeated Republican U.S. Rep. \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2 , according to the AP. Mr. Zeldin gained on her in recent polls, which gave Republicans hope he could become the first candidate from their party to win statewide office in two decades as he focused on voter concern about rising crime. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kathy-hochul-is-the-first-woman-to-be-elected-new-yorks-governor-11667979471"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ms. Hochul campaigned }}}\uc2  on her record from her year in office, including new gun-control laws, Covid-19 pandemic management and rebate checks for taxpayers.\par \par \uc2 Robust victories for Florida's \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and Texas' Greg Abbott put the two men in strong positions as they prepare for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/trump-says-it-would-be-a-mistake-for-desantis-to-run-for-the-white-house-in-2024-s4Ss0qY1YijptXFIzEOb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 possible presidential runs in 2024 }}}\uc2 , according to political analysts. Both have focused on issues that appealed to their party's base.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/texas-gov-greg-abbott-wins-third-term-defeating-beto-o-rourke-IjUet6g1VsVaL5PNdEDD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Abbott }}}\uc2 , who defeated former U.S. Rep. \uc2 Beto O'Rourke\uc2 , a Democrat, devoted much of his second term to immigration and border security. Mr. DeSantis, who won over Democrat \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2 , a former governor and U.S. representative, emphasized his stances on culture issues and his decision to reopen businesses in his state early in the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 In Kansas, Democratic Gov. \uc2 Laura Kelly\uc2  won a narrow victory in a state where Mr. Trump won 56% to 42% in 2020, according to the Associated Press. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/kansas-democratic-gov-laura-kelly-keeps-seat-hU2XLm61iF7R3DU4nsj9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ms. Kelly touted her record }}}\uc2  in office, including working with the Republican-controlled legislature. She ran ads showing herself standing in the middle of roadways and meeting with Mr. Trump when he was president.\par \par \uc2 Her challenger Derek Schmidt, the Republican attorney general, sought to tie his opponent to President Biden. He also sought to tap into voter dissatisfaction with inflation and the Covid-19 restrictions of 2020.\par \par \uc2 Michigan Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  defeated conservative political commentator Tudor Dixon, who criticized the incumbent for the length of Covid-19 shutdowns and pledged to expand the state's economy and stop what she described as the teaching of critical race theory in schools. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/gretchen-whitmer-wins-second-term-as-michigan-governor-AwIv6Q60TibTj9hXAl96"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ms. Whitmer focused }}}\uc2  on her record repairing roads and increasing education spending.\par \par \uc2 New Mexico Democratic Gov. \uc2 Michelle Lujan Grisham\uc2  won against former television meteorologist Mark Ronchetti, a Republican, according to the AP, in a race focused on issues such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/new-mexico-democratic-gov-michelle-lujan-grisham-re-elected-fYNx8f4YYQ4Q6R4ulrF0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crime and \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Maine, Democratic Gov. \uc2 Janet Mills\uc2  won re-election over former Republican Gov. Paul LePage, the AP said. Mr. LePage hammered the incumbent over energy costs, while Ms. Mills touted her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/democrat-janet-mills-re-elected-governor-of-maine-NjCQi9V1epY0dPEc3wI3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 efforts to diversify the state's energy sources }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania Democratic Attorney General \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  beat Republican State Sen. \uc2 Doug Mastriano\uc2 , according to the AP. After focusing his campaign on law-and-order issues and protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/democrat-josh-shapiro-wins-pennsylvania-governor-race-over-doug-mastriano-rdDSLqwHlckU7Q5yZYF2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Shapiro will succeed }}}\uc2  departing Democratic Gov. \uc2 Tom Wolf\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-different-groups-voted-in-the-2022-midterm-elections-11667955705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How People Voted }}}\par \par \uc2 Results of survey of about 115,000 registered voters\par \par \uc2 Georgia Republican Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  defeated former State House Minority Leader \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , a Democrat, the AP projected. Mr. Kemp largely {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/stacey-abrams-concedes-to-brian-kemp-in-georgia-governor-race-xinGQoJk1ns4ElJN1cuW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ignored attacks from Mr. Trump }}}\uc2  over Mr. Biden's win in the state in 2020 and focused on his efforts to promote business development, loosen gun laws and open the state quickly following Covid-19 lockdowns.\par \par \uc2 California Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  easily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/democrat-gavin-newsom-re-elected-as-california-governor-5bhSr5YimlgCaUjXOUIH"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won re-election }}}\uc2  in the nation's most populous state, according to the AP, after a campaign in which he spent much of his time feuding with Republicans including Messrs. Abbott and DeSantis and promoting liberal positions on issues such as climate change and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Races that were too close to call on Wednesday included Nevada, where a Democratic incumbent sought to keep his seat, and Alaska, where a Republican governor is campaigning for reelection.\par \par \uc2 The AP also didn't declare winners in the campaigns to succeed GOP Gov. \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  in Arizona and Democratic Gov. \uc2 Kate Brown\uc2  in Oregon, both of whom are leaving office because of term limits.\par \par \uc2 There are currently 28 states with Republican governors and 22 with Democratic governors. Twenty of the states that held elections Tuesday have GOP governors and 16 are led by Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Results from the AP showed Republicans holding on to the governorships in 16 states but not flipping any, while Democrats held on to 13 in addition to the two they flipped.\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts Attorney General \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2  will be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/maura-healey-wins-massachusetts-governor-race-rwzH4oBja6X24n14YMyL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first woman elected governor }}}\uc2  of her state, while author and nonprofit executive Wes Moore will become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/maryland-elects-its-first-black-governor-wes-moore-skHsnPOAscnJEWs5BfH5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the first Black governor of Maryland }}}\uc2 . Both defeated Republican nominees allied with Mr. Trump who tried to succeed popular moderate members of their own party who were stepping down.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, GOP gubernatorial candidate Kari Lake, a former television-news anchor, has embraced Mr. Trump's false claims of fraud in the 2020 election and said she would look to bolster election security, as well as devoting more state resources to patrolling the border with Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Her opponent, Democratic Secretary of State \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , has framed the election as an effort to save democracy and protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/arizona-gubernatorial-candidates-react-to-close-race-5U0r8qduleZXYPizrSG9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told supporters late Tuesday }}}\uc2  that they were pleased with the results they had seen so far.\par \par \uc2 Nevada Democratic Gov. \uc2 Steve Sisolak\uc2  is struggling to fend off GOP challenger Joseph Lombardo. Democrats won the past four presidential elections in Nevada and until recently seemed to be on the upswing, in part because of an influx of Latino residents. Interviews and polling suggest that the economic insecurity has pushed some voters, including Latinos, to vote Republican this year.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Lombardo, the sheriff of Clark County, which includes Las Vegas, has tried to connect high inflation and other economic concerns to Nevada's economic shutdown early in the pandemic. Mr. Sisolak said that he ordered the closure of casinos and other businesses in 2020 to protect citizens from an even bigger death toll and that Nevada has regained jobs faster than most other states.\par \par \uc2 Local officials said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/election-midterms-2022/card/nevada-results-may-take-until-thursday-or-longer-GiNBBPIOatsYgTvr4q19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it may take until Thursday or later }}}\uc2  for all ballots to be counted in Nevada amid issues that included a drenching rainstorm in Las Vegas.\par \par \uc2 Oregon might see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/oregon-might-elect-a-republican-governor-for-first-time-in-four-decades-11666863003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its first Republican governor in 40 years }}}\uc2 , as voters angry about homelessness and crime in and around Portland are calling for change. Former Democratic state House Speaker \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2  and former State House GOP leader Christine Drazan are running evenly, according to polls.\par \par \uc2 Betsy Johnson, a former Democratic state senator running as an independent, is polling far behind but drawing enough support that she could influence the outcome. Political strategists said Ms. Johnson is likely drawing more voters from Ms. Kotek than Ms. Drazan.\par \par \uc2 Write to Elizabeth Findell at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Elizabeth.Findell@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth.Findell@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/few-state-governor-races-result-in-change-of-control-11668024031"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Few State Governor Races Result in Change of Control }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221109eib9005v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
