\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Candidates Make Last Pitches in Final Hours of Midterms Campaigning; Over the weekend, President Biden and three of his predecessors fanned out in an effort to rally voters\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins in Phoenix and Joshua Jamerson in Atlanta \par \uc2 1,519 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2022\par 04:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats sought to keep control of Congress and Republicans looked to maintain their late momentum as candidates across the country {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-11-07"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made their closing midterm arguments }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans are seen by nonpartisan analysts as the favorites to take the House majority in Tuesday's contests, with surveys showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-gaining-support-among-black-and-latino-voters-wsj-poll-finds-11667822481"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key voting blocs trending away from Democrats }}}\uc2  as many voters say their top concerns are inflation and economic uncertainty. Senate control {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-to-know-about-midterm-elections-why-they-are-important-11663359723"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains a tossup }}}\uc2 , but polls show GOP candidates in states such as Arizona, New Hampshire and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/troubles-for-oz-and-fetterman-in-pennsylvania-keep-them-neck-and-neck-11667565820?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania }}}\uc2  have made gains in the final weeks. Democrats were also working to hold on to governors' offices in Oregon and New York, states that were once seen as safely Democratic but which have been competitive this year.\par \par \uc2 "There's many Democrats who wish this was held even a month ago. It seems the closer we get to Election Day, there is deterioration for Democrats," said Jessica Taylor, the Senate and governors editor for the nonpartisan Cook Political Report.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Taylor recently changed the group's projection for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mitch-mcconnell-helped-shape-gop-senate-midterm-field-now-pushes-for-strong-finish-11667797261"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate contests }}}\uc2  toward Republicans, saying the outcome could vary from no change to a net GOP gain of three seats. The Senate is currently split 50-50. In late October, Cook had projected that the elections could produce anything from a one-seat Democratic gain to a two-seat pickup by Republicans. On the House side, where Republicans need a net gain of five seats to take the majority, Cook has 35 seats rated as tossups. Democrats are defending 25; the GOP is defending 10. Cook also has four Democratic-led states and one GOP-led state listed as tossups for governor.\par \par \uc2 Democrats control the House, Senate and White House. The party in power typically loses seats in midterm elections, and President Biden has struggled with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-avoids-some-battleground-states-in-midterms-final-stretch-11667217622"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 low approval ratings }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prospects looked better for Democrats during the summer following the Supreme Court's decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating the federal right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . In addition, in some of the most competitive states, candidates endorsed by former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won primaries over candidates seen as more electable by many political analysts.\par \par \uc2 However, during the past few months, Republicans have regained momentum as voters have grown concerned about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-strains-voters-across-income-levels-ahead-of-midterm-elections-11667817001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 persistent inflation }}}\uc2 . A Wall Street Journal poll conducted about two weeks before Election Day showed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-prospects-rise-amid-economic-pessimism-wsj-poll-finds-11667295002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans with the edge }}}\uc2  and suggested that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-features-prominently-in-midterm-elections-after-demise-of-roe-v-wade-11667826002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  are less important to voters' decisions than the economy. That survey also found several voter groups, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/working-class-latino-voters-once-solidly-democratic-are-shifting-toward-republicans-a7578ecc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including Latino and Black voters }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/white-suburban-women-swing-toward-backing-republicans-for-congress-11667381402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white suburban women }}}\uc2 , had shifted toward Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, Mr. Biden, three former presidents and other prominent surrogates fanned out across the country in an effort to rally voters.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden campaigned Monday evening for Democratic gubernatorial candidate Wes Moore in Maryland. Mr. Moore is leading in polls.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Rev. \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  that aired on his radio show Monday, Mr. Biden said that if Republicans win congressional majorities in the midterm elections, they will try to "wipe out everything we've done." He said his efforts to help Black Americans would be at risk.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-11-07/card/trump-teases-very-big-announcement-on-nov-15-vp4yHOSkqpcp3ahW81Gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who said on Monday night }}}\uc2  that he'll make "a very big announcement on Tuesday, November 15," held a rally in Ohio with Republican J.D. Vance, who has a lead over Rep. \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2  (D., Ohio) in polling in the race for Senate.\par \par \uc2 House Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy (R., Calif.) rallied voters in Virginia for state Sen. Jen Kiggans, who is running to unseat Rep. \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2  in a race Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-virginia-battlegrounds-republican-candidates-borrow-from-youngkins-approach-11667390401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see as a top pickup opportunity }}}\uc2 . Mr. McCarthy told CNN if Republicans take control of the House, they will focus immediately on legislation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-11-07/card/what-kevin-mccarthy-wants-to-do-as-house-speaker-if-the-gop-wins-the-majority-mN93zIyDtfK0GbWSb2mw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strengthening border security }}}\uc2 . It is unlikely the Biden administration would agree to any such measure.\par \par \uc2 First lady Jill Biden was also on the campaign trail in Virginia on Monday, backing Democratic Rep. \uc2 Jennifer Wexton\uc2  in her re-election race against GOP challenger Hung Cao in the exurbs outside of Washington.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, the races for governor and senator remained competitive, according to public polls.\par \par \uc2 Kari Lake, a longtime local TV anchor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kari-lake-unites-many-arizona-republicans-after-partys-earlier-divisions-over-trump-11666690203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who is now the GOP nominee for governor }}}\uc2 , hasn't committed to accepting the results of this year's election if she doesn't win. Ms. Lake has called on Secretary of State \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2 , the Democratic candidate for governor, to recuse herself from running the election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-11-04/card/katie-hobbs-again-rejects-kari-lake-s-call-to-recuse-herself-from-oversight-of-arizona-race-PN3UqlPBvU4cU55S1ZHI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ms. Hobbs has refused to do so }}}\uc2 . She is the state's chief elections administrator but doesn't count ballots. Past secretaries of state have certified their own wins and losses in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 All four major statewide Republican candidates in Arizona have echoed Mr. Trump's false claims that he won the 2020 election. There was no fraud in the 2020 election widespread enough to change the result, according to federal officials. Dozens of lawsuits filed by supporters of Mr. Trump challenging the results failed.\par \par \uc2 Tom Hynes, a 77-year-old retiree from Tucson, said he voted for Democrats because he was concerned about the Republicans' "disengagement from reality and people being so adamant about their views based on misinformation."\par \par \uc2 On Sunday on CNN's "State of the Union," \uc2 Ronna McDaniel\uc2 , chairwoman of the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , said Republican candidates who question the result of the election should be allowed to exhaust legal and other options, but then {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-11-04/card/gop-candidates-who-question-elections-should-exhaust-process-accept-results-rnc-chief-says-18kAPYgOZSG3YAVEW6fW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should accept the results }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Perez, 64, a Phoenix retiree, attended an event Monday with Ms. Lake and the GOP ticket. "She literally wants to make America great again," she said, referring to Mr. Trump's slogan.\par \par \uc2 Also in Arizona, Democratic Sen. Mark Kelly is facing a serious challenge from Blake Masters, who has closed the polling gap in recent weeks amid increased spending from Republican groups.\par \par \uc2 Jon Ball, 69, a retiree from Marana, Ariz., voted for Mr. Kelly in 2020 when he was running to fill the remainder of the late Sen. \uc2 John McCain\uc2 's term. Mr. Ball said he is supporting Mr. Kelly's opponent this time.\par \par \uc2 "He claimed he was going to be an independent," Mr. Ball said, adding that he felt Mr. Kelly had voted with Democrats too often. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
