\par \par \uc2 Democratic Sen. Mark Kelly, gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  and former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in Arizona last week. PHOTO: Ash Ponders for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kelly defended his record during a news conference Monday alongside several Republicans who have endorsed his campaign. "I make every decision on how I'm going to vote on legislation based on what is in the best interest of Arizona and our country." Two of Mr. McCain's sons were in attendance at the event, but didn't speak.\par \par \uc2 In an interview later Monday, Mr. Masters said he didn't need to hold events with non-Republicans because the issues he was running on had wide appeal, such as combating inflation and closing the southern border.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Masters said he had no plans to go toward the center and promised to govern as a conservative if elected. "I would never call myself a moderate," he said. Mr. Masters was noncommittal when asked if he would support Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) to be Senate leader.\par \par \uc2 In Georgia's Senate race, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/a-quarter-billion-dollars-for-the-walker-warnock-georgia-senate-race-buys-a-toss-up-11667748797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than $241 million has been spent }}}\uc2 , Democratic Sen. \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and his Republican opponent, \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , a former All-Pro running back for the \uc2 Dallas Cowboys\uc2 , made their final rounds in an effort to rally voters.\par \par \uc2 Maryellen Wagner, a Republican from Hiram, Ga., said she opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but couldn't care less that Mr. Walker has been accused by two women of paying for them to have abortions after having intimate relationships with them. Mr. Walker has denied the claims. Democrats have accused him of hypocrisy because he opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "When he goes to Washington, as long as he is there for me and the American people, I don't care what he did years ago," said Ms. Wagner, 68 years old.\par \par \uc2 Andrea Cooke, a mental-health services worker from Macon, said she voted early for Mr. Warnock because he has pledged to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights at the federal level\u8212\'20\'14something that is her top concern after the Supreme Court overturned a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this summer. She said prices are rising for everyday items at the grocery store, but she doesn't blame Democrats.\par \par \uc2 She said inflation was the result of the Covid pandemic, adding later: "Nothing happens in a silo."\par \par \uc2 The Georgia Senate race is tight between Messrs. Walker and Warnock, and could go to a runoff if neither man hits 50% support on Tuesday. Asked if he was prepared for a runoff, Mr. Warnock said: "If I need to, I'll talk to you about it on Wednesday."\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins+1@wsj.com."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins+1@wsj.com. }}}\uc2  and Joshua Jamerson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:joshua.jamerson+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joshua.jamerson+1@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/candidates-make-last-pitches-in-final-hours-of-midterms-campaigning-11667817002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Candidates Make Last Pitches in Final Hours of Midterms Campaigning }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221107eib7000rz\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
