\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 When Are the 2022 Midterm Elections? What to Know; The economy, inflation and  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  are the issues voters have cited as most important this year\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joshua Jamerson \par \uc2 1,339 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2022\par 17:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats and Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/livecoverage/latest-updates/midterms-elections-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are fighting for control }}}\uc2  of the House of Representatives, Senate, governors' mansions and state legislatures in elections that conclude Tuesday. The party in power in Washington\u8212\'20\'14in this year's case, the Democrats, who control the House, Senate and presidency\u8212\'20\'14typically experiences losses in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/midterm-elections-2022-results-house-congress-11667866631"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the midterm elections }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Midterm elections occur every four years, in the middle of the president's four-year term. Although President Biden isn't on the ballot, the outcome will determine how the rest of his term will look.\par \par \uc2 Election Day is Tuesday, Nov. 8, but some voting in many states began earlier.\par \par \uc2 Here is what to watch through Election Day and beyond:\par \par \uc2 Who is in the running?\par \par \uc2 Members of the House are elected for two-year terms, so all 435 seats are decided during the midterm elections. The Senate's six-year terms are decided on a rolling basis, with roughly one-third on the map this year. There is also a slate of governors' mansions up for grabs, and the parties see a few statehouses on the verge of flipping control. Several states also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-features-prominently-in-midterm-elections-after-demise-of-roe-v-wade-11667826002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have ballot measures regarding \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 What are the chances for each party in the midterm elections?\par \par \uc2 Nonpartisan political analysts favor Republicans to win control of the House because of voter concerns over inflation and crime among other issues, and the historical tendency of the party that controls the White House to lose seats in midterm elections. Analysts see the Senate as more of a tossup, with crucial contests in Nevada, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/troubles-for-oz-and-fetterman-in-pennsylvania-keep-them-neck-and-neck-11667565820"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/a-quarter-billion-dollars-for-the-walker-warnock-georgia-senate-race-buys-a-toss-up-11667748797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia }}}\uc2 , Ohio, Arizona, North Carolina, Wisconsin and New Hampshire.\par \par \uc2 According to the most recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-prospects-rise-amid-economic-pessimism-wsj-poll-finds-11667295002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal poll }}}\uc2 , Republicans hold a slight edge over Democrats, 46% to 44%, when voters are asked which party they would support in their congressional district if the election were held today.\par \par \uc2 What are the issues animating the electorate?\par \par \uc2 In the latest WSJ poll, voters cited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-strains-voters-across-income-levels-ahead-of-midterm-elections-11667817001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the economy and inflation as top concerns }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the poll, views of the economy were more dour than at any point in the past year. Only 19% say the economy is headed in the right direction, down 11 percentage points from August, while 71% say the economy is on the wrong track. A majority of voters, 55%, disapprove of Mr. Biden's overall job performance, compared with 43% who approve.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling overturning Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , which had established a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has boosted the focus on that issue this year and has made supporters of legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly women, more likely to vote in November, surveys have shown.\par \par \uc2 But the latest WSJ poll suggested that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are less important in voting decisions than voters indicated in the summer. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
