\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Features Prominently in Midterm Elections After Demise of Roe v. Wade; Ballot initiatives, races for state office could determine future of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  after Supreme Court decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,102 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2022\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elimination of legal protections for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  has prompted months of speculation about how the ruling would affect the political landscape. Voters will provide some answers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/midterm-election-campaigning-intensifies-across-u-s-in-closing-days-11667730808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tuesday's midterm elections }}}\uc2 , where the issue is in play across state ballots.\par \par \uc2 The high court's decision in June to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturn Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  empowered voters and politicians to make decisions about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in ways not seen in 50 years. In a range of states, races for governor, the legislature and the courts could help determine where and to what extent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the procedure is available }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Voters in several states also are considering the issue directly through ballot measures. California, Michigan and Vermont have initiatives that propose amending their state constitutions to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, while Kentucky voters are considering an initiative that aims to specify its constitution doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How much do you think the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will factor into people's decisions on Election Day? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Many Democrats have sought to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/livecoverage/latest-updates/midterms-elections-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central to their campaigns }}}\uc2 , running television ads accusing their Republican opponents of inserting themselves into private medical decisions and endangering women's lives. Republicans have sought to focus on the economy, inflation and crime, issues they say are more resonant with voters.\par \par \uc2 Political scientists say it isn't clear how much Democrats can boost their fortunes in a challenging election year for the party by tapping into the anger felt by some voters, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/abortion-rights-push-some-suburban-women-in-west-michigan-toward-democrats-ddc94c89"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 moderate suburban women }}}\uc2 , about the rollback of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "Most would agree that overturning Roe absolutely helped Democrats," said Tresa Undem, a partner at PerryUndem, a public-opinion research firm. The question, she said, is how much it can counteract prevailing headwinds.\par \par \uc2 Democratic gubernatorial candidates including \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  in Michigan and \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  in Georgia have made support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights central talking points, as have candidates for attorney general in states including Wisconsin, Michigan and Arizona. The issue also has featured prominently in some congressional races.\par \par \uc2 In politically mixed states where the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains uncertain, voters' choices could play a central role.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/north-carolina-senate-race-spotlights-shrinking-slice-of-persuadable-voters-11666603802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In North Carolina }}}\uc2 , for example, Republicans are seeking to gain a legislative supermajority that could allow them to pass new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions over the veto of the state's Democratic governor. Republicans also could flip the ideological balance on the state's supreme court by winning one of two seats that are up for re-election.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at the center of a number contests for state supreme courts, which are in the spotlight as \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups seek legal protections for the procedure under state law.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken on a new prominence in state supreme court elections that it's never had before," said Douglas Keith, counsel at New York University's Brennan Center for Justice.\par \par \uc2 In Ohio, three seats on the state supreme court are up for grabs and could tip the court from a majority of Republican justices to Democrats. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-abortion-lawsuits-continue-in-states-cutting-access-11656543956"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A challenge to a state law }}}\uc2  banning most abortions after around six weeks of pregnancy is expected to eventually make its way up to the state justices.\par \par \uc2 Tensions have flared over whether the campaign has improperly politicized the court.\par \par \uc2 Three Republican candidates for the Ohio Supreme Court drew criticism from some legal observers for taking the position that life begins at fertilization, in response to a questionnaire from Cincinnati Right to Life.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio State Bar Association also sent a letter last week asking the state's Democratic Party to stop running an ad saying two Republican justices seeking re-election would ban abortions without exceptions for rape or incest. "While we support your constitutional right to vigorously make the case for the candidates you support, we encourage you to do so without using misleading terms or rhetoric that further damage public trust in the independence, integrity and impartiality of our judicial system," the letter said.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps nowhere is the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  more hotly contested than in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 The state has a 1931 law that would ban virtually all abortions in the state. The law had been dormant for five decades, but after Roe fell this summer, state courts began considering whether it can be enforced.\par \par \uc2 The law would be nullified if Michigan voters pass a ballot initiative that would amend the state constitution to include the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Opponents have argued the amendment would leave little room for the state to adopt any kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations.\par \par \uc2 Chelsea Kinjorski, a 33-year-old in Royal Oak, a Detroit suburb, said she has never placed a political sign in her yard until this year when she chose to display one in support of the amendment. "It feels like there's so much on the line," she said last week.\par \par \uc2 At Royal Oak Church of Christ next door, member Marque Cryderman has placed a sign opposing the amendment outside of the church and recently delivered a sermon about it.\par \par \uc2 "I never thought in the whole world that I would be preaching a sermon about a proposal that's on the ballot. But this one was so bad that it couldn't not be said," he said.\par \par \uc2 The presidents of three of the nation's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups were scheduled to campaign in the final days with Michigan Gov. Whitmer as she seeks re-election.\par \par \uc2 Tudor Dixon, Ms. Whitmer's Republican challenger, has sought to portray her opponent and the ballot proposal as extreme. "It would be the most radical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in the entire country," Ms. Dixon said at a recent gubernatorial debate.\par \par \uc2 Polling has indicated that more state voters support the amendment than oppose it. Initiatives codifying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights also are expected to pass in California and Vermont.\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky, voters are considering an amendment that would make explicit that the state constitution contains no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Supporters say the measure would help prevent the courts from reading a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into Kentucky law, while opponents say it would allow state lawmakers unrestrained power to impose strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits.\par \par \uc2 The Kentucky Supreme Court is expected to hear arguments later this month in a case challenging a state law that bans most abortions.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-features-prominently-in-midterm-elections-after-demise-of-roe-v-wade-11667826002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Features Prominently in Midterm Elections After Demise of Roe v. Wade }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221107eib7001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
