\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Seeks to Rally Voters on  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  as Polls Show Interest Waning; Some recent surveys indicate issue is losing potency as economic concerns take priority\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tarini Parti \par \uc2 1,112 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 November 2022\par 22:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will spend the final days of the midterms campaign seeking to rally Democrats around the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/story/abortion-rights-push-some-suburban-women-in-west-michigan-toward-democrats-ddc94c89"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issue of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access, }}}\uc2  as some polls show the issue losing potency in energizing voters and economic anxiety {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/economic-pressures-weigh-on-voters-in-final-midterms-campaign-stretch-11667035804"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 giving Republicans momentum }}}\uc2  ahead of Tuesday's vote.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris's efforts come as Democrats grow concerned that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-10-28/card/voters-get-key-inflation-reading-ahead-of-midterms-8Xhc9VybMRh55togwZQi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rising inflation and gas prices }}}\uc2  are overshadowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a priority for many voters. A Wall Street Journal poll conducted about two weeks before Election Day suggests that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are less important in voting decisions than voters indicated in the summer, after the Supreme Court's decision in June in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\uc2 , which overturned the constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and returned the issue to states to decide.\par \par \uc2 The same poll found Republicans now hold a slight edge over Democrats, 46% to 44%, when voters were asked which party they would support in their congressional district if the election were held today.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris will campaign in New York, Illinois and California in the coming days, all Democratic-leaning states where there is widespread support for ensuring access to legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The vice president will campaign on Thursday with New York Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , who is in a tight race against Republican Rep. \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  and has focused her message on protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Mr. Zeldin said in a recent ad that he wouldn't change New York's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. The unexpected competitiveness of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-10-24/card/hochul-zeldin-face-off-in-new-york-gubernatorial-debate-KFVeRy42PNdE1ifOJVgP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York contest }}}\uc2  has been cited by nonpartisan analysts as a sign of how much territory Democrats have to defend this cycle.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris will hold a rally with Illinois Gov. \uc2 J.B. Pritzker\uc2 , who has a more comfortable lead over his GOP opponent and has made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access a central issue to help get out the vote, and attend another event with Asian-American voters.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the summer and fall, Ms. Harris has been the administration's lead on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues. Many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates had expressed disappointment in the weeks after the Supreme Court ruling with what they viewed as a sluggish response from the White House, frustrations that some say have been assuaged by the vice president's efforts.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris has conducted roughly 60 events and interviews on the topic since the Supreme Court decision, many of them at universities, to appeal to younger people.\par \par \uc2 Although most of Ms. Harris's events are billed as White House discussions on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and not campaign rallies, she often touts the work of Democratic leaders up for re-election on the issue.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How much do you think the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights will factor into people's decisions on Election Day? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 She typically brings a color-coded map of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws as a prop, explains the implications of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-navigating-abortion-bans-in-medical-emergencies-11665684225"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's decision }}}\uc2  ending the federal constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and warns that Republicans will seek to pass a national ban if they win control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.) has introduced a bill to bar doctors from performing abortions after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lindsey-graham-defends-abortion-proposal-despite-gop-worries-11663524124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15 weeks of pregnancy }}}\uc2 . His proposal has gained little traction among Republicans in Congress, many of whom say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy should be left to states.\par \par \uc2 Some top Democrats and Sen. Bernie Sanders, a Vermont independent who twice sought the Democratic presidential nomination, say the party has lost ground because it hasn't focused enough on the economy, which they say is top of mind for most voters.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris said in an interview that Democrats "can walk and chew gum at the same time" by talking to voters about both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the economy. She and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-legalized-abortion-grows-since-dobbs-ruling-wsj-poll-shows-11662210020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supporters of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  say the ability to end an unplanned or risky pregnancy is an economic issue to many women.\par \par \uc2 "It's still a big issue for big demographics, and we will win some races that we shouldn't win because of it," said Democratic pollster John Anzalone, who conducted the WSJ survey with Republican pollster Tony Fabrizio.\par \par \uc2 The administration has taken some steps to preserve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, such as helping women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-sign-order-stepping-up-efforts-to-protect-access-to-reproductive-care-11657278000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 travel out of state }}}\uc2  to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Mr. Biden has said he would ask Congress to make its first priority a bill codifying Roe v. Wade into law if Democrats expand their ranks in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats are struggling to overcome the low approval ratings of both the president and Ms. Harris. The FiveThirtyEight average of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/approval/kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling results }}}\uc2 finds 38% of voters approve of Ms. Harris's performance in office and 51% disapprove, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President Biden's averages }}}\uc2  stand at 42% approval and 53% disapproval.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats in tight races have distanced themselves from the administration. White House officials said top Democratic leaders in some states have requested that Ms. Harris visit to remind voters of the issues surrounding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even if candidates in close races don't want to campaign alongside Ms. Harris or Mr. Biden.\par \par \uc2 In North Carolina, Ms. Harris said voters need to elect two more Democrats to the Senate to help codify Roe v. Wade into law. "Two votes," she said in Charlotte. "Right here in North Carolina\u8212\'20\'14Cheri Beasley\u8212\'20\'14who can win." A representative for Ms. Beasley, who didn't attend the event, didn't respond to a request for comment. Several recent polls show she is running behind her Republican opponent, Rep. \uc2 Ted Budd\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ms. Harris recently appeared at an event at Metropolitan State University in St. Paul, Minn., with elected officials from the state.\par \par \uc2 "It matters who represents the people of the state and is responsible for doing justice on behalf of those people when it comes to an issue like this," the vice president said. Her appearance was welcomed by Minnesota Attorney General Keith Ellison, who is running a close race against Republican candidate Jim Schultz. Mr. Ellison has made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a centerpiece of his bid for re-election.\par \par \uc2 "All I know how to do is try to do the best I can to excite as many people as I can. And she helped me do that," Mr. Ellison said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Schultz played down the significance of Ms. Harris's visit. "Minnesotans know that the twin themes of Ellison's office have been extremism and incompetence, and the vice president visiting Minnesota won't change their view," he said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tarini Parti at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Tarini.Parti@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tarini.Parti@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kamala-harris-seeks-to-rally-voters-on-abortion-as-polls-show-interest-waning-11667480402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris Seeks to Rally Voters on \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  as Polls Show Interest Waning  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221103eib3002jr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
