\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 In Virginia Midterm Battlegrounds, Republican Candidates Borrow From Youngkin's Approach; School policy in spotlight alongside inflation and  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  in three competitive House races\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalie Andrews \par \uc2 1,316 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 November 2022\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WOODBRIDGE, Va.\u8212\'20\'14In the final days of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wsj.com/livecoverage/latest-updates/midterms-elections-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the midterm campaign }}}\uc2  with a trio of Democratic House seats in play, Virginia Republicans are embracing an approach that helped Glenn Youngkin capture the governor's mansion: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-education-battles-republicans-see-a-winning-campaign-issue-11636109260"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 making the case that they listen to parents }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a recent television ad, Republican Yesli Vega stands before a classroom and says she will "never co-parent with the federal government." She references {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/youngkins-virginia-win-offers-midterm-road-map-for-gop-warning-for-democrats-11635942003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Youngkin's upset victory last year }}}\uc2 , in which the Republican won over independents and some Democrats in a blue-leaning state that backed President Biden by 10 percentage points in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Vega, a Prince William County deputy sheriff, is challenging two-term Democratic Rep. \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  in the exurbs and rural areas between Washington, D.C., and Richmond. In the two other competitive races, Republican state Sen. Jen Kiggans is challenging Democratic Rep. \uc2 Elaine Luria\uc2  in the Virginia Beach area, and Democratic Rep. \uc2 Jennifer Wexton\uc2  is defending her suburban Northern Virginia district against Republican Navy veteran Hung Cao. Of the three, Ms. Wexton's district is seen as the most likely to stay in Democratic hands, while the other two are true tossups.\par \par \uc2 How the state's races play out will form one piece of a broader puzzle of dozens of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-10-31/card/2022-midterms-election-outlook-house-iP1KhFGXlnc4JbsQovfU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 competitive House contests nationwide }}}\uc2 , as voters weigh issues such as inflation, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and crime. Nonpartisan election analysts favor Republicans to win the House, where they need to pick up a net of five seats to take control. Democrats now lead in the chamber, 220 to 212, with three absences.\par \par \uc2 In his 2021 run, Mr. Youngkin argued that parents had been shut out of decisions about race in the curriculum, Covid-19 precautions and academic standards. He has cast it as a guide that could help Republicans win in competitive races in 2022\u8212\'20\'14even as voters' focus has shifted to other issues\u8212\'20\'14and Ms. Vega has followed that lead.\par \par \uc2 "You all know the fight that we started here in this state last year, it was a movement where we said that parents absolutely mattered, and we haven't forgotten about that," Ms. Vega said last week at a rally with the governor.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Youngkin followed by saying Democrats "want to make sure the bureaucrats and politicians are inserted between parents and their kids."\par \par \uc2 Democrats say that they approved hundreds of billions of dollars in aid to reopen schools and distribute funding to communities and households during the pandemic. They also say that Republicans are politicizing decisions about classroom content best made by teachers and administrators. Democrats more broadly cite efforts to tame inflation by lowering prescription-drug costs and seeking to boost gasoline supplies, and they tout their support of broad access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which many Republicans oppose.\par \par \uc2 House Republicans, when introducing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-house-leader-kevin-mccarthy-rolls-out-commitment-to-america-for-midterms-11663953617"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their "Commitment to America" policy plan }}}\uc2  in September, said they would pass a Parents Bill of Rights that gives parents the "right to know what's being taught in schools and to see reading material." They also plan to push back on transgender girls being allowed to participate in school sports.\par \par \uc2 Christine Matthews, a Republican pollster, said increased concern over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access may temper GOP candidates' ability to win over Democratic votes in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 "You're not going to get a Democratic woman to vote for a Republican who is not going to support their right to choose," she said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal in Virginia up until 26 weeks and six days of pregnancy. Republican Virginia state Sen. Amanda Chase said Sunday that she would introduce a bill that bans all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nationally, nonpartisan Public Religion Research Institute polling published last week showed that voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prri.org/research/challenges-in-moving-toward-a-more-inclusive-democracy-findings-from-the-2022-american-values-survey/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ranked increasing costs and the health of democracy }}}\uc2  as the two top issues driving their vote. Education ranked sixth on the list with 41% of voters saying it was a key issue, behind crime, access to guns and gun safety, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Spanberger-Vega race is one of the most closely watched in the country. Ms. Spanberger, who worked undercover as a Central Intelligence Agency case officer, flipped a red seat in 2018 then narrowly won re-election in 2020. She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pelosi-faces-lawmakers-frustrated-over-loss-of-house-seats-11604621624"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been a critic of members of her own party }}}\uc2  who called to defund the police, and on the campaign trail she speaks mostly of policy plans to lower food and gas prices.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Spanberger has said that Ms. Vega is too extreme for the district, highlighting a clip in an ad where Ms. Vega doubted that a woman can get pregnant from rape and expressed support for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. She also says Ms. Vega's plans to boost parent involvement in schools is "no plan, it's fluffy words that mean different things to different people." Later, she quipped: "She could absolutely run for school board if she wanted to."\par \par \uc2 Ms. Vega says she is "proudly pro-life," and during the primary said she would support a law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from conception. But she says that isn't a top issue for voters she has talked to.\par \par \uc2 "Parental rights is above \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Ms. Vega said. "I believe that we have to get back to a place where our children are going back to school to learn how to read, do math, etc."\par \par \uc2 Voter Jennifer Quinonez, 36 years old, backs Ms. Vega, saying she likes candidates who speak to family values and the economy. She hopes Ms. Vega will "change things up" and "go against the flow of what Northern Virginia is right now," which she sees as too liberal.\par \par \uc2 "Definitely not Yesli Vega," said Sandra Brionez, 38, at a shopping center in Woodbridge. She said she couldn't support Ms. Vega because of the Republican's position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "That's the reason I definitely will not vote for her," she said.\par \par \uc2 Virginia's House delegation is composed of seven Democrats and four Republicans. The other competitive races also have touched on school issues. In an ad for her primary in the Virginia Beach district, Ms. Kiggans said that she protected students from what she calls politicized policies on gender identity and the teaching of race, saying schools "should be about education, not indoctrination."\par \par \uc2 In her recent ads, Ms. Kiggans ties Ms. Luria to high inflation and gas prices and doesn't bring up education. Ms. Luria won by about 6 points in 2020, but the area became more Republican in redistricting, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/virginia-democrat-plays-up-defense-as-build-back-better-stalks-sidelines-11638363600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raising Republican hopes of winning it back }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Which issues are most important to you as a voter? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 In the closing weeks, Ms. Luria has focused on her record as a Navy veteran and accused her opponent of being too extreme in her positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and for expressing doubts about the outcome of the 2020 presidential election. In responding to questions from local media, Ms. Kiggans has declined to say whether she thought Mr. Biden was fairly elected.\par \par \uc2 An Oct. 21 poll by the Wason Center in Newport News, Va., showed Ms. Kiggans and Ms. Luria tied, both with 45% of support among likely voters, with 8% undecided.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Wexton's district is seen as less competitive, but Republicans are excited about Mr. Cao. They see him as a strong candidate who could emerge with a victory amid a Republican wave on election night.\par \par \uc2 "Parents' rights are the biggest issue here in this district, besides the economy," he said Monday on Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Wexton said she is "proud that through my work in Congress we've successfully reopened schools and are helping students continue to make up for lost learning during the pandemic."\par \par \uc2 Write to Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Natalie.Andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Natalie.Andrews@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-virginia-battlegrounds-republican-candidates-borrow-from-youngkins-approach-11667390401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Virginia Midterm Battlegrounds, Republican Candidates Borrow From Youngkin's Approach }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221102eib2001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
