\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Kari Lake Unites Many Arizona Republicans After Party's Earlier Divisions Over Trump; Gubernatorial candidate claims 2020 presidential election was stolen; some supporters see her as a Reagan acolyte\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins | Photographs by Ash Ponders for The Wall Street Journal \par \uc2 1,639 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2022\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PHOENIX\u8212\'20\'14Kari Lake, the Republican candidate in the Arizona governor's race, has taken many pages from former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  's campaign playbook.\par \par \uc2 She repeats his false claims of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/jan-6-committee-subpoenas-former-president-donald-trump-11666374580"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rampant fraud in the 2020 election  }}}\uc2 . She attacks the legacy of the late Arizona GOP senator, \uc2 John McCain\uc2  . And she has made the media a favorite foil, even though she spent 22 years as an anchor for a local news station.\par \par \uc2 Where she and the former president differ is that Mr. Trump's contentions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/with-arizona-a-toss-up-in-midterms-infighting-reigns-among-gop-democrats-11650360600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tore apart the Arizona Republican party  }}}\uc2 , with supporters of the former president on one side and traditional pro-business Republicans on the other. Ms. Lake, by contrast, has gone a long way to stitching it back together even while claiming the 2020 election was stolen and saying that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/primary-election-results-august-2-az-ks-mo-mi-wa/card/kari-lake-wins-arizona-republican-gubernatorial-primary-yGX6Xfo89FDhq8EnfTbP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her win in the August primary  }}}\uc2  "drove a stake through the heart of the McCain machine."\par \par \uc2 Several Republicans who had supported Ms. Lake's opponent in the primary and are now backing her said they agreed with her policy proposals\u8212\'20\'14especially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/europes-economy-contracts-as-tough-winter-looms-11666608770"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the economy  }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14and they played down or omitted her contentions on election fraud.\par \par \uc2 There was no fraud in the 2020 election widespread enough to change the result, according to federal officials. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-made-legal-claims-of-election-fraud-he-knew-were-false-judge-says-11666215931"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dozens of lawsuits  }}}\uc2  filed by supporters of Mr. Trump challenging the results failed.\par \par \uc2 The party's coalescence behind her isn't unanimous, but it has given the political newcomer momentum in the race in the final weeks before the election, according to interviews with Republican and Democratic officials, strategists and voters.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake in an interview said the first things she would do as governor would be to take control of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/record-arrests-at-southern-u-s-border-fueled-by-migration-wave-11666556328"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 southern border  }}}\uc2  from the federal government and work {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/trump-biden-election-day-2020/card/Cp6Qn4nfW4MfEBymCHgK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to secure elections  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Don't believe what the, you know, corrupt media is saying that 'Oh, the party is not going to come.' They have completely come behind us," said Ms. Lake, 53 years old, in her campaign office with a large photo of Mr. Trump behind her.\par \par \uc2 The outcome Nov. 8 will depend on Ms. Lake's ability to bring independents and Republicans to her side in a contest likely to be close, as many recent elections in the state have been. Her opponent, Secretary of State \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  , a Democrat, won her last race by less than 6,000 votes; President Biden won Arizona by less than 11,000 votes. A Republican-led audit of the 2020 election results {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-gops-election-audit-confirms-biden-win-in-draft-report-11632467822"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed Mr. Biden's victory  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Most polls show the race as a statistical tie. Ms. Lake has committed only to accepting the results in the governor's race if she wins.\par \par \uc2 "I'll be very disappointed if Kari Lake doesn't win. And even though she's a little Trumpy, that's not a deal breaker for me," said Steve MacMillan, 59, a resident of Goodyear, a Phoenix suburb. He said he liked Ms. Lake's policy proposals but wishes she would talk less about the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Arizona voters know Ms. Lake because of her years anchoring newscasts for the local Fox channel in Phoenix. (Fox Corp. and News Corp, owner of The Wall Street Journal, share common ownership.) Many say they are nervous {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/inflation-definition-cause-what-is-it-11644353564"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about inflation  }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-gasoline-prices-are-climbing-again-and-may-get-worse-11665048601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high gas prices  }}}\uc2 , and polls show they trust Republicans over Democrats to handle the economy. The Phoenix metro area had the nation's highest rate of inflation at 13%, according to \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2  data released last month.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you think Kari Lake will fare in Arizona's gubernatorial race? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake also has proven to be an effective communicator\u8212\'20\'14often targeting the media, which she calls "fake news"\u8212\'20\'14while Ms. Hobbs has been stuck in a monthslong controversy over her refusal to debate Ms. Lake. Ms. Hobbs said in an interview that Ms. Lake's focus on the debate issue is "because she has nothing else to run on. She has no experience. She doesn't understand how government works. She's not offering real solutions to any of the issues we're facing."\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hobbs has said debating Ms. Lake would be a disservice to voters because Ms. Lake is a "conspiracy theorist."\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats are calling on Ms. Hobbs to be more aggressive toward Ms. Lake and to emphasize her governing credentials stemming from her experience as a former state legislator and secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake "is essentially a more polished version of Trump. My concern is that, as we learned with Trump in 2016, it's not enough to simply label a candidate as an extremist and therefore disqualified from being elected," said Roy Herrera, who worked as Mr. Biden's Arizona counsel in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake has said, if elected, she would eliminate cities' ability to put in place a rent and grocery tax. She has promised to offset the cost for five years with surplus state funds and then expects the state's rapid growth to provide a larger tax base to fund cities in the years to come.\par \par \uc2 "We will be providing the good people of Arizona some relief," she said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hobbs has proposed making diapers and baby formula tax exempt, a sales tax holiday on school supplies and a child tax credit. She said she wouldn't roll back tax cuts put in place under GOP Gov. \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2  , who is term-limited from running again. Changes in tax policy must be approved by the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 On the border, Ms. Lake has said she would declare an invasion and use state law enforcement to conduct border-security operations, including arresting and deporting migrants. Such plans are likely to face logistical and legal challenges from the federal government. Under federal law, only the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  has the authority to deport migrants accused of being in the country illegally.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Hobbs has called for more funding for border communities, including for law enforcement.\par \par \uc2 On elections, Ms. Lake has said she would work with the legislature to craft bills that would keep future elections secure. Ms. Lake is focused on ways to remove software from the process. As secretary of state, Ms. Hobbs is the chief elections administrator for the state and she was a leading figure in defending against fraud claims in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Not all Republicans are on board. "The very low bar that I've set for people to endorse in this election is No. 1 don't be an election denier," said John Giles, the Republican mayor of Phoenix suburb Mesa who has endorsed Ms. Hobbs.\par \par \uc2 "I'm worried about suffering potentially a real reputational risk and kind of losing the aura and the glow that the state has right now," said John Graham, the chairman of real-estate developer Sunbelt Holdings and a Republican supporting Ms. Hobbs.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake has made clear she isn't separating herself from Mr. Trump. "What would it say about my character if I stepped away from my friends?" she said as she hugged the former president at a rally earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 For many Republican voters, it is Ms. Lake's embrace of Mr. Trump, especially his claims of election fraud, that holds appeal. "There's Republicans and there's patriots, and she's a patriot," said Karen Phillips, 75, a real-estate agent from Chandler, another Phoenix suburb.\par \par \uc2 Yet Ms. Lake gauges how much to talk about Mr. Trump and his agenda depending on her audience, said four people who have been at events with her. "When Kari needs to turn on Trumpism she can and when she needs to switch to Reaganism she can," said senior adviser Colton Duncan. A video that plays ahead of events includes Ms. Lake talking about how former President \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  is her hero.\par \par \uc2 There is no better example of the party coming around to Ms. Lake than Gov. Ducey.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake hammered him during her primary campaign for his decision to certify the 2020 election results, among other things. She called him "do nothing Ducey" and "doormat Ducey." Mr. Ducey said Ms. Lake was putting on an act and "misleading voters" with her claims of a fraudulent election.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake said the pair since have had one meeting and Mr. Ducey has said he would support the whole Republican slate. The \uc2 Republican Governors Association\uc2  , of which Mr. Ducey is the chairman, has spent roughly $10 million to support Ms. Lake. Mr. Ducey, through a spokesman, declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Sara Glass, 64, a Chandler resident who works in human resources, is unhappy with Ms. Lake's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the election. As a "former news anchor, she would know that you do your due diligence, you do your research. When your research proves otherwise, you've got your answer," she said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats say differences between Ms. Lake and Ms. Hobbs on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could benefit Ms. Hobbs following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Supreme Court decision in June  }}}\uc2  that eliminated the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state is in dispute. Arizona {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-legislature-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11648156791"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans most abortions after 15 weeks  }}}\uc2 , but a separate law from when Arizona was a territory {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-appeals-court-blocks-territorial-era-abortion-law-11665194904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could impose a near-complete ban  }}}\uc2 . Its applicability is now being litigated in court.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake has said she opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will enforce whatever the law is. Ms. Hobbs opposes any restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has said she would veto any legislative measure to impose them.\par \par \uc2 Alicia A. Caldwell contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins+1@wsj.com."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins+1@wsj.com.  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kari-lake-unites-many-arizona-republicans-after-partys-earlier-divisions-over-trump-11666690203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kari Lake Unites Many Arizona Republicans After Party's Earlier Divisions Over Trump  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221025eiap000rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
