\par \par \uc2 GOP gubernatorial candidate Tudor Dixon is a conservative commentator new to politics. She opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except in cases where the mother's health is at risk. PHOTO: Emily Elconin for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Ms. Dixon, a 45-year-old conservative commentator new to politics, said in a statement that Michigan voters tell her they care far less about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than they do about the increase in violent crime, their children's learning loss during the pandemic and what they see as overregulation that is driving away businesses.\par \par \uc2 Both parties say that appealing to suburban women, a key swing group, will be critical to winning races across the country this fall. Women are more likely to vote for Democrats, and pollsters and political strategists say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is an issue that could push independent and some Republican suburban women toward the party. Polling has consistently shown that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-legalized-abortion-grows-since-dobbs-ruling-wsj-poll-shows-11662210020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most Americans support legal access }}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Election Day is less than three weeks away. Democrats and Republicans across the country are fighting for control of the House of Representatives, Senate, governors' mansions and state legislatures. The WSJ is providing live coverage as campaigns enter the final stretch. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-10-21"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Follow along here }}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is legal and where it loses protections without Roe v. Wade }}}\par \par \uc2 About Us\par \par \uc2 This newsletter is written by the WSJ Washington bureau. Sign up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/newsletters?sub=230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 . Send feedback to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:capitaljournal@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 capitaljournal@wsj.com }}}\uc2 . You can follow politics coverage on our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/news/politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politics }}}\uc2  page and at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WSJPolitics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @wsjpolitics }}}\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortions-impact-on-the-2022-midterm-elections-11666378930"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 's Impact on the 2022 Midterm Elections }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221023eian000jh\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
