\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Republican Midterm Prospects Brighten in Closing Weeks of Election; Renewed focus on the economy has stalled Democrats' momentum in key contests, analysts say; Senate control remains up for grabs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Aaron Zitner \par \uc2 1,198 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2022\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Infusions of ad spending for GOP candidates and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/us-inflation-september-2022-consumer-price-index-11665628037"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 persistent voter anxiety over high inflation }}}\uc2  have brought new momentum to the Republican Party in House and Senate races, analysts say, just as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-10-19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early voting has begun }}}\uc2  for the midterm elections in many states.\par \par \uc2 A Democratic lead of about 2 percentage points on the generic ballot\u8212\'20\'14the question of whether voters plan to back a Democrat or Republican for Congress\u8212\'20\'14has been cut by more than half since late September, the FiveThirtyEight average of polling results finds. Democratic leads in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/2022-senate-and-house-midterm-election-ratings-and-analysis-11664905703"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many Senate races }}}\uc2  have declined, according to aggregated polls, and Democratic candidates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wisconsins-ron-johnson-showing-strength-in-state-biden-won-11665602003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now trail in surveys in Wisconsin }}}\uc2  and Nevada, where they were once ahead. Control of both chambers hangs in the balance.\par \par \uc2 A surge of good news for Democrats in the summer and early fall, as well as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pushes-some-suburban-women-in-west-michigan-toward-democrats-11666085403"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 burst of Democratic engagement }}}\uc2  in the election after the Supreme Court ended federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in June, appears to have given way to the factors that traditionally weigh on the president's party in a midterm election, as many voters tend to sour on the party in power and those backing the party that lost the White House are most eager to vote again.\par \par \uc2 The bottom line, analysts from both parties say, is Republicans are increasingly likely to gain well over the net five seats needed to retake the majority in the House, which they lost in 2018, while control of the 50-50 Senate could still fall to either party.\par \par \uc2 "Throughout the summer, there had been quite a few advantages for Democrats, with the dramatic intervention of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision. It energized younger voters, women and Democrats," said Democratic pollster Celinda Lake. Now, she said, "you do see some settling down into traditional patterns of off-year elections."\par \par \uc2 "Dobbs changed the election and put Democrats back into contention\u8212\'20\'14that's true," said Republican pollster Bill McInturff, referring to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high court's \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ruling. }}}\uc2  But about 70% of voters say the country is headed in the wrong direction, he added.\par \par \uc2 Even as many voters remained concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , President Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is drawing low job-approval ratings, }}}\uc2  and worries about inflation and the economy remain high.\par \par \uc2 "There has never been a time when an incumbent party is going to thrive with that set of factors," Mr. McInturff said.\par \par \uc2 Since World War II, the president's party has lost House seats in every midterm election except two, and presidents with low approval ratings fare the worst. In midterms from 1962 through 2018, presidents with job-approval ratings under 50% have lost 39 House seats on average, Mr. McInturff finds, using Gallup data that excludes the Watergate year of 1974. Mr. Biden's approval rating has been in the low- to mid-40% range in aggregated polls.\par \par \uc2 Democrats faced a difficult environment heading into this year's midterms. The party's legislative priorities in Congress had stalled, and substantially more Democrats in vulnerable House races than Republicans chose not to seek re-election, a factor that usually helps challengers.\par \par \uc2 But in August, Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/joe-biden-to-sign-bill-aimed-at-lowering-drug-costs-boosting-renewable-energy-11660642202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 navigated a major bill into law }}}\uc2  that aims to invest in clean energy and reduce healthcare costs. Wariness of new state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations was credited with helping Democrats win a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-outlook-for-midterm-elections-brightens-after-new-york-win-11661368975"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tossup special election }}}\uc2  for a House seat from New York and with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-vote-signals-abortion-could-emerge-as-top-political-issue-in-november-11659555741"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unexpected defeat of a referendum in Kansas }}}\uc2  that would have eliminated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state. Analysts said the Supreme Court \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling drove up voter registration in many states among women, who as a group lean Democratic.\par \par \uc2 Now, said Nathan Gonzales, editor of the nonpartisan newsletter Inside Elections, "Democratic momentum has stalled. The optimism coming out of the special election wins has waned a little bit." But at the same time, he said, "we haven't seen a dramatic shift toward Republicans."\par \par \uc2 Several Senate races remain tight, with the two candidates separated by 3 percentage points or less in polling aggregates in four states: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ohios-ryan-offers-potential-road-map-for-democrats-struggling-in-rust-belt-11664616604"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio, }}}\uc2  Nevada, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/wisconsins-ron-johnson-showing-strength-in-state-biden-won-11665602003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin }}}\uc2  and North Carolina. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aarp.org/content/dam/aarp/research/surveys_statistics/politics/2022/aarp-pennsylvania-october-2022-elections-voter-survey.doi.10.26419-2Fres.00550.031.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll released Tuesday }}}\uc2  in a fifth state, Pennsylvania, finds {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/john-fettermans-health-clouds-pennsylvania-senate-race-11657713602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat John Fetterman, }}}\uc2  the lieutenant governor, with a 2-point lead over Mehmet Oz, the celebrity doctor. Mr. Fetterman had led by 6 points in a June survey by the same pollsters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/walker-warnock-set-to-square-off-in-lone-debate-in-georgia-senate-race-11665764251"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia's contest }}}\uc2  also remains closely watched.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What are your predictions for the midterm elections? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts had expected Senate races to tighten as Republicans emerged from contentious primary elections and eventually unified GOP voters behind them, while their allies began spending on TV ads intended to tarnish their Democratic opponents. That appears to be the case in Pennsylvania's neck-and-neck race, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/republicans-mount-rescue-effort-in-pennsylvania-for-mastriano-oz-campaigns-11662131864"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Oz and his allies had been outspent }}}\uc2  3-to-2 by their Democratic opponents in advertising dollars during July and August, according to AdImpact, which tracks ad spending by campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the two sides have been closer to parity in their ad spending, with Mr. Oz and his allies running multiple TV ads that portray Mr. Fetterman as too eager to release dangerous criminals in his role as head of the state Board of Pardons. The Fetterman campaign has said that many inmates were deserving of release, among them those with model records in prison.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say that the voting decisions of independents is a top concern.\par \par \uc2 "A quarter to a third of independents are still undecided, and they moved slightly from leaning slightly Democratic to slightly Republican," said Ms. Lake. These voters, she said, tend to have lower incomes than core members of either party and are more concerned about the economy and inflation.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Lake said the Democratic Party's challenge is to show voters that it has a better economic plan than the GOP, possibly by focusing on the party's efforts to cut medical costs and protect Social Security and Medicare.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden in recent weeks has released a plan to forgive student loans for many borrowers. On Tuesday, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/midterms-elections-voting-2022-10-18/card/biden-to-push-abortion-rights-bill-if-democrats-keep-control-of-congress-xBC4jF4vDlnbWBNZLvkF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returned to the issue of legalized \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 , }}}\uc2  saying he would fast-track a bill to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into law if Democrats maintained control of the Senate and House.\par \par \uc2 Still, polls show that voters rate the economy and inflation as the most important issue in deciding which party to support, and they give Mr. Biden low marks for his economic stewardship. In Mr. McInturff's view, those are substantial problems that will make it hard for Democratic candidates who may be leading, but still shy of a majority, to gain the last few votes they need to win.\par \par \uc2 "A great candidate can run 8 points ahead of their president," Mr. McInturff said. "That's what fabulous candidates do in a campaign with a flawed opponent. But to do it everywhere, in every campaign, in one night, is really hard. That's why I think the Senate is in a coin flip."\par \par \uc2 Write to Aaron Zitner at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:aaron.zitner@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aaron.zitner@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/republican-midterm-prospects-brighten-in-closing-weeks-of-election-11666171802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Midterm Prospects Brighten in Closing Weeks of Election  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221019eiaj000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
