\par\par \uc2 CMO Today\par \uc2 C Suite\par \b \uc2 Uber\uc2  to Let Marketers Target Riders by Destination; The ride-hailing company is expanding its advertising business, offering ads across its app for the first time\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patrick Coffee \par \uc2 823 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2022\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ride-hailing company \uc2 Uber Technologies Inc\uc2 . wants to help marketers target consumers with ads based on where they have been and where they are going.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  announced the new capability as it rolled out its mobility media division, offering ads across its ride-hailing app for the first time. These ads will be available in select markets at launch. The company sees huge potential for revenue growth in the new ad-targeting product, though some experts say it could raise concerns about consumer privacy.\par \par \uc2 Companies like \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 .'s \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Meta Platforms Inc\uc2 .'s \uc2 Facebook\uc2  have long recorded users' web behavior to target them with ads. Retailers such as \uc2 Walmart Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Kroger Co\uc2 . can track when, where and how you shop for the benefit of brands that advertise with them.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  has been building its ad business for several years, though most of its growth to date has come from ads placed on the Uber Eats food-delivery app, said Mark Grether, general manager of Uber Advertising.\par \par \uc2 The ride-hailing ad business could grow far larger, Mr. Grether said, especially when self-driving cars become more common.\par \par \uc2 "Cars will become our next living rooms," Mr. Grether said. "We spend eight hours a week in a car; it's a huge advertising opportunity."\par \par \uc2 At a February investor event, Mr. Grether said \uc2 Uber\uc2 's overall ad revenue jumped to $141 million in 2021 from $11 million in 2020, and he predicted it would hit $1 billion by 2024.\par \par \uc2 The new ad-targeting product will let brands place ads using data drawn from both riders' recent travel history and their precise geographic destinations, according to the company. If a user books an \uc2 Uber\uc2  to a specific retailer, cinema or airport, for example, a company could buy ads centered on that location.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  will also now let a single brand sponsor the entire trip, starting when a user first calls a car. These so-called "journey ads," which will be sold on a per-trip basis instead of digital advertising's common pricing by consumer impression, let brands show a user different ads at three points in the user's trip: while waiting for a car, while riding in the car and upon reaching the destination.\par \par \uc2 The rider can also conduct transactions, such as clicking the ad to buy a product without leaving the \uc2 Uber\uc2  app, said Mr. Grether. Separate pilot programs in the U.S. and India will also include ads on in-car tablets, he said.\par \par \uc2 The geotargeting options could lead to legal complications, said Brandi Bennett, who leads the data-privacy practice at law firm The Beckage Firm.\par \par \uc2 "Precise geolocation data is what I call 'digital plutonium.' When you have geolocation data, you can unravel people's lives," Ms. Bennett said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  displayed a heightened interest in geolocation data {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ftc-sues-idaho-company-for-selling-sensitive-tracking-data-11661798303"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by suing data broker Kochava Inc. }}}\uc2  in August, looking to halt the sale of data it said could be used to track people to sensitive locations. \uc2 Kochava\uc2  had previously sued the F.T.C. in anticipation of the suit.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2 's computers were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/uber-says-it-is-victim-of-lapsus-a-hacking-group-motivated-by-fame-not-money-11663674367"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 breached by a teenage hacker }}}\uc2  in September, and in 2016 a former employee claimed that \uc2 Uber\uc2  staffers were able to search and review travel data for politicians, former romantic partners and celebrities like Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  has one of the tech industry's richest data sets on users, including their credit-card numbers, home addresses and places they often visit, said Ms. Bennett. The Supreme Court's decision to eliminate the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/phones-know-who-went-to-an-abortion-clinic-whom-will-they-tell-11659873781"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presents another potential concern }}}\uc2 , as states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal could subpoena data on customers who may have taken an \uc2 Uber\uc2  to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, Ms. Bennett said.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Uber\uc2  spokeswoman said the company doesn't share individual users' data with advertisers. The data it does share is aggregated information or data related to ad-campaign performance, she said. Users can opt out of targeted ads on the \uc2 Uber\uc2  app at any time, said Mr. Grether.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2 's advertising policy forbids targeting users by factors such as race, religion or sexual orientation, and it also prohibits basing ad targeting on certain types of destinations, including government buildings, hospitals and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  centers.\par \par \uc2 The company recently said it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lyft-to-cover-legal-costs-of-drivers-sued-under-texas-abortion-law-11630700449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cover the legal bills }}}\uc2  of any drivers sued for transporting women to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. The spokeswoman said \uc2 Uber\uc2  will follow all applicable laws, including one recently passed in California that protects residents and businesses from lawsuits related to other states' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2 's top competitor, \uc2 Lyft Inc\uc2 ., {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lyft-creates-media-division-to-expand-its-advertising-services-11659956407"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officially launched its Lyft Media advertising division }}}\uc2  in August. Both companies began selling ads atop their cars in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patrick Coffee at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:patrick.coffee@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patrick.coffee@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/uber-to-let-marketers-target-riders-by-destination-11666184402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uber to Let Marketers Target Riders by Destination }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221019eiaj001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
