\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Biden's Top 2023 Priority:  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; The President tells voters what he wants to do first next year if Democrats retain control of Congress.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 427 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 October 2022\par 22:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats are worried that voters are moving toward Republicans as the midterm elections near, and President Biden on Tuesday came out with his counteroffer: A national law that would allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to the last day of pregnancy in all 50 states.\par \par \uc2 With three weeks before Election Day, Mr. Biden told the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  that if Democrats keep control of Congress, "the first bill that I will send to the Congress" will codify a nationwide right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Not lowering the price of gas or home heating (see nearby), not rebuilding U.S. defenses, and not easing his regulatory onslaught amid what economists now say is a likely recession in 2023. No, job one in year three of the Biden Presidency will be imposing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  values of New York and California on Louisiana and Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden didn't stipulate what the law he'd support would look like, but it's a fair surmise that it would be close to what House Democrats passed, and Senate Democrats tried to pass, this year. That bill is more permissive than the Roe v. Wade regime the Supreme Court struck down in late June.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic bill allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand through what it calls "fetal viability," or about 23 weeks. After that an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would still be legal if there is a risk to the mother's "health," which isn't defined. In practice this would be interpreted to include mental-health or emotional issues and would contradict state laws that define it as physical health. The Senate version was too much even for pro-choice Republicans \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  and \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2 , who opposed it.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's speech is a political bet that stressing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will drive more suburban women to the polls and save imperiled Democrats. But polls show that, while a majority of Americans want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal early in pregnancy, they also want more restrictions than the Democratic bill allows.\par \par \uc2 Every poll also shows that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is well down the list of voter priorities\u8212\'20\'14after the economy and inflation. In this week's Siena/New York Times poll, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ranks fourth at 5%, tied with immigration, as the most important voter concern. At least Mr. Biden is telling voters what his party's priority is, and it isn't easing the price of gasoline or groceries.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/president-bidens-top-2023-priority-abortion-law-50-states-congress-11666128798"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden's Top 2023 Priority: \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221018eiai0073l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
