\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , Raphael Warnock Spar Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 , Inflation in Lone Georgia Senate Debate; Contest that could help determine Senate control draws more attention as Walker grapples with controversies about personal life\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lindsay Wise and Joshua Jamerson \par \uc2 1,438 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 October 2022\par 01:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic Sen. \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and Republican challenger \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  clashed over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/us-inflation-september-2022-consumer-price-index-11665628037"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflation }}}\uc2  and healthcare in their only debate Friday night, a hotly anticipated event thanks to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/herschel-walkers-georgia-senate-campaign-scrambled-by-allegations-about-past-behavior-11664912481"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Walker's controversial campaign }}}\uc2  and Georgia's emergence as a perennial battleground state.\par \par \uc2 "This race ain't about me. It's about what \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  have done to you and your family," Mr. Walker said in his opening remarks. He went on to try repeatedly to link the incumbent senator to the president.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warnock pointed out that he had grown up in housing projects about a mile from where the debate was taking place in Savannah. "When I think about the arc of my life, the short distance and the long distance from there to here, I know that only in America is my story possible," he said. "At the end of the day. This race is about who's ready to represent Georgia in the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2 . I think that choice is clear."\par \par \uc2 The Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-happens-if-the-senate-is-split-50-50-after-the-georgia-runoffs-11609965242"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is split 50-50 between the parties }}}\uc2 , with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  casting tiebreaking votes. Democratic officials in Washington have said their easiest path to keeping the Senate majority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/nevada-senate-race-emerges-as-test-of-abortion-issue-after-roe-v-wade-overturned-11661004000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is protecting four vulnerable incumbents }}}\uc2 : Mr. Warnock, \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  of Nevada, Mark Kelly of Arizona and \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  of New Hampshire. If Republicans hold all their current seats, they only need to defeat one of those Democrats to take control of the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warnock has a fundraising advantage and holds an edge in most polling. He leads Mr. Walker by roughly 4 percentage points in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/senate/2022/georgia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FiveThirtyEight's average of public surveys }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If no candidate gets more than 50% of the vote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-to-vote-in-the-2022-midterm-elections-a-state-by-state-guide-11665750154"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Election Day }}}\uc2 , the winner will be determined in a runoff Dec. 6.\par \par \uc2 Endorsed by former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Mr. Walker has faced scrutiny of his record as a businessman and questions about his family life, including allegations that he threatened to kill his ex-wife. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/primary-election-results-latest-news/card/football-star-herschel-walker-wins-georgia-senate-gop-primary-bfDIAAhIIfc2LleWGVDI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former football star }}}\uc2  has said he can't remember his actions at that time, when he said he was struggling with his mental health, and that he since has sought forgiveness.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker also in recent weeks faced allegations of violence and hypocrisy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/herschel-walkers-georgia-senate-campaign-scrambled-by-allegations-about-past-behavior-11664912481"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 leveled by his adult son on social media }}}\uc2 . "You're not a 'family man' when you left us to bang a bunch of women, threatened to kill us, and had us move over 6 times in 6 months running from your violence," Christian Walker said on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . The younger Mr. Walker, a conservative social-media influencer, also said in a video that his father shouldn't present himself as a moral family man: "He has four kids, four different women, wasn't in the house raising one of them."\par \par \uc2 Christian Walker's social-media remarks came after the Daily Beast reported that his father\u8212\'20\'14who has said during his campaign that he opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even in cases of rape, incest or danger to a mother's life\u8212\'20\'14reimbursed a woman for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  he urged her to get when they were dating in 2009. The Wall Street Journal hasn't verified the reporting by the Daily Beast. Mr. Walker has denied that he had paid for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker denied the allegation again when asked by the moderators Friday.\par \par \uc2 "I say that's a lie, and on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , you know I'm a Christian. I believe in life," he said. "And I tell people this: Georgia is a state that respects life. And I'll be a senator that protects life."\par \par \uc2 Throughout the debate, Mr. Walker repeatedly hit Mr. Warnock for voting too much with Mr. Biden, whose approval ratings are low but have inched up in recent months.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What do you hope the candidates discuss at the Georgia Senate debate? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warnock said it is clear that Mr. Walker would rather be running against Mr. Biden.\par \par \uc2 "There are only two people who are going to sit in the seat, either me or my opponent," Mr. Warnock said.\par \par \uc2 "I'm running against he and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  because they're the same," Mr. Walker replied, citing a FiveThirtyEight analysis that shows Mr. Warnock has voted with Mr. Biden about 96% of the time.\par \par \uc2 Later, in response to questions from the moderators, Mr. Walker said he would support Mr. Trump should he run for president in 2024 while Mr. Warnock wouldn't say if he wanted Mr. Biden to run again.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether Mr. Biden had won the 2020 election, Mr. Walker said he had. The Republican avoided answering similar questions at times earlier in his campaign and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2021/08/28/politics/fact-check-herschel-walker-2020-election-january-6/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falsely said }}}\uc2  there was widespread fraud in the election.\par \par \uc2 The men also argued about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with Mr. Warnock saying the government should stay out of women's private medical decisions, and Mr. Walker saying he supports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-abortion-restrictions-spark-new-debate-over-claims-to-fetal-personhood-11661601601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia's current law banning \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  once a heartbeat is detected, typically at about six weeks. Mr. Walker had previously said he didn't support exceptions that would allow abortions in cases of rape, incest or to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 "We are witnessing right now what happens when politicians\u8212\'20\'14most of them men\u8212\'20\'14pile into patients' rooms. You get what you're seeing right now," Mr. Warnock said. "And the women of Georgia deserve a senator who will stand with them. I trust women more than I trust politicians."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker said that there was a baby in that room as well. "And also did [Mr. Warnock] not mention that he's asking the taxpayer to pay for it? So he's bringing the government back into the room," he said.\par \par \uc2 In another exchange, Mr. Warnock noted that Mr. Walker has said he would vote against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/whats-in-joe-manchin-and-chuck-schumers-reconciliation-deal-on-climate-health-and-tax-policy-11658973323"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Inflation Reduction Act }}}\uc2 , which included provisions championed by Mr. Warnock that will cap the out-of-pocket cost of insulin next year at $35 a month for Medicare Part D beneficiaries.\par \par \uc2 "You know, I believe in reducing insulin, but at the same time you got to eat right\u8230\'20\'26so you have to get food prices down and you got to get gas down so they can go get insulin," Mr. Walker responded.\par \par \uc2 "I meet people all the time in my church who are trying to manage their diabetes," Mr. Warnock said. "I've been there when they've gotten the news that they've got to get an amputation. And I think we're hearing from my opponent tonight, that it's their fault that prices of insulin are being gouged. I don't think it's their fault. I think it's the fault of these pharmaceutical companies."\par \par \uc2 One odd moment during the debate came when Mr. Warnock suggested that, unlike his opponent, he had never pretended to be a police officer. Mr. Walker then flashed a law-enforcement badge and was admonished by the moderators for using a prop, which wasn't allowed under the rules. Mr. Walker has drawn scrutiny in the past for his unverified claims that he has worked in law enforcement; his campaign has said he was an honorary sheriff's deputy.\par \par \uc2 Georgia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-make-historic-gain-in-georgia-as-senate-control-hangs-in-balance-11609941722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has shifted toward the Democrats }}}\uc2  after decades of Republican dominance. Democrats notched back-to-back victories in the state in the 2020 presidential race, when Mr. Biden narrowly defeated Mr. Trump, and in January 2021 Senate runoff elections, when victories by Mr. Warnock and \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  gave Democrats control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warnock, the pastor of Rev. \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2 .'s former church in Atlanta, defeated GOP businesswoman Kelly Loeffler two years ago in a special election to fill the remainder of the late GOP Sen. Johnny Isakson's term, putting him back on the ballot earlier than Mr. Ossoff, who won a full six-year term.\par \par \uc2 The two highest-profile races on the ballot in Georgia this year also may be headed toward an election-year rarity: a split decision between Democrats and Republicans for the state's top offices. While Mr. Walker risks losing his race, Republican Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2  leads in most polls over \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , the Democratic nominee for governor. Those two are set to debate twice: Oct. 17 and Oct. 30.\par \par \uc2 Write to Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Joshua Jamerson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:joshua.jamerson+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joshua.jamerson+1@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/walker-warnock-set-to-square-off-in-lone-debate-in-georgia-senate-race-11665764251"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Herschel Walker, Raphael Warnock Spar Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 , Inflation in Lone Georgia Senate Debate }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221014eiae0058x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
