\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Arizona  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law Dating Back to 1864 Blocked by Appeals Court; Lower court had allowed the near-total ban to become enforceable again\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 477 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2022\par 13:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 An Arizona appeals court on Friday temporarily halted enforcement of a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state, a victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups in a novel legal battle over whether the courts should allow enforcement of a law tracing back to the mid-19th century.\par \par \uc2 The three-judge appellate panel said in a written order that the pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  side had demonstrated "a substantial likelihood of success on the merits," saying the trial judge had failed to take into account more recent laws governing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state, including legislation passed this spring {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-legislature-passes-15-week-abortion-ban-11648156791"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning most abortions after 15 weeks.  }}}\par \par \uc2 "Arizona courts have a responsibility to attempt to harmonize all of this state's relevant statutes," Judge Peter Eckerstrom wrote in the order.\par \par \uc2 The near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban traces back to an 1864 territorial rule\u8212\'20\'14before Arizona was a state. The law bans nearly all abortions in the state except in cases where it is necessary to save the life of the woman. Under the statute, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers could face two to five years in prison for violating the law.\par \par \uc2 The ban had previously been blocked by the court for some 50 years, since the Supreme Court found a federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  in Roe v. Wade.  }}}\uc2  After the Supreme Court overturned Roe in late June, Arizona Attorney General \uc2 Mark Brnovich\uc2  filed a motion in mid-July asking a court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-can-enforce-near-total-abortion-ban-blocked-for-50-years-judge-rules-11663976573"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to lift the injunction on the law,  }}}\uc2  saying it was based solely on the protections formerly provided by the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 "Our office understands this is an emotional issue, and we will carefully review the court's ruling before determining the next step," a spokeswoman for the \uc2 Arizona Attorney General's office\uc2  said following Friday's appeals court ruling.\par \par \uc2 Eight states, including Michigan, Arizona and Wisconsin, had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laws on the books that predated Roe  }}}\uc2  but had been dormant for the past 50 years, causing significant confusion in many of these places in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Arizona said Friday that it plans to resume offering abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 "While today's ruling brings temporary respite to Arizonans, the ongoing threat of this extreme, near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban that has no regard for the healthcare of those across the state, including survivors of rape or incest, remains very real," said Brittany Fonteno, the group's president and chief executive.\par \par \uc2 The Arizona decision was the second legal victory Friday for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters. A state court judge in Ohio also blocked enforcement of a ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state after around six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-appeals-court-blocks-territorial-era-abortion-law-11665194904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law Dating Back to 1864 Blocked by Appeals Court  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221008eia80008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
