\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 66  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Clinics No Longer Provide Abortions After Roe Overturned, Study Says; Twenty-six of those clinics have closed, though some have reopened or plan to reopen in other locations\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 727 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par 21:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 60 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics across the U.S. have stopped providing the procedure since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated federal constitutional protections }}}\uc2  in June, according to a new study.\par \par \uc2 The report, published Thursday by the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , found 14 states in which all clinics have ceased \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services since the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v. Wade. More broadly, 66 clinics in 15 states have stopped providing abortions; 40 of those clinics still provide other services, while 26 have closed, according to Guttmacher, a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and tracks national and state statistics.\par \par \uc2 The report offers a glimpse into the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 patchwork of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  that has emerged since the Supreme Court sent the legality of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back to the states }}}\uc2 . Over the past three months, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/west-virginia-passes-near-total-abortion-ban-11663107167"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans on nearly all abortions }}}\uc2  have taken effect in about a dozen states, while restrictions on most abortions after six weeks or 15 weeks of pregnancy have been enforced in others.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups and providers say the implementation of these new laws have caused chaos and confusion for patients and staff, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-wake-of-roe-v-wade-ruling-abortion-providers-confront-new-landscape-11656268445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 particularly in the days and weeks }}}\uc2  immediately after the high court's decision. Legal advocacy groups and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuits-to-test-whether-state-constitutions-protect-abortion-rights-11657375200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenged the new laws }}}\uc2  in state courts, arguing they violate aspects of state constitutions. Continuing litigation over the laws in some states has caused local clinics to close, then reopen, then close again.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  report focused on states where bans and narrow restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have taken effect over the past few months. In those 15 states, which include Alabama, Georgia, Kentucky, Texas and Mississippi, 79 clinics provided abortions before the Supreme Court's decision in June. By Oct. 2, 13 clinics still provided abortions. All of those are located in Georgia, where a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-six-week-abortion-ban-goes-into-effect-11658352186"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban on most abortions after six weeks }}}\uc2  of pregnancy took effect in July.\par \par \uc2 Since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-nearly-century-old-abortion-ban-in-effect-for-now-states-high-court-says-11656780694?"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enforcement of Texas laws banning nearly all abortions }}}\uc2 , 12 clinics in the state have completely closed. Eleven others have remained open, offering services other than \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to the study.\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, legal uncertainty over a 1849 ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has prompted the state's clinics to stop providing the procedure. The state's attorney general has vowed not to prosecute clinics under the law, but providers have said they are worried about future actions against them.\par \par \uc2 Some of the closed clinics have already reopened or announced plans to find a new location in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains legal. Clinics closing in states including Mississippi, Texas, North Dakota, Tennessee and Louisiana are aiming to reopen in Illinois, New Mexico or, potentially, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Jackson Women's Health Organization, the Mississippi clinic at the center of the Supreme Court case, closed in Jackson and opened a new location in Las Cruces, N.M., the clinic's owner said. Red River Women's Clinic, previously the only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in North Dakota, moved equipment and staff across state lines to Moorhead, Minn., in August. North Dakota wasn't included in the research group's study since the state's trigger law banning most abortions has been temporarily blocked in court.\par \par \uc2 Researchers at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  said the number of clinic closures will likely grow. They expect new restrictions will take effect in more states, including Indiana, South Carolina and Ohio, the timing of which depends on ongoing litigation and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-abortion-bans-face-obstacles-as-republicans-clash-11660908536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state legislative efforts }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "An already precarious \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access landscape is likely to continue to deteriorate," \uc2 Rachel Jones\uc2 , principal researcher at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , said in a statement. Ms. Jones said more research will need to be done to understand the full impact of the high court's decision.\par \par \uc2 "The picture that is starting to emerge should alarm anyone who supports reproductive freedom and the right to bodily autonomy," she added.\par \par \uc2 Representatives at national antiabortion groups said they believe the report is an encouraging sign for a post-Roe America.\par \par \uc2 "When an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility closes, that hopefully means more babies will live," said Carol Tobias, president of the \uc2 National Right to Life Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/66-abortion-clinics-no-longer-provide-abortions-after-roe-overturned-study-says-11665090090"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 66 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Clinics No Longer Provide Abortions After Roe Overturned, Study Says }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221006eia6007bx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
