\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 The Political Case for Federal  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Limits; Only 10% of voters support the Democrats' extreme position, while 72% back restrictions at 15 weeks.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Marjorie Dannenfelser \par \uc2 945 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 October 2022\par 21:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ahead of November's midterm elections, Republicans have a $124 million problem. That's how much pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrats have already spent on TV ads slamming the GOP after the Supreme Court's June decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization. The Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/2022-midterm-elections-abortion-health-congress-4be6df000de67933fcdabcd6f7b56a3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  this is more than twice what Democrats are spending on their "next top issue this year, 'character,' and almost 20 times more than Democrats spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ads in the 2018 midterms."\par \par \uc2 Faced with this onslaught, too many ordinarily outspoken pro-life Republicans have ducked for cover\u8212\'20\'14with consultants leading the retreat. But whether the consultants like it or not, the debate won't go away. The only way to win is to confront it head-on.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsjplus.com/invites/opinion-live-congress-dallas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WSJ Opinion Live: Can Republicans Retake Congress?}}}\par \par \uc2 Join Journal Editorial Page Editor Paul Gigot and Columnists Kimberley Strassel and Karl Rove live from Dallas as they discuss how inflation, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Supreme Court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling will affect the midterms. What's at stake in the House and Senate? Will the red wave hit as many predict? The panel will break down what the election will mean for the economy, President Biden's legislative agenda, and the run up to the 2024 presidential race.\par \par \uc2 WSJ members are invited to attend this exclusive member event live in Dallas, TX, or via livestream online on Monday, October 17 at 7:00 PM CT / 8:00 PM ET. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://events.wsjplus.com/OpinionLiveOct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Purchase}}}\uc2  tickets to the live event in Dallas or to register for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/live-qa/wsj-opinion-live-can-republicans-retake-congress/35FC8ECA-5145-4355-AA65-F235F1F47C30"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 virtual livestream}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By introducing a minimum federal limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks, Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.) and Rep. Chris Smith (R., N.J.) stepped up to offer fellow Republicans the political gift of contrast. They would be wise to use it. Every pro-life Republican should support these bills\u8212\'20\'14indeed, many previously voted to protect unborn babies at 20 weeks\u8212\'20\'14and go on offense to expose their opponents as the true extremists.\par \par \uc2 When Republicans are silent on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , their opponents and the media fill the gaps, often with blatant misinformation. This consensus legislation flips the script, and not a moment too soon. The bill is neither a total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  "ban," as Democrats claim, nor a ceiling that overrides pro-life state efforts to enact stronger protections throughout pregnancy. It would simply apply a minimum level of protection in states such as New York and California to stop inhumane late-term abortions after a point when evidence shows unborn children feel pain.\par \par \uc2 Many Republicans question the timing. But there is never a bad time to take a morally right and politically smart stand. A federal minimum standard is reasonable, necessary and constitutionally sound. And it will yield benefits come Election Day if pro-life Republicans find their voice.\par \par \uc2 Widespread public consensus exists around limiting late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Seventy-two percent of Americans think their state should limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point before 15 weeks, including 75% of women, 70% of independents and 60% of Democrats, according to a June Harvard-Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://harvardharrispoll.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/HHP_June2022_KeyResults.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2 . Only 10% support the near-universal position of the Democratic Party under President Biden, which is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand, paid for by taxpayers, up to the moment of birth. One after another, \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Ryan\uc2 , \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  and other Democratic candidates have refused to name a single limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  they would support.\par \par \uc2 In September, the Trafalgar Group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetrafalgargroup.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/TRF-AbortionLaw-Full-Report-0917.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  that by an 18-point margin, voters prefer a 15-week federal limit (with certain exceptions, including lifesaving emergency care for the mother) to the so-called Women's Health Protection Act, co-sponsored by nearly every House and Senate Democrat, which would impose a "right" to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time for any reason in all 50 states.\par \par \uc2 Georgia gubernatorial candidate \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2  proved how big a liability Democrats' pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremism is when she claimed that an unborn child doesn't have a heartbeat at six weeks and ultrasound technology is part of a vast right-wing conspiracy to control women. What could be more out of touch?\par \par \uc2 Scientists and medical experts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7065984/#:~:text=In the first trimester, pelvic,and other pregnancy-related complications"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirm}}}\uc2  that by six weeks, an unborn child's heart beats at an average rate of 110 beats a minute. By 15 weeks, the child sucks his thumb and feels pain. Yet thanks to permissive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, a new "all-trimester" \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility in Maryland will be allowed to abort children up to 34 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Republicans stand to gain by going on offense. Sen. Graham has provided the winning model: Expose pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Democrats who will stop at nothing to keep U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy on par with China's and North Korea's\u8212\'20\'14including by destroying the filibuster to shut down opposing voices for good; highlight the humanity of the child while showing compassion for mothers; point out how wildly out of step the U.S. is with European nations like France and Germany, which limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 15 weeks; and make it plain that more than 55,000 unborn children a year face an excruciating death after 15 weeks if federal leaders don't act.\par \par \uc2 This debate is Republicans' to lose. They must take charge of the narrative if they don't want to wake up on Nov. 9 wondering why their "red wave" never came ashore. I hope every one heeds the divine encouragement invoked by Mr. Graham in defending the unborn: Be not afraid.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Dannenfelser is president of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-political-case-for-federal-abortion-limits-lindsey-graham-15-weeks-dobbs-midterms-november-gop-11665071968"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Political Case for Federal \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Limits}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020221006eia60086h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
