\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights Shouldn't Be Promoted on Campus, University of Idaho Warns Staff; Vague law leads to conservative guidance also limiting contraception offerings and accusations the school is violating free speech\b0\par\par\uc2 By Douglas Belkin and Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 801 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 September 2022\par 20:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The University of Idaho is advising its employees to limit contraception offerings to students and refrain from promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on campus, to avoid running afoul of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws that the school's top lawyer has called exceedingly vague.\par \par \uc2 The blanket warning from the school's general counsel has led to criticism from national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights activists and even generated reaction from the White House, underscoring the legal and political tensions that have emerged since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court reversed Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  this summer.\par \par \uc2 At issue in Idaho are three laws, two recently enacted by state legislators and one from 1972. Since August, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/justice-department-files-lawsuit-challenging-idaho-abortion-law-11659463607"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly all abortions have been banned in the state }}}\uc2 , with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-must-allow-abortions-in-certain-emergencies-judge-rules-11661386919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exceptions for cases of rape, incest or medical emergencies }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The 1972 law prohibits advertising or promoting services for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or for the prevention of conception, which has in turn led the university to advise employees to limit when they offer students contraception.\par \par \uc2 "In this new and evolving legal landscape, how these laws will be enforced remains unclear," the University of Idaho's general counsel wrote in a seven-page memo addressed to employees last week in which he described one of the laws as "not a model of clarity."\par \par \uc2 "Accordingly, the university and its employees should be aware of the potential risks and penalties associated with conduct that may be perceived to violate the laws," the general counsel wrote in the memo.\par \par \uc2 The memo says condoms may be given out on campus to prevent sexually transmitted diseases but not as contraception and that teachers must remain neutral in classroom discussions about topics related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Employees who violate the laws could face misdemeanor or felony charges and loss of employment, the memo said. The laws affect all public universities in Idaho, including Boise State.\par \par \uc2 Dorothy Moon, chairwoman of the Idaho Republican Party, said in an email that the 1972 law has an exception that allows health professionals to distribute birth control, including condoms. "If a public university has licensed medical professionals, for example at the university health center, then those individuals can responsibly distribute birth control," she said. But a law passed last year meanwhile prohibits public employees from promoting or counseling in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Ms. Moon said. "The bill's intention was simple: to remove the state, including its publicly funded universities, from advocating for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than a dozen states are enforcing bans }}}\uc2  on many or most abortions, but under virtually all of these laws contraception generally remains legal. State \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans also typically don't explicitly prohibit medical providers, counselors, clergy and others from discussing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2 , a state policy analyst at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , which supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said the university is "taking an extremely conservative approach to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in Idaho." But she said the incident reflects the current confusion in many states. "What we're seeing is the chilling effect that comes from these \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that has organizations nervous about what services and information they can provide," Ms. Nash said.\par \par \uc2 The University of Idaho memo says professors may continue to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception in class as long it is relevant to the class and they remain neutral.\par \par \uc2 "We support our students and employees, as well as academic freedom, but understand the need to work within the laws set out by our state," said Jodi Walker, the university's executive director of communications.\par \par \uc2 In an email Wednesday Ms. Walker said the school has long given out condoms and continues to do so.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  tweeted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1574831638575517699?ref_src=twsrc^tfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement condemning the memo }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "To be clear, nothing under Idaho law justifies the university's decision to deny students access to contraception. But the situation in Idaho speaks to the unacceptable consequences of extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans," she wrote. "The overwhelming majority of Americans believe in the right to birth control, as well as the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , without government interference."\par \par \uc2 Adam Steinbaugh, an attorney for the Foundation for Individual Rights and Expression, a nonprofit group that advocates for free speech on college campuses, said the school's guidance directing faculty to limit discussion of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  violates the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 "Faculty members don't shed their First Amendment rights at the classroom door," Mr. Steinbaugh said on the organization's website. "It isn't just misguided to keep faculty from speaking freely\u8212\'20\'14it's illegal."\par \par \uc2 Write to Douglas Belkin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:doug.belkin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doug.belkin@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/university-of-idaho-warns-staff-on-promotion-of-birth-control-abortion-11664469319"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights Shouldn't Be Promoted on Campus, University of Idaho Warns Staff }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220929ei9t0058x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
