\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Policy Angers GOP as Democrats Urge More Action; Administration is constrained by limits on how federal funding can be used, risk of court challenges\b0\par\par\uc2 By Stephanie Armour \par \uc2 1,031 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 September 2022\par 01:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Three months after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , the Biden administration has made a series of moves aimed at protecting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has angered opponents of legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and left supporters urging the federal government to do more.\par \par \uc2 Republicans and some other critics say the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 's actions\u8212\'20\'14such as directing doctors to provide abortions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hospitals-must-provide-abortions-in-emergency-situations-biden-administration-says-11657569637"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when needed in emergency situations }}}\uc2  and telling pharmacists not to deny access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-an-abortion-pill-leaked-supreme-court-decision-11651775689"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  medications }}}\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14have gone too far and will require healthcare providers to potentially violate their own moral or religious beliefs.\par \par \uc2 The initiatives stem from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-sign-order-stepping-up-efforts-to-protect-access-to-reproductive-care-11657278000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two executive orders }}}\uc2  President Biden signed in July and August instructing \uc2 HHS\uc2  to take actions to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Some measures have faced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-sues-biden-administration-over-abortion-medical-emergency-guidelines-11657836049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal challenges from states }}}\uc2  that say they go beyond what is allowed under federal law, and GOP lawmakers have proposed legislation to block department guidance.\par \par \uc2 "The president's radically aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda undermines the law," said Sen. Roger Marshall (R., Kan.).\par \par \uc2 Many Democrats, meanwhile, have praised the administration's actions after the high court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminated the constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . But they want the federal government to do more, including stronger steps to bar doctors from sharing patients' \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  information with law enforcement, which they fear could lead to prosecutions of women who have abortions.\par \par \uc2 The two parties are clashing over a patchwork of state laws and federal guidelines in a charged political environment heading into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-to-know-about-midterm-elections-why-they-are-important-11663359723"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the midterm elections }}}\uc2 , when the ability {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democratic-midterm-prospects-improve-as-races-heat-up-wsj-poll-finds-11662024601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to obtain an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  is expected to be a pivotal issue. The Biden administration, meanwhile, is constrained in what it can do because of limits on how federal funding can be used and the risk of more court challenges.\par \par \uc2 "Steps that push the limits of federal powers could be temporarily satisfying to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters, but a hollow victory if the conservative Supreme Court ends up overturning them," said Larry Levitt, executive vice president for health policy at the \uc2 Kaiser Family Foundation\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sarah Lovenheim, assistant secretary for public affairs at Health and Human Services, said: "\uc2 HHS\uc2  is committed to doing everything we can to protect access to health care. This includes \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, including birth control, emergency medical care and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 White House officials said the president's executive orders have led to many actions that will allow women across the country to access contraception and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Voter support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access has increased following the Supreme Court decision, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-legalized-abortion-grows-since-dobbs-ruling-wsj-poll-shows-11662210020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Wall Street Journal poll }}}\uc2  in August found. Sixty percent of voters said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases, up from 55% in March. Twenty-nine percent said it should be illegal, except in cases of rape, incest and when the woman's life is endangered, compared with 30% in March.\par \par \uc2 Following the court's Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization decision, some states already have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-can-enforce-near-total-abortion-ban-blocked-for-50-years-judge-rules-11663976573"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans }}}\uc2  in effect, while 16 states and Washington, D.C., have established {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protections for legalized \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some GOP state lawmakers have expressed support for legislation that would seek to bar women from traveling across state lines for abortions, but no such bill has been passed.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 HHS\uc2  proposals that stem from the executive orders have drawn both support and criticism.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  issued a proposed rule in July saying that provisions in the Affordable Care Act barring discrimination based on sex also prevent discrimination based on pregnancy or \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Republican lawmakers say the proposal could force Catholic hospitals that oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to perform them.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  also issued guidance in July saying providers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hospitals-must-provide-abortions-in-emergency-situations-biden-administration-says-11657569637"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 must include \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  services }}}\uc2  if necessary in emergency medical situations. A federal judge in Texas in August blocked that guidance from applying in the state, saying that Texas law already allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in life-threatening conditions and that \uc2 HHS\uc2  issued its guidance without a required public-comment period.\par \par \uc2 The department issued guidance in July to roughly 60,000 pharmacies telling them not to deny access to prescription \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or contraceptive medication. The \uc2 American Pharmacists Association\uc2  denounced the guidance, saying it undermines the professional judgment of pharmacists.\par \par \uc2 A bill introduced in September and co-sponsored by 26 House Republicans would grant pharmacists the ability to refuse to provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medications, though it is unlikely to pass the Democratic-led House.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  also invited states to work with it on waivers, which let states test out new approaches for delivering Medicaid care. Those waivers would allow people who are enrolled in Medicaid to travel across state lines to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Republicans say any Medicaid waivers would run afoul of the Hyde Amendment, which bars the use of federal funds to pay for most abortions. Some advocates of legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  say funding could be used to pay for travel or other related expenses.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Is the Biden administration doing too much, too little or the right amount to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Some Democrats and advocates of legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  want the federal government to do more to make the ability to terminate a pregnancy more accessible.\par \par \uc2 HHS\uc2  issued guidance clarifying that, under federal law, disclosing patient data to law-enforcement officials is permitted only in narrow circumstances. But a group of Democratic lawmakers led by Sen. \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2  (D., Wash.) wants \uc2 HHS\uc2  to bar doctors from sharing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or other reproductive information with law enforcement or in legal proceedings over accessing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the patient consents.\par \par \uc2 Some Democratic senators also have pushed for assessing whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics can operate on federal lands. The National Park Service and Bureau of Land Management, for instance, administer public lands in states that have strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. The push has faced White House opposition. The administration said it has reviewed the idea of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on federal lands but has been concerned it could create a dangerous environment for providers and patients as they leave.\par \par \uc2 Write to Stephanie Armour at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:stephanie.armour@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stephanie.armour@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-abortion-policy-angers-gop-as-democrats-urge-more-action-11664026713"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Policy Angers GOP as Democrats Urge More Action  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220924ei9o001md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
