\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  Bets on Infrastructure to Keep Alaska Senate Seat, Deny Trump Revenge; Former president vowed to bring incumbent GOP lawmaker down and endorsed GOP rival \uc2 Kelly Tshibaka\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lindsay Wise \par \uc2 1,782 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2022\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NOME, Alaska\u8212\'20\'14To former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Sen. \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  is a turncoat RINO\u8212\'20\'14"Republican in Name Only"\u8212\'20\'14who so infuriated him that he vowed to campaign for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gop-sen-murkowski-unsure-if-she-will-support-trump-in-november-11591299447"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anyone with a pulse }}}\uc2  who could defeat her.\par \par \uc2 To the mayor of Nome, John Handeland, Ms. Murkowski is a powerful ally in Washington with the pull to funnel $250 million in federal funds for an expansion of his city's port, 200 miles south of the Arctic Circle. The long-sought project will make Nome home to the remote region's lone deep-draft port and enable it to shelter ships during fierce storms such as one earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 "I mean, whether it's right to call Lisa a RINO or not, I don't give a damn," Mr. Handeland said. "She does a good job for me."\par \par \uc2 The competing views of Ms. Murkowski lie at the heart of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/sarah-palin-advances-in-alaska-house-race-11660724298"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alaska's Senate race }}}\uc2 , which pits the centrist Republican against Trump-endorsed challenger \uc2 Kelly Tshibaka\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The state Republican Party and Mr. Trump backed Ms. Tshibaka after what they see as a series of betrayals by Ms. Murkowski, most notably by joining Democrats in trying unsuccessfully to convict Mr. Trump of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/jan-6-committee-hearing-to-focus-on-trumps-actions-during-attack-on-capitol-11658395800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inciting insurrection }}}\uc2  in early 2021, when he was impeached for a second time. To win, Ms. Murkowski will need to convince a broad coalition of Alaskans that her power to deliver for them outweighs ideological differences.\par \par \uc2 "We are a young state, a new state, still," said Ms. Murkowski, 65, who was born when Alaska was still a territory. "We're not connected with our roads. We're not connected with our coastal communities. We lack broadband." Given the infrastructure needs, she said in an interview, her Capitol Hill experience and relationships are critical. "Alaskans have come to understand the value of seniority," she said.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Tshibaka, 43, said Ms. Murkowski squanders that seniority. "She's used those 21 years to become a complete D.C. insider, and she's doing the work of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ," Ms. Tshibaka said in an interview.\par \par \uc2 When Mr. Trump endorsed her in June 2021, he said Ms. Tshibaka is a fighter who is "MAGA all the way." This summer, he flew to Alaska to rally Republicans to support her and former vice presidential nominee and onetime Gov. \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2 , who is running for the state's House seat.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Tshibaka worked in federal watchdog agencies in Washington, D.C., before becoming commissioner of an Alaska department that provides administrative services to state agencies. She cheered the Supreme Court ruling in June that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended a federal right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . Ms. Tshibaka has emphasized voter-fraud concern, and back in November 2020, called for a "prudent pause in declaring a winner" of the presidential election to sort out now-discredited claims of irregularities promoted by Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Murkowski has angered many state Republicans with her vote against repealing the Affordable Care Act in 2017, her support for codifying federal rights to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and same-sex marriage and more recently her votes to confirm Biden nominees \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2  for Interior Secretary and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-set-to-confirm-ketanji-brown-jackson-to-supreme-court-11649329202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Ketanji Brown Jackson }}}\uc2  for the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 At a \uc2 Walmart\uc2  store in Anchorage, retired bookkeeper Mary Allen, 74, said that Alaskans need new blood and that she will vote for Ms. Tshibaka.\par \par \uc2 "I am so tired of Lisa leaning toward the left for so long, baby killing and all of that," Ms. Allen said, referring to Ms. Murkowski's stance in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The senator's vote to convict Mr. Trump also turned her off, she said, reinforcing her belief that Ms. Murkowski isn't really a Republican. Maybe "a very liberal independent," she said.\par \par \uc2 Kelly Smith, 44, of Eagle River, said Ms. Murkowski is his top choice, especially after the Supreme Court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling. Polls show a majority of Alaskans believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal most or all of the time.\par \par \uc2 "She does a good job of representing women, even though it might go against what the conservative platform is, and I think that's really important," said Mr. Smith, a registered Democrat who works in finance. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw584\pich480\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal8760\pichgoal7200
