\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  at a campaign meet-and-greet event in downtown Anchorage, Alaska. PHOTO: Ash Adams for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Months later, Ms. Murkowski was one of seven Republicans who voted to convict Mr. Trump in his second impeachment trial. She is the only one of those seven running for re-election this year.\par \par \uc2 Today, Ms. Murkowski rarely brings up Mr. Trump. Asked whether she would ever consider leaving the Republican Party if she felt it was too closely aligned with him, Ms. Murkowski replied that she identifies with GOP values such as small government and strong defense, but that the party "is going to have to figure out where they are right now."\par \par \uc2 She added: "I just want to make sure that our party doesn't become a party of an individual."\par \par \uc2 Ms. Murkowski has a large fundraising advantage\u8212\'20\'14she has reported $9.4 million in donations compared with Ms. Tshibaka's $3.3 million\u8212\'20\'14and the senator's supporters say she has already demonstrated that she can survive without the GOP. After narrowly losing a primary to conservative Republican Joe Miller in 2010, Ms. Murkowski launched a successful write-in campaign that involved teaching voters to spell her name correctly.\par \par \uc2 Working to Ms. Murkowski's advantage this time is the state's new nonpartisan primary and ranked-choice general-election system. In Alaska, most voters aren't affiliated with any major party. Registered Republicans make up about 24% of the electorate, and about 13% are Democrats.\par \par \uc2 In the August primary, Ms. Murkowski advanced as one of four finalists. In November's general election, voters will rank those four in order of preference. If no candidate wins 50% of the first-choice votes, the weakest candidate is eliminated and the second-choice votes on those ballots are distributed to the remaining candidates. The process is repeated as necessary until one candidate gets a majority. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw584\pich480\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal8760\pichgoal7200
