\par \par \uc2 Kelly Tshibaka\uc2 , wearing a blue jacket at the state fair, says she would have voted against the infrastructure bill. PHOTO: Photo: Ash Adams for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Ms. Murkowski won 45% of the primary vote to Ms. Tshibaka's 38.6%, followed by Democrat Pat Chesbro at 6.8%, and Republican Buzz Kelley with 2.1%. Mr. Kelley has endorsed Ms. Tshibaka.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Tshibaka said Ms. Murkowski is vulnerable in a state Mr. Trump won by 10 percentage points two years ago. She adds that turnout will be higher in November and cites an internal poll that shows the race to be very close.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Is there a place in the Senate for a Republican with an independent streak? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Election watchers said Ms. Murkowski, who has never won a majority in her prior Senate victories, will need a significant number of Democrats to rank her at least second in order to pass the 50% mark for victory.\par \par \uc2 At the Alaska state fair in Palmer, retired healthcare worker Valerie Mittelstead, 69, was tending to the Democrats' booth. While she is no fan of Ms. Murkowski, she is alarmed by Ms. Tshibaka, who she said is too extreme.\par \par \uc2 She said she might put the senator on her ballot, after Ms. Chesbro, the Democrat.\par \par \uc2 "To tell you the truth, I've never voted for a Republican," Ms. Mittelstead said. "And I'm going to have to hold my nose to put her second."\par \par \uc2 Write to Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lisa-murkowski-bets-on-infrastructure-to-keep-alaska-senate-seat-deny-trump-revenge-11663992297"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lisa Murkowski Bets on Infrastructure to Keep Alaska Senate Seat, Deny Trump Revenge }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220924ei9o000xe\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngbl