\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 GOP House Leader Kevin McCarthy Rolls Out 'Commitment to America' for Midterms; Plan criticizes Democrats' move to expand IRS, emphasizes cutting crime, lowering prices\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalie Andrews \par \uc2 1,201 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 September 2022\par 18:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MONONGAHELA, Pa.\u8212\'20\'14House Minority Leader Kevin McCarthy (R., Calif.) laid out his vision for the Republicans if they win control of the House in the midterms, targeting Democrats' plans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-80-billion-more-for-the-irs-means-for-your-taxes-11660901409"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to expand the Internal Revenue Service }}}\uc2 while also emphasizing cutting crime, lowering prices and giving parents more influence over their schools.\par \par \uc2 "On that very first bill, we're going to repeal 87,000 IRS agents. Our job is to work for you, not go after you," said Mr. McCarthy, who is the favorite to become the House speaker if his party captures the majority.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you think Republicans will fare in this year's midterms? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Republicans need just a handful of seat pickups to take over the House, which Democrats now control 221-212 with two vacancies. Democrats' hopes have been buoyed by recent special election wins in New York and Alaska, but election analysts say Republicans remain the favorites to win control. The Senate, currently split 50-50, remains a tossup.\par \par \uc2 Mr. McCarthy, who was accompanied by other party leaders as well as far-right members Reps. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  of Georgia and Burgess Owens of Utah, traveled Friday to Monongahela, a small, working class community near Pittsburgh, to formally present his Commitment to America plan. Republicans walked onstage to country music star \uc2 Toby Keith\uc2 's "Made In America."\par \par \uc2 In an effort to get the often-unruly caucus on board with the agenda, Mr. McCarthy delegated parts of the plan to top Republicans. Unlike past GOP speakers including \uc2 Paul Ryan\uc2 , Mr. McCarthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kevin-mccarthy-republican-house-speaker-midterm-elections-11662505517"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has avoided being personally identified }}}\uc2  with any particular policy or ideological wing of the party. He also has remained close to former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Republicans' effort evokes former GOP leader Newt Gingrich's Contract With America, which helped the party win the House majority in 1994 for the first time in 40 years. That plan included provisions on balancing the budget, cutting cash welfare and cracking down on crime.\par \par \uc2 "I believe we have a lot to run against\u8230\'20\'26but if you want to drive up more votes, you have to stand for something too," said Rep. \uc2 Don Bacon\uc2  (R., Neb.), who is defending a competitive seat. "So I think you need both. You need a left hook and a right hook."\par \par \uc2 Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) has opted to not unveil a policy plan as he works to win the majority in his chamber. Sen. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  (R., Fla.), who is leading the Senate Republican campaign efforts, released a plan earlier this year that called for tax increases on some Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/rick-scott-revises-tax-increase-proposal-after-facing-criticism-11654786802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 before revising it to be less specific }}}\uc2 ; he would also require Congress to periodically review all government programs, a category that would include Social Security. Other Republicans panned Mr. Scott's proposal.\par \par \uc2 The House GOP commitment has four main themes: building a strong economy focused on fighting inflation and curbing costs; a safe nation which focuses on reducing crime and securing the border; a freedom-themed category related to schools and confronting big tech; and a focus on accountable government, a nod to planned scrutiny of Biden administration officials.\par \par \uc2 If Republicans do win control of the House, they will have the power to hold hearings and propose and pass legislation, but their ability to make new law will be limited\u8212\'20\'14even if the party also takes the Senate. President Biden can veto bills, and many policies related to crime as well as school curriculum and transgender issues are controlled at the state or local level. Still, the plan served to stake out what the party considers key pitches to win over voters in November.\par \par \uc2 Republicans said they want to provide incentives for hiring 200,000 more police officers in the country to lower crime rates, as well as cut government spending to rein in inflation. The GOP also plans to "protect the lives of unborn children and their mothers," a reference to the party's antiabortion stance. Many GOP lawmakers have signed onto a proposed 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, though it wasn't discussed at the event.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court ended the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in a ruling earlier this year, leaving the matter to the states, some of which quickly passed bill to restrict or protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Democrats have pushed to reinstate broader rights to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Republicans have backed more limited access or an outright ban.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) called the GOP plan an "alarming new extreme MAGA platform," citing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance and other parts of the proposal. Headed into the midterms, Democrats have worked to tie Republicans to Mr. Trump and his "Make America Great Again" slogan.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden, in a speech Friday at a \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  event, called Mr. McCarthy's plan a "thin series of policy goals with little or no detail."\par \par \uc2 He challenged Mr. McCarthy's argument that Republicans would keep the country safe, citing their opposition to his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-set-to-approve-covid-19-relief-bill-11615372203"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1.9 trillion American Rescue Plan }}}\uc2 , which provided money to cities and states for public safety. He also highlighted that most Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-expected-to-approve-landmark-gun-legislation-11656087915"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted against a recently passed gun law }}}\uc2  that had bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 The climate, healthcare and tax law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/joe-biden-to-sign-bill-aimed-at-lowering-drug-costs-boosting-renewable-energy-11660642202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed by Mr. Biden last month }}}\uc2 , known as the Inflation Reduction Act, include efforts to lower prescription-drug prices. It also provided $80 billion to the \uc2 IRS\uc2  for a decadelong transformation and expansion of tax enforcement, and the administration said last year that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/irs-faces-tight-job-market-and-competition-for-talent-as-it-recruits-thousands-11663407003"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could include hiring 87,000 new employees }}}\uc2 . Some would be agents and auditors to crack down on tax dodging; some would answer phones or rebuild aging computer systems to clear up long-running customer-service problems.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have defended the spending as necessary to step up tax enforcement. They have emphasized that the money would reduce the budget deficit and police tax cheating by high-income households and corporations. Republicans have warned that the new agents would unfairly pursue small-business owners, and some have urged the administration to emphasize taxpayer service, privacy protections and computer improvements.\par \par \uc2 In comments Friday, GOP lawmakers also highlighted investigating the origins of Covid-19, as well as holding oversight hearings on many of Mr. Biden's cabinet secretaries, including the head of the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  Alejandro Mayorkas, over what Republicans call lax U.S. border policy.\par \par \uc2 "We will give Secretary Mayorkas a reserved parking spot, he will be testifying so much about this," said House Republican Whip Steve Scalise (R., La.).\par \par \uc2 Monongahela has been shrinking for decades, as factories closed. The area consistently voted for Democrats until 2008 and now favors Republicans.\par \par \uc2 "In a lot of ways, the Democrat party left these voters," said Rep. \uc2 Guy Reschenthaler\uc2 , the Republican who represents the area. He helped write the China part of the Commitment to America agenda that calls for a select committee to look at Beijing's business practices, and looks at ways to keep businesses in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Catherine Lucey contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Natalie Andrews at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:natalie.andrews@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 natalie.andrews@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220923ei9n004s9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
