\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Indiana Near-Total  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban Temporarily Blocked by Judge; Judge issues preliminary injunction on new law, which went into effect last week\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 804 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par 17:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 An Indiana judge temporarily blocked enforcement of the state's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/indiana-legislature-is-first-to-approve-abortion-bans-since-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-11659755538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  a week after it took effect, allowing clinics to resume the procedure as litigation over the new law continues.\par \par \uc2 Judge Kelsey Hanlon, a special judge in the Monroe County Circuit Court, issued a preliminary injunction Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "There is reasonable likelihood that this significant restriction of personal autonomy offends the liberty guarantees of the Indiana Constitution," Judge Hanlon wrote in the order.\par \par \uc2 Indiana's Republican-led legislature was the first to pass a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  in June. The law banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout pregnancy with exceptions in some cases of rape and incest, fatal fetal anomalies and emergencies that threaten the life or physical health of the pregnant woman. It took effect Sept. 15.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers representing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the state including Planned Parenthood and Whole Woman's Health filed a lawsuit against the near-total ban in August, arguing the new law violated the right to privacy and equal privileges protections under the Indiana Constitution.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Is Legal and Where It Loses Protections Without Roe v. Wade }}}\par \par \uc2 "We knew this ban would cause irreparable harm to Hoosiers, and in just a single week, it has done just that," the group of providers said in a statement after the judge's decision.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Planned Parenthood said they aim to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  appointments as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 Indiana Attorney General \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2 , a Republican, said he planned to appeal the decision.\par \par \uc2 "Our office remains determined to fight for the lives of the unborn, and this law provides a reasonable way to begin doing that," Mr. Rokita said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Indiana Gov. \uc2 Eric Holcomb\uc2 , a Republican, signed the law shortly after it passed in the legislature Aug. 5. Erin Murphy, his press secretary, on Thursday said laws with significant policy changes often face legal challenges and Mr. Holcomb and his office "will closely follow this court case as it unfolds."\par \par \uc2 About a dozen states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enforced bans or narrow restrictions on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  since the Supreme Court ended federal protections for the procedure, creating a patchwork of access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the nation. Since the June decision, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates have sought to block these laws {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lawsuits-to-test-whether-state-constitutions-protect-abortion-rights-11657375200"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 citing provisions in state constitutions }}}\uc2  they argue protect the right to the procedure. Judges in Ohio and South Carolina have temporarily blocked those states' bans on most abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers representing Indiana \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers argued the state law would cause irreparable harm to Hoosiers\u8212\'20\'14a legal standard that typically must be met for a judge to issue a preliminary injunction. In their complaint, providers said the ban could place substantial economic and health consequences on pregnant Hoosiers, most of whom would no longer have the option to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 The state attorney general's office said in court filings that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers failed to prove the law would cause irreparable harm. An injunction, the office said, would instead inflict such harm on "thousands of unborn Hoosiers and the public."\par \par \uc2 The office also argued the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't protected under the state constitution. "The constitutional text nowhere mentions \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," it said.\par \par \uc2 Judge Hanlon wrote in her order the potential harm caused by the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law outweighed any brought by an injunction temporarily blocking its enforcement.\par \par \uc2 Debate in the Indiana legislature over the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban was at times heated\u8212\'20\'14including shouting matches between senators on the floor\u8212\'20\'14as lawmakers weighed dozens of proposed amendments. The bill initially faced opposition from antiabortion groups and many GOP legislators, who said it didn't go far enough. Some Republicans sought to find a compromise with Democratic lawmakers who opposed the near-total ban. They pitched a ban on most abortions after 13 weeks of pregnancy, which was eventually rejected.\par \par \uc2 After the legislation passed, Indiana-based companies \uc2 Eli Lilly & Co\uc2 . and \uc2 Cummins Inc\uc2 . criticized the law, voicing concern it would affect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/eli-lilly-speaks-out-against-indianas-ban-on-most-abortions-11659813615"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their ability to recruit and maintain employees }}}\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Other Republican-led state legislatures that sought to quickly pass new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions after the Supreme Court's decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-abortion-bans-face-obstacles-as-republicans-clash-11660908536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have also faced hurdles }}}\uc2 . Disagreements over details of the bills have split Republicans in legislatures in West Virginia and South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 West Virginia lawmakers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/west-virginia-passes-near-total-abortion-ban-11663107167"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a near-total ban on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  last week after a weekslong pause due to disputes over some provisions. Lawmakers in South Carolina, who have been debating and modifying newly proposed restrictions for weeks, are set to reconvene next week to consider their latest version.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220922ei9m003s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
