\par \par \uc2 Riders in a Kansas City parade on Sep. 3. PHOTO: Chase Castor for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 The ability of Kansas to defy stereotypes was at play in the high-profile campaign and vote on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum, a somewhat confusing ballot initiative in which a vote against the measure was a vote for upholding a state supreme court decision that found the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution. Turnout for the vote was enormous\u8212\'20\'14more than 900,000 votes, nearly double the turnout in the last midterm primary. More than 180,000 more voters cast ballots on the referendum than voted in the two parties' gubernatorial primaries, suggesting a surge of unaffiliated voters showed up solely to vote on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  question.\par \par \uc2 Those who worked on both sides of the referendum tend to agree that the outcome wasn't a statement that voters wanted to significantly liberalize the state's current \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, in which the procedure is legal but late-term abortions are prohibited and restrictions such as parental notification are in place. Rather, it was largely a vote to retain a middle-ground position.\par \par \uc2 More than that, people in both parties agree, it was a vote against turning over such a highly personal and emotional matter to a state legislature that might have moved further toward an outright ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  than many voters wanted. "Now you have this situation where the large majority of people in Kansas, I think, have a nuanced position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jim Slattery, a moderate Democrat who represented Kansas in Congress for 12 years.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Pahls, the Republican consultant, said simply: "The prevailing message was, 'Maintain the status quo.'" Ironically, Republicans say, the onus now has shifted to Kansas Democrats to show that they will not use the August vote to push for liberalizing state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law by bringing court cases designed to erode current restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  vote also affirmed, once again, the power of women. Women were particularly motivated to both campaign and vote on the referendum on both sides, but particularly on the pro-choice side. Catalist, a Democratic analytical firm, calculated that the share of new Kansas voter registrants who were women began rising immediately after the draft Supreme Court decision overturning the Roe v. Wade decision was leaked in May, and then spiked to about 70% of new registrants after the Court's final decision was issued in late June.\par \par \uc2 That finding also has national implications. Catalist said it has seen similar registration spikes in a series of swing states this year.\par \par \uc2 More broadly, the August vote, in which Kansans showed up for a primary election on a hot summer day in numbers of the kind normally seen in a presidential election in November, may send what everybody on all sides can see as a positive signal. "If the voters are given a shot at making decisions that are important to them, not only will they show up, but they will show up in record numbers," said former Gov. Sebelius. "People are eager to have their voices heard."\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald F. Seib at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jerry.seib@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jerry.seib@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Mr. Seib retired in May as the Journal's executive Washington editor and weekly Capital Journal columnist. He is a fellow this fall at the Robert J. Dole Institute of Politics at the \uc2 University of Kansas\uc2 , his alma mater.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-finds-a-path-beyond-partisanship-11663253693"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas Finds a Path Beyond Partisanship }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220915ei9f003e9\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
