\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Senate Midterm Map Shaped by  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  and the Economy; Election analysts see a tight contest for control of the chamber, currently split 50-50\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lindsay Wise and John McCormick \par \uc2 1,510 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par 14:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Democrats' prospects for holding the Senate have brightened in the months since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended the federal right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , but election watchers say Republicans still have an even chance of recapturing the majority as candidates enter the final weeks of campaigning.\par \par \uc2 With New Hampshire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-hampshire-gop-senate-primary-pits-establishment-candidate-against-outsider-11663070403"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrapping up its primaries }}}\uc2  on Tuesday, the contenders for all Senate battlefields now are set. In the 50-50 Senate where about a third of the chamber is up for re-election, Republicans are defending 21 seats, while Democrats are defending 14. A dozen are competitive, with particularly hard-fought contests unfolding in Arizona, Georgia, Nevada, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/republicans-mount-rescue-effort-in-pennsylvania-for-mastriano-oz-campaigns-11662131864"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania }}}\uc2  and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The November midterms {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/climate-bill-draws-clear-battle-lines-for-midterms-11660222802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will serve as a referendum }}}\uc2  on the first two years of President Biden's term, and the results will shape the prospects for legislation and the president's nominees. Aside from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, voters are grappling with rising prices and broader economic worries as well as concerns about crime. The races will also test the power of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to get his handpicked candidates elected and voters' appetite for his brand of Republican politics.\par \par \uc2 Democrats' top pickup opportunities are in Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, both states Mr. Biden won in 2020. The party also sees opportunities to expand its offensive map to include North Carolina, Ohio and Florida\u8212\'20\'14states that voted for Mr. Trump two years ago.\par \par \uc2 For Republicans, Democratic-held seats in Nevada and Georgia are the main targets, followed by New Hampshire. In that state, nonpartisan political observers view the primary win by Don Bolduc, a retired Army general, over a more establishment candidate, Chuck Morse, as hurting the GOP's odds of unseating Democratic Sen. \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  in November.\par \par \uc2 The Republican Party's hope of flipping Arizona from blue to red also appears to be in jeopardy, as Democratic Sen. Mark Kelly, a former astronaut with a fundraising advantage in the tens of millions of dollars, hits Trump-endorsed businessman \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2  with negative ads characterizing him as an extremist on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other issues. Polls show Mr. Kelly with a 7.3 percentage point lead, on average, as of Sept. 13, according to aggregator FiveThirtyEight.\par \par \uc2 Zachery Henry, a spokesman for the Masters campaign, pointed to recent polling from Emerson College that showed Mr. Masters narrowing the gap with Mr. Kelly. Anyone saying Mr. Masters is going to lose is "certainly not plugged into Arizona politics," Mr. Henry said.\par \par \uc2 The party out of power historically has an advantage in picking up seats in the midterms, and Democrats have been weighed down by Mr. Biden's weak approval numbers, which have rebounded from their lowest point but remain underwater. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democratic-midterm-prospects-improve-as-races-heat-up-wsj-poll-finds-11662024601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In the latest Wall Street Journal poll }}}\uc2 , the president's job approval stood at 45%, up from 42% in March, while 54% disapprove.\par \par \uc2 Political analysts ratcheted back their expectations of GOP wins in the House and Senate after the Supreme Court's decision this summer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-the-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-and-abortion-rights-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to overturn Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The nonpartisan Inside Elections, which analyzes campaigns, had projected in April that Republicans would gain one to three seats in the Senate. Now the publication's prediction is that Democrats will gain one seat, or Republicans gain one seat\u8212\'20\'14or there will be no net change and the Senate remains evenly divided.\par \par \uc2 "I started out skeptical that news events are political game-changers. I think that it's rare," said Inside Elections editor and publisher Nathan Gonzales. But he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision "brought Democratic enthusiasm up to parity with Republican enthusiasm, and that limits Republican opportunities," particularly in Democratic-held states such as Colorado and Washington, where Republicans were hoping to flip seats.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think the Republicans will win control of the Senate in November? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Gary Peters\uc2  of Michigan, chairman of Senate Democrats' campaign arm, said in an interview that his party is making the case that Republican candidates are too extreme to appeal to general election voters, especially when it comes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas voters' rejection last month }}}\uc2  of a state constitutional amendment that would have removed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections demonstrated how motivating the issue can be, he added.\par \par \uc2 "It's a real wake-up call for folks as to how powerful this issue is," Mr. Peters said.\par \par \uc2 He said he feels increasingly good about Democrats' ability to keep control of the Senate but expects the races to be close.\par \par \uc2 Republicans say the midterm elections will be a referendum on Democrats' handling of the economy, crime and immigration. While Democrats are trying to go on offense on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , GOP strategists say, the aftershocks of the court's ruling are fading and the issue won't swing undecided voters.\par \par \uc2 "You can sense the Democrats' desperation to talk about anything but out-of-control inflation, collapsing retirement savings and violent crime, but those visceral fears are now driving voters as the fall elections come into focus," said Steven Law, president of the Senate Leadership Fund, a Republican super PAC allied with Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.).\par \par \uc2 Florida Sen. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , chairman of Senate Republicans' campaign committee, said he is optimistic the GOP could net as many as six seats, winning Nevada, Georgia, Arizona, New Hampshire, Colorado and Washington. He even raised the possibility that Republican Leora Levy, a first-time candidate endorsed by Mr. Trump, potentially could be competitive in deep-blue Connecticut, which analysts see as a solid Democratic hold.\par \par \uc2 "The Biden agenda is really, really unpopular," Mr. Scott said.\par \par \uc2 Hampering Republicans' chances are some first-time candidates endorsed by Mr. Trump\u8212\'20\'14among them celebrity doctor Mehmet Oz in Pennsylvania, author J.D. Vance in Ohio and Mr. Masters in Arizona\u8212\'20\'14who have frustrated some GOP strategists and senators with their weak fundraising and soft poll numbers.\par \par \uc2 Mr. McConnell recently tamped down expectations of a Republican wave, citing "candidate quality" as a factor. He predicted last month that Republicans had a 50-50 chance of winning control.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, most polls show Mr. Oz trailing Democratic Lt. Gov. \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 , who is recovering from a stroke. Mr. Oz has criticized Mr. Fetterman for not debating him, suggesting he might be too sick. Mr. Fetterman has said he would agree to debate Mr. Oz but is seeking accommodations for auditory processing problems related to the stroke.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Peters said Mr. Fetterman is recovering and will continue to campaign. "There is no backup plan whatsoever. That's absolutely not necessary," Mr. Peters said.\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, Democrats are trying again to unseat GOP Sen. Ron Johnson. A poll released Wednesday by the Marquette University Law School showed Mr. Johnson leading by one point among likely voters, within the margin of error.\par \par \uc2 Another close race is between Nevada Democratic Sen. \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  and the state's former GOP attorney general, \uc2 Adam Laxalt\uc2 . The FiveThirtyEight average has Ms. \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2  leading Mr. Laxalt by about 3 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 The two Nevada candidates and their allies have spent more than $11 million already this month on advertising, according to ad-tracking firm AdImpact.\par \par \uc2 Ms. \uc2 Cortez Masto\uc2 's TV ads in recent days have included an emphasis on endorsements she has received from Republicans, part of an apparent effort to woo independent voters. Mr. Laxalt, meanwhile, has been airing spots focused on his law-enforcement credentials, inflation and an ad about ads that accuses his opponent of playing "gutter politics."\par \par \uc2 It's possible that Senate control could again come down to a runoff in Georgia, where Mr. Biden upset Mr. Trump in 2020, and a pair of Democratic victories in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-make-historic-gain-in-georgia-as-senate-control-hangs-in-balance-11609941722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate runoffs in January 2021 }}}\uc2  secured the Senate majority for the party.\par \par \uc2 Polls on average show Republican \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2 , a former football star endorsed by Mr. Trump, neck and neck with incumbent Democratic Sen. \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , a pastor. If neither candidate gets more than 50% of the vote, the runoff will be held on Dec. 6.\par \par \uc2 The race is expected to see the most advertising in a Senate contest this election cycle.\par \par \uc2 One recent ad sponsored by Mr. Warnock features video of Mr. Walker's ex-wife describing how the GOP candidate once "held a gun to my head" and threatened to "blow my brains out."\par \par \uc2 When a similar ad appeared in August using the same video, Mr. Walker responded with a video of his own where he said the interview was being used out of context and that he was glad it was running because it gave him the "opportunity to end the stigma around mental health."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Walker, who like Mr. Warnock is Black, appears in one ad arguing that Democrats too often complain about racism. "Warnock wants to divide us," he says. "I want to bring us together."\par \par \uc2 Write to Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and John McCormick at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:mccormick.john@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mccormick.john@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/senate-midterm-map-shaped-by-abortion-and-the-economy-11663247187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate Midterm Map Shaped by \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  and the Economy  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220915ei9f002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
