\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 West Virginia Passes Near-Total  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; State is second to approve new restrictions after Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 780 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2022\par 22:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 West Virginia lawmakers on Tuesday passed a ban on nearly all abortions, the second state legislature to approve new restrictions since the Supreme Court eliminated the federal constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers in Charleston had earlier encountered disagreements over some provisions and failed to quickly pass a ban after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade  }}}\uc2  this summer. After a weekslong pause, the Republican-controlled state Senate approved the legislation 22-to-7 Tuesday afternoon, with the GOP-led House following in a 77-to-17 vote, as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters protested outside the chambers to voice their opposition.\par \par \uc2 The bill now heads to Republican Gov. \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  , who had called on lawmakers to clarify the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. A representative for the governor didn't immediately respond to a request for comment Tuesday. The legislation would take effect after the governor's signature.\par \par \uc2 About a dozen states have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enforced bans and narrow restrictions on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  since the Supreme Court's Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Center decision in June returned the question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 's legality to states, upending nearly 50 years of precedent. Indiana was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/indiana-legislature-is-first-to-approve-abortion-bans-since-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-11659755538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first state to pass a new ban  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The West Virginia legislation bans nearly all abortions in the state with a few exceptions, including cases of medical emergencies or lethal fetal anomalies. It also includes exceptions for rape and incest within the first eight weeks of pregnancy for adults and within the first 14 weeks for minors and incompetent or incapacitated adults. Adults must first report the sexual assault or incest to a law-enforcement agency and provide that report to the doctor providing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Minors and incompetent or incapacitated adults would either have to report the assault or incest to law enforcement or receive medical treatment for it.\par \par \uc2 The bill stipulates that only licensed medical professionals\u8212\'20\'14doctors of medicine and doctors of osteopathic medicine\u8212\'20\'14can provide abortions under the allowed exceptions. Those doctors who provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under other circumstances could potentially lose their license to practice. Anyone who performs an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and isn't a licensed medical professional, as defined by the law, could face between three and 10 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 Lawmakers had initially moved rapidly to pass a law banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their state, but the House and Senate later paused their efforts because of questions over exceptions for sexual-assault victims and over penalties. Details of the approved near-total ban were hammered out as a compromise.\par \par \uc2 "There are so many variables and factors," Sen. Tom Takubo, a Republican, said Tuesday. "What I do know is that we do have to do something."\par \par \uc2 Democrats criticized the bill, saying the exceptions are illusionary and the new law could chill businesses and keep young people and doctors from moving to or staying in the state.\par \par \uc2 "I am shaken to my core," Delegate Danielle Walker, a Democrat, said before the House vote. "I definitely respect the choices of the Mountaineers that I know are capable of making their decisions on their healthcare."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights protesters disrupted debate in the House ahead of the vote, yelling "shame on you" and "our lives matter."\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans, meanwhile, criticized the bill for not going far enough, because of its inclusion of rape and incest exceptions.\par \par \uc2 West Virginia is one of several states where Republican lawmakers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/state-abortion-bans-face-obstacles-as-republicans-clash-11660908536"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced hurdles passing \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans and restrictions  }}}\uc2  in the wake of the Dobbs decision. In Indiana, legislators' approval of the new near-total ban came after hours of debate and after initial opposition from antiabortion groups and many Republican legislators for not going far enough. Indiana's law is expected to take effect Thursday.\par \par \uc2 South Carolina's Senate failed to pass a proposed near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month as Republicans split over exceptions for rape and incest and other details. The Senate there last week amended the bill to ban nearly all abortions after around six weeks of pregnancy, rather than the near total ban. The House will take up the bill again later this month.\par \par \uc2 In West Virginia, a judge in July temporarily blocked enforcement of the state's 1849 criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8212\'20\'14halting its enforcement following the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  's decision. That allowed the state's only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic to resume scheduling appointments after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-state-abortion-restrictions-at-odds-with-federal-law-11657445400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weeks of confusion  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Days later, Mr. Justice called for a coming special session to "clarify and modernize" the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jennifer.calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jennifer.calfas@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/west-virginia-passes-near-total-abortion-ban-11663107167"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 West Virginia Passes Near-Total \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220913ei9d00669\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
