\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Bill Gets Cold Shoulder From Some Republicans; Supreme Court ruling has made  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  access a top issue in midterm elections\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katy Stech Ferek and Lindsay Wise \par \uc2 990 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2022\par 19:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.) introduced a bill on Tuesday that would ban doctors from performing abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy, putting a brighter spotlight on the contentious issue headed into the November midterms and drawing a chilly reception from some prominent Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Graham called the bill a response to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-set-to-vote-on-bills-protecting-abortion-access-11657896570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bill passed earlier this year by House Democrats }}}\uc2  that would ensure a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through fetal viability, or around 21 to 24 weeks. Neither measure has a chance of passing into law, but Mr. Graham drew a straight line to the election this fall, as Republicans try to take back control of the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 "If we take back the House and the Senate, I can assure you we'll have a vote on the bill," he said. "If the Democrats are in charge I don't know if we'll ever have a vote on our bill."\par \par \uc2 He said Republicans aren't afraid to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that the debate is more likely to hurt Democrats, who he said back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws that are out of step with the country.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access groups denounced the bill, which they called a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and said it helps to show off the parties' differences on the issue.\par \par \uc2 "It's very simple," Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.) said. "You want to protect the right to choose, and you want to protect a woman's right to healthcare? Vote for more Democratic senators."\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court overturned }}}\uc2  precedent establishing the federal right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leaving the matter to the states. That set off a flurry of new laws in states both to protect and restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and has become a central issue in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Other Republicans said they didn't support a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure.\par \par \uc2 "I think most of the members of my conference prefer that this be dealt with at the state level," said Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  (R., Ky.) at a press conference when asked about the Graham bill. Looking toward the midterms, he said: "I will leave it up to our candidates who are quite capable of handling this issue to determine what their response is."\par \par \uc2 Asked if he backed Mr. Graham's proposal, Sen. \uc2 Roy Blunt\uc2  (R., Mo.) said: "I still think the best place to deal with that is at the state level."\par \par \uc2 Any \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill would require 60 votes to advance in the Senate, currently divided 50-50. Mr. McConnell has said he wouldn't eliminate that supermajority requirement if Republicans retake control.\par \par \uc2 The court's ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been seen as favoring Democrats in the midterms. In early tests of how the issues will play out at the ballot box, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-vote-signals-abortion-could-emerge-as-top-political-issue-in-november-11659555741"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters in Kansas rejected }}}\uc2  a measure that would have amended the state's constitution to say it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Democrats also fared better than expected in some special elections, attributed in part to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  politics.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/support-for-legalized-abortion-grows-since-dobbs-ruling-wsj-poll-shows-11662210020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal poll conducted }}}\uc2  in August found that 57% of voters opposed a ban on abortions at 15 weeks that included an exception only for the health of the mother. The survey showed opposition from 38% of Republicans, 55% of independents and 77% of Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Graham said his bill, called Protecting Pain-Capable Unborn Children from Late-Term Abortions Act, wouldn't apply the ban to situations involving rape or incest or when a mother's health is at risk.\par \par \uc2 The timing of the bill's introduction alarmed some Republican strategists, who fretted privately that it would give Democrats a strong talking point heading into November. They were particularly irked that Mr. Graham announced the bill the same day as news broke that inflation pressures remain stubbornly high, potentially overshadowing Republican efforts to focus voters' dissatisfaction with the economy.\par \par \uc2 "Democrats couldn't have asked for better timing," said one GOP strategist working on Senate races. "They started the day hiding from terrible inflation news but they'll end it leaning forward on their favorite topic."\par \par \uc2 Brittany Yanick, a spokeswoman for Pennsylvania Senate candidate Mehmet Oz, said he supports banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with exceptions for saving the life of the mother, rape and incest. Still, he wouldn't want the federal government "involved in interfering with the state's decisions on the topic."\par \par \uc2 Other Republican strategists said that the proposal gave candidates on the campaign trail an opportunity to weigh in on the issue while being able to refocus the debate to core priorities.\par \par \uc2 The proposal "gives Senate candidates a way to talk about a tough issue and go back on offense on inflation, crime and the border," said Kevin Sheridan, a Republican strategist, saying this ban was a safe compromise position.\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 John Thune\uc2  (R., S.D.), the No. 2 Senate Republican, said he would support a 15-week ban and that Mr. Graham's proposal could serve to counter Democrats who claim that all Republicans favor an outright ban on all abortions.\par \par \uc2 "Democrats have tried to convert this into a one-sided argument that represents their singular view of the world, which is that all Republicans are for an outright ban," Mr. Thune said. Mr. Graham's legislation is "an attempt to give Republican candidates, people running for office this year, something to be for that represents a reasonable middle ground," he added.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Thune said Mr. Graham hadn't looped in Senate GOP leadership on his bill introduction plans.\par \par \uc2 Natalie Andrews, Siobhan Hughes and Joshua Jamerson contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Katy Stech Ferek at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:katherine.stech@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 katherine.stech@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Lindsay Wise at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:lindsay.wise@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lindsay.wise@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lindsey-grahams-abortion-bill-gets-cold-shoulder-from-some-republicans-11663098886"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lindsey Graham's \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Bill Gets Cold Shoulder From Some Republicans  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220913ei9d005bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
