\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 's 15-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; It's constitutionally dubious and risks misreading the politics.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 771 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2022\par 22:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats want to make the midterms about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not inflation, and on cue Tuesday Sen. \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  introduced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lgraham.senate.gov/public/_cache/files/3065785d-86b8-4d36-986a-72aa1c8f100c/protecting-pain-capable-unborn-children-from-late-term-abortions-act-.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legislation}}}\uc2  to enact a nationwide ban at 15 weeks of pregnancy. This is constitutionally dubious, and although Mr. Graham is right that Democratic \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  absolutists too often get a pass, he is taking a big political gamble.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsjplus.com/invites/opinion-live-congress-dallas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 WSJ Opinion Live: Can Republicans Retake Congress?}}}\par \par \uc2 Join Journal Editorial Page Editor Paul Gigot and Columnists Kimberley Strassel and Karl Rove live from Dallas as they discuss how inflation, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Supreme Court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling will affect the midterms. What's at stake in the House and Senate? Will the red wave hit as many predict? The panel will break down what the election will mean for the economy, President Biden's legislative agenda, and the run up to the 2024 presidential race.\par \par \uc2 WSJ+ members are invited to attend this exclusive member event live in Dallas, TX, or via livestream online on Monday, October 17 at 7:00 PM CT / 8:00 PM ET. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://events.wsjplus.com/OpinionLiveOct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Purchase}}}\uc2  tickets to the live event in Dallas or to register for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/live-qa/wsj-opinion-live-can-republicans-retake-congress/35FC8ECA-5145-4355-AA65-F235F1F47C30"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 virtual livestream}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As a policy, 15 weeks of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand is about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/europe-abortion-law-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-european-union-leak-alito-dobbs-pro-life-choice-civil-womens-rights-11651757568"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on par with the laws}}}\uc2 in Western Europe. That would continue to permit most of the abortions done in the U.S. In 2019, 92.7% were performed at 13 weeks or before, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/70/ss/ss7009a1.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a study}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2 . That's why Mr. Graham styles his bill a ban on later abortions, which the legislative text describes as procedures that often "involve the use of surgical instruments to crush and tear an unborn child apart."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Graham's bill has exceptions for when the mother's life is in "physical" danger, "not including psychological or emotional conditions." It also includes exemptions for rape victims. Mr. Graham's goal is to draw a line that the GOP can defend to the public. According to the Gallup figures, 67% of Americans want \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be "generally legal" in the first 12 weeks. That {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/393104/pro-choice-identification-rises-near-record-high.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falls to 36%}}}\uc2  in the first 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 But the nuances might be lost on voters, and Democrats are trying to ensure that they are. Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 's statement Tuesday was illustrative. "The nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban proposal put forth today," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.speaker.gov/newsroom/91322-1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she said}}}\uc2 , "is the latest, clearest signal of extreme MAGA Republicans' intent to criminalize women's health freedom in all 50 states and arrest doctors for providing basic care."\par \par \uc2 That's demagogic, but notice how Mrs. Pelosi refers to it as a "nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban," without mentioning anything about 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats' bill in Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/chuck-schumers-radical-abortion-bill-senate-democrats-roe-v-wade-womens-health-protection-act-11652133702"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is far more extreme}}}\uc2 . Their bill would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand through fetal viability, about 23 weeks. After that line, it would also guarantee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access whenever the pregnancy is a risk to the patient's "health," which isn't defined and is often interpreted to include emotional factors. The bill appears to protect sex-selective abortions, if parents who wanted a boy decide they would prefer to terminate a girl.\par \par \uc2 Republicans already had plenty of political ammunition, and signing on to Mr. Graham's bill leaves them open to charges of hypocrisy. After Roe v. Wade, conservatives spent five decades arguing that the Supreme Court had inflamed the country by nationalizing the debate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is properly a state issue. This summer the Justices reversed that mistake in Dobbs, and the result has been hurly-burly democratic arguments in state legislatures.\par \par \uc2 There's no need to re-nationalize the question, and it isn't clear Congress has the authority to do so. Mr. Graham's bill cites the Constitution's Commerce Clause and the Equal Protection Clause as justifications for federal power, but neither is convincing. If Republicans care about originalism, and many of them do, then it's a mistake to start arguing that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations qualify as "commerce."\par \par \uc2 Fighting for policy change in all 50 states is arduous, with victories offset by defeats and unsatisfying compromises. Democrats and some Republicans don't want to bother, since it's easier to pass one bill in Congress, constitutional or not.\par \par \uc2 But by Mr. Graham's political logic, if voters in Colorado, Pennsylvania or Arizona think 15 weeks is too restrictive, they now have a reason to vote against those GOP Senate candidates. Every Republican candidate will be asked to take a stance, and a Senate majority is made by swing states.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/lindsey-grahams-15-week-abortion-ban-congress-nancy-pelosi-republicans-democrats-11663108380"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lindsey Graham's 15-Week \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220913ei9d006v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
