\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Michigan Supreme Court Orders  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Proposal Be Included on November Ballot; Initiative before voters proposes to amend state constitution to enshrine  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 582 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 September 2022\par 00:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Michigan voters will decide in November whether to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in their state's constitution, after the Michigan Supreme Court ruled Thursday that an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -access initiative must be included on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The state high court overrode an election board decision that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-abortion-rights-ballot-measure-falters-at-state-elections-board-11661991648"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had declined to place the measure on the November ballot }}}\uc2  after opponents of the measure argued that poor spacing between the words in the proposal rendered some of the text incomprehensible.\par \par \uc2 The Michigan amendment fight is being closely watched after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -rights supporters decisively defeated a Kansas ballot measure }}}\uc2  in August that would have amended the state's constitution to explicitly say it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Michigan's four-member Board of State Canvassers had deadlocked along party lines in a vote last week, with two Republicans voting against certifying the ballot measure and two Democrats voting in favor.\par \par \uc2 The majority of high court justices said the meaning of the ballot measure wasn't changed by the allegedly insufficient spacing between the words and chastised the Republican members of the board.\par \par \uc2 "They would disenfranchise millions of Michiganders not because they believe the many thousands of Michiganders who signed the proposal were confused by it, but because they think they have identified a technicality that allows them to do so, a game of 'gotcha' gone very bad," Chief Justice Bridget McCormack wrote.\par \par \uc2 The court voted 5-2 to order that the initiative be placed on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 In dissent, Justice Brian Zahra said adding a provision to the state constitution is an exacting process, for good reason. "Our system for allowing citizens to access the ballot through the exercise of direct democracy is an elaborate one" that requires "exacting detail" from those who propose an initiative, he said.\par \par \uc2 The Reproductive Freedom for All campaign is leading the push for the ballot measure. Its spokeswoman, Darci McConnell, said the group is "energized and motivated now more than ever to restore the protections that were lost" after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  in June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended the constitutional right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Christen Pollo, a spokeswoman for Citizens to Support Michigan Women and Children, which opposes the initiative, said: "It falls to voters now to reject this mistake-ridden, extreme proposal on Election Day."\par \par \uc2 For months, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters and opponents have battled in Michigan over the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. A 1931 Michigan law would ban nearly all abortions except to save the life of the pregnant woman. It has been largely dormant since the Supreme Court's 1973 decision in Roe v. Wade first established a constitutional right to the procedure, but the high court's June decision to overrule Roe has thrown the law into question.\par \par \uc2 A Michigan judge permanently blocked enforcement of the 1931 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on Wednesday, saying that it violates rights to equal protection and bodily integrity under the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 That ruling doesn't change the status quo in Michigan, where prosecutors have largely been blocked from enforcing the ban since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  decision overruling Roe. It also isn't likely to be the last word in the case, which ultimately is expected to be decided by the state Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-supreme-court-orders-abortion-rights-proposal-be-included-on-november-ballot-11662674386"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan Supreme Court Orders \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Rights Proposal Be Included on November Ballot  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220908ei980086h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
