\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Michigan  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights Ballot Measure Falters at State Elections Board; Group backing proposed constitutional amendment will ask state Supreme Court to allow the initiative on November ballot\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto \par \uc2 530 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2022\par 00:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A Michigan elections board declined to place on the November ballot a measure that seeks to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections to the state's constitution, the latest twist in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigans-abortion-tensions-reflect-uncertain-future-in-battleground-states-11651834802"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a tumultuous legal and political fight }}}\uc2  over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the state.\par \par \uc2 The state's four-member Board of State Canvassers deadlocked along party lines in a vote Wednesday, with two Republicans voting against certifying the ballot measure and two Democrats voting in favor. Opponents of the measure had filed a challenge arguing that poor spacing between the words in the proposal rendered some of the text incomprehensible.\par \par \uc2 The Reproductive Freedom for All campaign, which wants to add a "fundamental right to reproductive freedom" to the state's constitution, said it would appeal to the state's Supreme Court, asking it to intervene to force the board to put the proposed amendment before voters in November.\par \par \uc2 A possible Michigan vote on the amendment is being closely watched around the country after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas voters handed a decisive victory }}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters on Aug. 2, rejecting a measure that would have amended the state's constitution to explicitly say it doesn't protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That win has spurred Democrats' optimism about using voter-driven initiatives to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 The Michigan proposal is an attempt to invalidate a 1931 law that would ban nearly all abortions in the state. The law had been dormant since the Supreme Court's 1973 decision in Roe v. Wade first established a constitutional right to the procedure, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the high court's decision in June to overrule Roe }}}\uc2  has thrown the future of the Michigan law into question.\par \par \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All submitted more than 750,000 signatures to place the proposal on the ballot, far more than the roughly 425,000 required, to the state's Bureau of Elections office.\par \par \uc2 "Hundreds of thousands of voters from every county in the state said they want to ensure women have the freedom to make their own decisions about abortions," Darci McConnell, a spokeswoman for the organization said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Opponents of the measure, Citizens to Support Michigan Women and Children, challenged its validity, saying that poor spacing would lead to "nonexistent words" being inserted into the state's constitution.\par \par \uc2 Christen Pollo, a spokeswoman for Citizens to Support Michigan Women and Children, said, "The Board of State Canvassers today did the right thing by refusing to insert into our constitution the gibberish proposed by advocates for this extreme amendment."\par \par \uc2 Aside from the ballot measure, the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Michigan could also be affected by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-governor-abortion-rights-groups-challenge-dormant-state-abortion-ban-11649345756"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuits filed by \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers and the state's Democratic governor }}}\uc2 , \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 . Those cases challenge the 1931 law, arguing that the Michigan Supreme Court should recognize a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state's constitution. A lower court judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-judge-suspends-enforcement-of-pre-roe-abortion-ban-11652819032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has blocked the law from being enforced }}}\uc2  while litigation proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/michigan-abortion-rights-ballot-measure-falters-at-state-elections-board-11661991648"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights Ballot Measure Falters at State Elections Board }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220901ei9100001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
