\par\par \uc2 Health Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Georgia  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Restrictions Spark New Debate Over Claims to Fetal Personhood; Recently implemented state measure presents practical, political and legal tests\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Cameron McWhirter \par \uc2 1,170 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 August 2022\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 In the wake of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court's decision overturning Roe v. Wade,}}}\uc2  Georgia is emerging as the lead testing ground for an idea some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have touted for decades: that fetuses deserve the same types of legal protections as people after birth.\par \par \uc2 The state is one of about a dozen that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have banned many or most abortions}}}\uc2  since the Supreme Court's decision in Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization ended federal constitutional protections for the procedure. But Georgia has taken an additional step, declaring that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legis.ga.gov/api/legislation/document/20192020/187013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "natural persons include an unborn child,"}}}\uc2  with potentially wide-ranging implications for everything from taxes to welfare benefits.\par \par \uc2 The state's law {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-six-week-abortion-ban-goes-into-effect-11658352186"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  after about six weeks of pregnancy,}}}\uc2  with exceptions for medical emergencies, rape or incest, or if a fetus isn't medically viable. The law was passed in 2019 but blocked in the courts until it was allowed to move forward about a month ago.\par \par \uc2 Ed Setzler, the bill's Republican author, said the recognition of fetal personhood is the logical extension of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. "If at the point of detectable heartbeat we're going to protect children from the violence of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , naturally that protection should apply across Georgia law," he said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats and some legal scholars say the law opens the door for any of the dozens of local Georgia prosecutors to charge women with murder for taking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills or traveling to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in another state.\par \par \uc2 "Folks are going to be really surprised just how significant of a law this is," said Jen Jordan, the Democratic candidate for attorney general and a state senator who voted against the law.\par \par \uc2 Republicans say the law isn't designed to penalize women for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Under Georgia law, women cannot be convicted of murder because of this statute," Mr. Setzler said.\par \par \uc2 Agencies in Georgia are now grappling with how to implement the law. The \uc2 Georgia Department of Revenue\uc2  recently issued guidance that said taxpayers with an unborn child "with a detectable human heartbeat" can claim a personal income tax exemption of $3,000 per unborn child. The department declined to explain how someone would provide proof of an unborn child, or what should happen in the event a woman miscarries after claiming the exemption. The department will answer further questions about the impact of the law on taxes later this year, a spokesman said in an email.\par \par \uc2 The author of the bill said it could also allow pregnant women to drive in commuter lanes that require more than one passenger. The state Department of Transportation said the issue would be one for local law enforcement to decide.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Reed, leadership director with the Georgia Life Alliance, which helped write the law, said the group has connected lawyers with women seeking child support during pregnancy. The new Georgia measure says that a court can award support up to the full amount of medical and pregnancy-related expenses.\par \par \uc2 "I think it will also just inspire or ignite men, a little bit forcibly, to take responsibility for these things and be committed to be a father," Ms. Reed said.\par \par \uc2 A 2019 letter from the state's legislative counsel said the law was also likely to increase demand for public benefits because undocumented immigrants could potentially be eligible for certain support, including food stamps and Medicaid, through their unborn children, who would be U.S. citizens at birth. The \uc2 Georgia Department of Human Services\uc2 , which administers such benefits, didn't respond to questions seeking comment.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What are the potential ramifications of Georgia's new personhood law? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Efforts to implement personhood protections for fetuses have been largely unsuccessful over many years. Voters rejected efforts to pass personhood amendments to state constitutions in conservative states such as Mississippi and North Dakota, while a number of laws with similar provisions were blocked by the courts, which said they would violate protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  established in Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 A federal appeals court allowed Georgia's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, including the personhood component, to go into effect after the Dobbs decision, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/pdf/2022/07/20/sistersong_women_of_color_reproductive_justice_collective_v._governor_of_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers are still challenging}}}\uc2  the personhood part of the statute, arguing it is vague and should be unenforceable.\par \par \uc2 Both sides in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate say the Supreme Court's decision to overrule Roe has given the push for personhood laws new momentum.\par \par \uc2 "For years, they've been viewed as promoted by fringe actors and never going to go anywhere. I think post-Dobbs we can't assume that anymore," said \uc2 Jessica Arons\uc2 , a lawyer for \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Josh Craddock, a scholar with the James Wilson Institute, a conservative think tank that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the work of legislators on both the federal and state level won't be done until unborn children have a full spectrum of legal rights. "Talk isn't enough, there has to be action as well, because fetal personhood is the capstone for the pro-life movement," Mr. Craddock said.\par \par \uc2 Legislators, he said, can craft rights to take into account the differences between unborn children and others in society.\par \par \uc2 Georgia's law is the most explicit in enumerating the rights granted to unborn children, but National Advocates for Pregnant Women, a left-leaning legal organization, says there are at least 10 other states that have fetal personhood language on the books that could be interpreted similarly to Georgia's law after the Dobbs decision. A bill introduced in Ohio in July seeks to recognize personhood from conception, a proposal that could test the political appetite for such measures post-Dobbs.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.txnd.365015/gov.uscourts.txnd.365015.73.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision this week by a Texas judge}}}\uc2  temporarily blocking the Biden administration from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/idaho-must-allow-abortions-in-certain-emergencies-judge-rules-11661386919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 requiring doctors to perform abortions in certain emergencies}}}\uc2  also could provide a boost for the fetal personhood movement. The judge said medical providers must balance the interests of a fetus against the interests of a pregnant woman when deciding whether to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With elections in November looming, Democrats have sought to make the Georgia law a top political issue, especially with female voters. Campaign officials for \uc2 Stacey Abrams\uc2 , the Democratic candidate for governor, have criticized the personhood law and blanketed metro Atlanta television stations in recent weeks with a commercial showing tearful, angry women.\par \par \uc2 Republican Gov. \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 's remarks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and personhood have been limited during the campaign. After the Supreme Court's ruling, he said he was overjoyed by the decision and pledged that the state would focus on supporting adoption and other services. His campaign literature and ads make no mention of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but focus instead on improving the economy and battling inflation, which his campaign blames on the Democratic Party.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com}}}\uc2  and Cameron McWhirter at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:cameron.mcwhirter@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cameron.mcwhirter@wsj.com}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/georgia-abortion-restrictions-spark-new-debate-over-claims-to-fetal-personhood-11661601601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Restrictions Spark New Debate Over Claims to Fetal Personhood}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220827ei8r00106\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
