\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Jerrold Nadler\uc2  Defeats \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2  in New York Democratic House Primary Matchup; New York Rep. \uc2 Mondaire Jones\uc2  loses to Dan Goldman in crowded Democratic congressional primary\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jimmy Vielkind and Siobhan Hughes \par \uc2 1,155 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2022\par 05:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Jerrold Nadler\uc2 , the long-serving congressman from Manhattan's Upper West Side, defeated fellow veteran Rep. \uc2 Carolyn Maloney\uc2  in a Democratic primary Tuesday after redistricting in New York state forced them to compete for a single House seat.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Nadler drew national attention when he helped lead the first impeachment of then-President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as chairman of the House Judiciary Committee. He secured more than 50% of the vote in the Manhattan district, parts of which he and Ms. Maloney have represented for nearly 30 years. Ms. Maloney, the head of the Oversight and Reform Committee, trailed well behind with about a quarter of the vote.\par \par \uc2 In a race seen as an early test of Democrats' efforts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-set-to-vote-on-bills-protecting-abortion-access-11657896570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to use \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access to motivate their base }}}\uc2  in competitive contests, Democrat Pat Ryan defeated Republican \uc2 Marc Molinaro\uc2  in a special election to fill an open House seat in New York's Hudson Valley, the Associated Press projected.\par \par \uc2 In other elections held Tuesday, voters in Florida and Oklahoma set the matchups for closely watched races this fall.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, U.S. Rep. \uc2 Charlie Crist{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/charlie-crist-wins-democratic-primary-for-florida-governor-set-to-face-ron-desantis-11661302416"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defeated }}}\uc2  state Agriculture Commissioner \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2  for the Democratic nomination for governor and the right to take on incumbent Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a rising Republican star.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic candidates in Florida had debated who was best suited for that uphill battle and, in the wake of the Supreme Court decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating a constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , who would be the most effective advocate for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In a Senate primary, Democratic Rep. Val Demings won the party's nomination to run against Republican Sen. \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the House seat being vacated by Ms. Demings, 25-year-old Maxwell Frost, a candidate backed by Sen. Bernie Sanders (I., Vt.), won a Democratic primary against two former Democratic lawmakers, Alan Grayson and Corrine Brown. The district is heavily Democratic. In an interview, Mr. Frost, a gun-control activist, said that his interest in politics began after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424127887323297104578179271453737596"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the 2012 shootings at Sandy Hook Elementary School }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  (R., Fla.), a close ally of Mr. Trump, won his GOP primary, essentially ensuring re-election in his solidly Republican district. Mr. Gaetz will face Democrat Rebekah Jones.\par \par \uc2 In New York City, Democrats poured their energy into primary contests for the 10th and 12th districts. Longtime Reps. Nadler and Maloney found themselves facing off when they were drawn together in the 12th District, which includes Midtown Manhattan and residential areas surrounding Central Park.\par \par \uc2 Another incumbent, freshman Rep. \uc2 Mondaire Jones\uc2 , was defeated in a Democratic primary for a district covering Manhattan and Brooklyn. Dan Goldman, a former federal prosecutor who also served as lead counsel in Mr. Trump's first impeachment, finished first in the crowded field, with Assemblywoman Yuh-Line Niou second and Mr. Jones third.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Goldman, an heir to the \uc2 Levi Strauss & Co\uc2 . fortune, has lent his campaign several million dollars and has outspent his rivals. Ms. Niou was backed by the progressive \uc2 Working Families Party\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Following redistricting, Mr. Jones scrapped plans to seek re-election from his Westchester County home when a more senior member, Rep. \uc2 Sean Patrick Maloney\uc2 , said he would run there. Mr. Maloney, who heads the Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee, won his primary race against state Sen. \uc2 Alessandra Biaggi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Oklahoma, Rep. \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  won a GOP primary runoff in the race to fill the remainder of the term of retiring Republican Sen. \uc2 Jim Inhofe\uc2 . Mr. Mullin defeated T.W. Shannon, who was the first Black person to serve as House speaker in Oklahoma.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Mullin will take on former Democratic Rep. \uc2 Kendra Horn\uc2  in a special election this fall in the deep-red state. Mr. Inhofe, who plans to retire in early January, was elected to a six-year term in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Separately, in an Oklahoma Democratic primary, Madison Horn beat Jason Bollinger to be the party's candidate against incumbent Republican Sen. \uc2 James Lankford\uc2  in the fall.\par \par \uc2 New Yorkers cast ballots in two special elections for the \uc2 U.S. House\uc2  as well as in primary elections for Congress and the state Senate. All New York primaries were originally scheduled for June 28, but the congressional and state Senate contests were moved to August after a judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/top-new-york-court-throws-out-proposed-congressional-maps-11651087762"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down Democrat-drawn district lines }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the Hudson Valley's 19th District, the AP projected just after midnight that Mr. Ryan, a Democrat, defeated the GOP's Mr. Molinaro in a closely watched contest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/candidates-for-congress-in-new-yorks-hudson-valley-are-running-in-two-districts-at-once-11661086801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to fill the term }}}\uc2  of ex-Rep. Antonio Delgado. With most of the vote counted, Mr. Ryan led 51.1% to 48.9%.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Ryan, the Ulster County executive, aired ads touting his support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access after the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  struck down Roe v. Wade in July. Mr. Molinaro, the Dutchess County executive, said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy should be left to states and has said he personally opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Both also campaigned on inflation and the cost of living. Mr. Molinaro highlighted the rise in prices under President Biden and said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/joe-biden-to-sign-bill-aimed-at-lowering-drug-costs-boosting-renewable-energy-11660642202"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats' tax, healthcare and climate package }}}\uc2 , signed into law last week, would do little to curb inflation. Mr. Ryan supports that measure.\par \par \uc2 The seat opened up with Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 's appointment of Mr. Delgado as lieutenant governor when the previous holder of that office, \uc2 Brian Benjamin\uc2 , resigned after being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-lt-gov-brian-benjamin-charged-with-public-corruption-11649773533"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged in an alleged bribery scheme. }}}\uc2  Mr. Benjamin has pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 The other special election was to serve out the end of the term of former GOP Rep. \uc2 Tom Reed\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/rep-tom-reed-says-he-wont-run-for-re-election-in-2022-11616368571"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 canceled his re-election efforts }}}\uc2  after apologizing for inappropriate sexual conduct and later resigned to take a job at a government-relations firm. In the red-leaning district, Republican Joe Sempolinski defeated Democrat Max Della Pia, who is also running in the November general election for the term starting next year.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Sempolinski will serve about four months as he isn't running for the next full term. In the GOP primary for that full term, \uc2 Nick Langworthy\uc2  defeated Carl Paladino after a heated contest in which both candidates have expressed their long ties to Mr. Trump, who hasn't made an endorsement in the race.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What are you watching for in this week's primaries? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Langworthy chairs the state Republican Party but was seeking elected office for the first time. Mr. Paladino, a real-estate developer, was the GOP's 2010 gubernatorial candidate after he harnessed tea-party support for an unexpected primary victory over the party-endorsed candidate. He lost in the general election.\par \par \uc2 Joshua Jamerson and Arian Campo-Flores contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jimmy Vielkind at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jimmy.Vielkind@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Siobhan Hughes at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:siobhan.hughes@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 siobhan.hughes@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-democrats-fight-for-redistricted-seats-in-new-york-primaries-11661247002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jerrold Nadler Defeats Carolyn Maloney in New York Democratic House Primary Matchup }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220823ei8n000gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
