\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  Wins Democratic Primary for Florida Governor, Set to Face \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ; Crist, a former GOP state attorney general and governor, squares off against an incumbent widely expected to be a 2024 presidential candidate\b0\par\par\uc2 By Arian Campo-Flores \par \uc2 805 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2022\par 01:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 U.S. Rep. \uc2 Charlie Crist\uc2  secured the Democratic nomination for governor in Florida, setting up what promises to be an uphill battle against incumbent Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , a rising Republican star with a formidable fundraising advantage.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Crist, a former Florida governor and attorney general, prevailed against \uc2 Nikki Fried\uc2 , the state agriculture commissioner. With the lion's share of the ballots counted, Mr. Crist took nearly 60% of the vote.\par \par \uc2 Both Democrats sought to portray themselves as the strongest candidate to take on Mr. DeSantis, who raised his national profile over his handling of the pandemic and is widely considered a potential 2024 presidential candidate. The incumbent's legislative and policy agenda targeting what he calls {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/floridas-desantis-takes-aim-at-woke-capital-11659043495"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "woke indoctrination" by schools and corporations }}}\uc2  has electrified conservatives and enraged liberals.\par \par \uc2 In Other Election News:\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-democrats-fight-for-redistricted-seats-in-new-york-primaries-11661247002"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jerrold Nadler Defeats Carolyn Maloney in New York Democratic House Primary Matchup }}}\par \par \uc2 "This is the most consequential race in the history of our state," Mr. Crist told supporters in St. Petersburg after winning the primary. Floridians "want a governor who cares about them to solve real problems, that preserves our freedom, not a bully who divides us and takes our freedom away."\par \par \uc2 Ms. Fried congratulated Mr. Crist in a concession speech and urged Democrats to unite in November. "We are going to make \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  a one-term governor and a zero-term president," she said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Crist, who is 66 and an experienced campaigner with a genial style, cast himself as a unifying consensus-builder who can heal what he considers the divisiveness of Mr. DeSantis's tenure. He secured endorsements from prominent Democrats, large unions and major newspaper editorial boards.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Crist won his 2006 race for Florida governor as a Republican, and governed as a moderate. He chose not to seek re-election in 2010 and instead unsuccessfully ran for the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  as an independent against Republican \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Two years later, he became a Democrat, saying the GOP had been overtaken by the extreme right, and in 2014, he lost a race for governor against \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 . He has been a Democratic congressman representing a district in the St. Petersburg area since 2017.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the Supreme Court's June decision {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating a constitutional right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  became a central focus of the campaigns. Ms. Fried accused Mr. Crist of appointing conservative judges to the Florida Supreme Court who could vote to uphold the state's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-15-week-abortion-ban-into-law-11649961049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently enacted 15-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2 . Mr. Crist vowed to sign an executive order to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state under the Florida constitution.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis championed the 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and celebrated the Supreme Court decision. But unlike Republican leaders in some other states, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-pauses-on-more-abortion-restrictions-following-supreme-court-decision-11656591626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hasn't proposed significant new restrictions }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the general election against Mr. DeSantis, Mr. Crist will face an incumbent whom Democrats would relish defeating but whom political analysts consider a solid favorite. Mr. DeSantis has maintained largely favorable approval ratings. He has raised about $172 million, vastly outpacing Democratic rivals, according to FollowTheMoney.org, which tracks campaign contributions. Mr. Crist has raised about $15 million.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis significantly boosted his profile during the pandemic by reopening businesses and schools faster than other large states, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/battle-over-covid-19-school-mask-rules-plays-out-in-florida-court-11630006339"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposing mask mandates }}}\uc2  and clashing with public health officials who called for a more cautious approach. Those moves, he argued, helped Florida recover economically more quickly than many states.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis's legislative and policy proposals have galvanized conservative supporters, including backers of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who endorsed him in his 2018 gubernatorial run. Among the recent laws he has championed are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-bill-restricting-teaching-about-sexual-orientation-11648498840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one banning instruction on sexual orientation or gender identity in early grades }}}\uc2  and another prohibiting public schools and private employers from mandating certain types of racial-sensitivity instruction.\par \par \uc2 Though Florida used to be one of the most closely divided states in the nation, it has leaned right in recent years. Mr. Trump won the state in 2020 by 3 percentage points, compared with 1 percentage point in 2016, partly because of significant gains among Hispanic voters. Last year, Republicans overtook Democrats among registered voters in Florida for the first time in state history.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic state party in Florida has trailed Republicans in fundraising and voter turnout operations, presenting a further hurdle for Mr. Crist. Democrats argue that with liberal and moderate voters galvanized over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and other issues such as decreased housing affordability, Mr. Crist can seize an opening.\par \par \uc2 Write to Arian Campo-Flores at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:arian.campo-flores@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arian.campo-flores@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/charlie-crist-wins-democratic-primary-for-florida-governor-set-to-face-ron-desantis-11661302416"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charlie Crist Wins Democratic Primary for Florida Governor, Set to Face Ron DeSantis }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220824ei8o000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
