\par \par \uc2 Two medications, mifepristone and misoprostol, are typically used in a medication-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimen. PHOTO: Natalie Behring for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Medside24.com, a website based in Kazakhstan, said its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill sales across the U.S. have doubled since Roe v. Wade was overturned. The site buys \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs manufactured by companies in China, Russia and Vietnam, a representative for the site said, including Vietnam-based Stellapharm J.V. Co.\par \par \uc2 Stellapharm said it manufactures mifepristone and misoprostol but wasn't aware its products were being sold on medside24.com. Stellapharm's pills are only sold with a prescription in Vietnam, a spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 A woman from Florida said she ordered pills from abortionrx.com in July. She said that would have preferred to visit a clinic near her home but didn't want to wait three weeks until an appointment was available. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-providers-in-illinois-colorado-and-florida-prepare-for-patient-influx-if-roe-is-overturned-11655560800"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is legal in Florida until 15 weeks }}}\uc2  of gestation.\par \par \uc2 No screening or prescription was required to complete the $249 purchase via \uc2 PayPal\uc2 , she said, and the pills arrived four days later in a brown envelope from an address in Las Vegas. There were no instructions, she said, so she followed guidance she found online to take the pills over several days. She said she didn't experience complications during her \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Abortionrx.com is registered to Rablon Healthcare Private Ltd. in Mumbai. Rablon didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 At least six sites selling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills without a prescription in July were registered under the name Richard Asamoah Agyemang of Denver, according to information on domain ownership. Mr. Agyemang said he is a college student and web developer. He said he doesn't sell \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. "I don't know who made those websites," Mr. Agyemang said. Two of the sites had been taken offline in August.\par \par \uc2 Some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -pill websites say that they sell pills from manufacturers in India. Three manufacturers mentioned on some sites, \uc2 Zydus Lifesciences Ltd\uc2 ., \uc2 Cipla Ltd\uc2 . and Naman Pharma Drugs, said they weren't aware of the sites. \uc2 Cipla\uc2  said it stopped making \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication about seven years ago. Naman manufactures \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills on a contract basis for companies in Africa and doesn't export to the U.S., a spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 A teacher in Ohio said she sought out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills this spring using Plan C, a nonprofit that provides information about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, including some half-dozen websites that sell the pills without a prescription. Plan C said it regularly orders from the websites to vet them.\par \par \uc2 The teacher said she bought pills from Aid Access, a telemedicine provider in Austria, before realizing she would have to wait as long as three weeks for the pills to arrive from India.\par \par \uc2 "We really understand that this wait can be hard for women, and it's really unfortunate that it's something we cannot change," Aid Access founder Rebecca Gomperts said.\par \par \uc2 The teacher in Ohio said she consulted Plan C again and bought pills for $470 from onlineabortionpillsrx.com. The site sent her a link to pay via \uc2 PayPal\uc2 , she said. The site instructed her not to mention the medications she was purchasing on \uc2 PayPal\uc2 , according to an email viewed by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 "In case \uc2 PayPal\uc2  comes to know about what you purchased, \uc2 PayPal\uc2  may take legal action against you," the email said.\par \par \uc2 Onlineabortionpillsrx.com, which is registered to a post-office box in Sydney, Australia, didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 PayPal\uc2  generally doesn't pursue legal action against buyers, said a person familiar with the platform's operations, but the company could close accounts if they violate its acceptable-use policy. The policy says sales of products requiring a prescription aren't allowed without approval.\par \par \uc2 The teacher said she received a message from onlineabortionpillsrx.com saying the pills were delayed in transit from India. She said she paid $350 via \uc2 PayPal\uc2  to a third site, genericabortionpills.com. She said the pills arrived in a couple of days postmarked from Denver in a box marked "Antipreg Kit," which was viewed by the Journal.\par \par \uc2 Genericabortionpills.com didn't respond to requests for comment. The website says it sells pills made by Zydus. Zydus manufactures \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills on a contract basis, a spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 "We have no information on how they are being sold online," he said.\par \par \uc2 Jim Oberman contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Dominique Mosbergen at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:dominique.mosbergen@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dominique.mosbergen@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Vibhuti Agarwal at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:vibhuti.agarwal@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vibhuti.agarwal@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/websites-selling-unapproved-abortion-pills-are-booming-11661079601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Websites Selling Unapproved \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Pills Are Booming }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220821ei8l000b6\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
