\par\par \uc2 Business\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Walmart\uc2  Expands  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Coverage in Employee Health Plan; Retailer expands the types of medical situations for which its employee health plan would cover abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sarah Nassauer \par \uc2 506 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 August 2022\par 20:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Walmart Inc\uc2 . is expanding the types of medical situations for which its employee health plan would cover abortions and the cost of travel, to include conditions such as ectopic pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The shift at \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , the country's largest private employer, is another sign of how companies are grappling with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124#:~:text=Hide Caption-,Protesters gathered in Columbus, Ohio, in support of abortion rights,Supreme Court ruling on Friday.&text=WASHINGTON���The Supreme Court eliminated,abortion's legality to the states."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Supreme Court's decision }}}\uc2  earlier this summer to overturn the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , based in Bentonville, Ark., sent a memo to its roughly 1.7 million U.S. workers that said its healthcare plan would cover the cost of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when "there is a health risk to the mother, rape or incest, ectopic pregnancy, miscarriage or lack of fetal viability." A \uc2 Walmart\uc2  spokeswoman said it would defer to the woman's doctor in determining whether those conditions are met.\par \par \uc2 Previously, \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's health plan said the company would cover the procedure "when the health of the mother would be in danger if the fetus were carried to term, the fetus could not survive the birthing process, or death would be imminent after birth."\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's policy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/on-abortion-coverage-company-health-plans-diverge-11656700014"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contrasts with some other large companies }}}\uc2 , including banks, technology companies and retailers such as \uc2 Target Corp\uc2 ., which broadly cover \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and related travel under company healthcare plans.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's expanded coverage was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/08/19/walmart-expands-abortion-coverage-for-employees-after-roe-v-wade.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier reported by CNBC }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this summer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-roe-v-wade-ruling-companies-reimbursing-medical-and-travel-expenses-for-abortion-risk-blowback-11656109337"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several large companies added coverage for travel }}}\uc2  related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to employee healthcare plans in response to the Supreme Court's decision.\par \par \uc2 Target, \uc2 Walgreens Boots Alliance Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2 . offer employee healthcare plans that cover \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  broadly, according to people familiar with the plans. Large banks and technology companies, including \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 . and \uc2 JPMorgan Chase & Co\uc2 ., tend to cover the costs of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care for employees and family members under their plans. The companies are among those that have also promised to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-roe-v-wade-ruling-companies-reimbursing-medical-and-travel-expenses-for-abortion-risk-blowback-11656109337"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reimburse employees for travel to receive \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and other healthcare services that aren't provided in their state.\par \par \uc2 Walmart\uc2  is headquartered in Bentonville, Ark., a state that allows \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to save a mother's life but not in the case of rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 The type of health-insurance plan offered by large and midsize U.S. companies tends to include some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefits. A federal antidiscrimination statute requires all employers that provide health insurance to cover an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the life of the mother is at risk from the pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \uc2 Walmart\uc2  told workers it would also cover travel for medically necessary abortions. "Given how recent events are resulting in state-by-state healthcare environments, we will expand our travel coverage," said \uc2 Walmart\uc2  Chief People Officer \uc2 Donna Morris\uc2  in a memo. The benefit extends to workers and their covered dependents accessing covered \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when it isn't available within 100 miles of their location, she said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sarah Nassauer at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:sarah.nassauer@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sarah.nassauer@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/walmart-to-cover-medically-necessary-abortions-for-workers-11660931412"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Walmart Expands \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Coverage in Employee Health Plan }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220819ei8j004v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
