\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \uc2 Tech\par \b \uc2 Google Workers Press Company to Stop Collecting  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Data; Petition sent to CEO \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2  also calls on \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  to remove search results for crisis pregnancy centers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Miles Kruppa \par \uc2 600 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 August 2022\par 13:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A group of workers at \uc2 Google\uc2  parent \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 . has asked the company to stop collecting data on users seeking information about abortions, according to a petition sent to Chief Executive Officer \uc2 Sundar Pichai\uc2  this week.\par \par \uc2 The petition, signed by more than 650 workers, also called on the company to remove search results for crisis pregnancy centers, which it said were misleading to those seeking abortions. Crisis pregnancy centers are typically nonprofits that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-exempts-christian-social-services-group-from-non-discrimination-rule-11548282932"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 counsel women against having abortions }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Representatives from the Alphabet Workers Union sent the petition to Mr. Pichai on Monday after circulating it among employees last week, a spokesman for the union said. Mr. Pichai hadn't responded by the end of the workday on Wednesday, the spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Google\uc2  spokeswoman declined to comment on the petition. \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  has reported that it had 174,014 full-time employees at the end of June, in addition to a large number of contract workers.\par \par \uc2 Tech companies and location-data brokers are under heightened scrutiny after the Supreme Court ruling in June that overturned Roe v. Wade. Privacy advocates fear that prosecutors will use warrants or subpoenas to demand {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/phones-know-who-went-to-an-abortion-clinic-whom-will-they-tell-11659873781"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data revealing users }}}\uc2  who have visited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics or sought out related information. That data could be used to build legal cases against people who are charged with having an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that have outlawed the procedure }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 , like most tech companies, has said it responds to lawful requests from government agencies for user data and that it pushes back against requests that it deems overly broad or otherwise objectionable.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 's handling of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related policies has become a politically charged issue. Before the Supreme Court ruling, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warner.senate.gov/public/_cache/files/5/6/5698c724-cc0d-42f6-bbb6-b05e472b4564/26F26BB28841042A7931EEC58AC80E08.anti-abortion-letter-to-google-final.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 20 congressional Democrats }}}\uc2  urged \uc2 Google\uc2  in a letter to Mr. Pichai to take action limiting the appearance of crisis pregnancy centers in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related searches.\par \par \uc2 The following month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reason.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/StateAttorneysGeneralLettertoGoogleJuly212022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17 Republican attorneys general }}}\uc2  responded with their own letter warning that they would take action against the company if it suppressed results related to crisis pregnancy centers, which the group said provide important medical services.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  union in late June released a public statement asking \uc2 Google\uc2  to stop storing "any data that could be used to prosecute users in the U.S. exercising their bodily autonomy."\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  said in July it would begin automatically deleting data on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/google-to-delete-visits-to-abortion-clinics-from-users-location-history-11656710884"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 physical visits to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinics }}}\uc2  logged by the company's products.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Pichai said in an email to employees following the announcement last month that \uc2 Google\uc2  would "work on new ways to strengthen and improve these protections over time."\par \par \uc2 The petition this week pressed the company to go farther. It asked that \uc2 Google\uc2  introduce "immediate user data privacy controls for all health-related activity," such as searches related to reproductive issues, and to stop saving any user information related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services. It also called on \uc2 Google\uc2  to fix "misleading search results related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services by removing results for fake \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers."\par \par \uc2 Among its other demands, the workers asked \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  to extend certain reproductive-healthcare benefits to contractors, end lobbying efforts through its in-house political-action committee and take steps to limit advertisements on publishers of "disinformation related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services."\par \par \uc2 Workers who signed the petition asked \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  to create a task force with 50% employee representation for handling \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related issues across the company.\par \par \uc2 Write to Miles Kruppa at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:miles.kruppa@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 miles.kruppa@wsj.com }}}\par \par 