\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Schumer Shrugs as Roe v. Wade Falls; The Inflation Reduction Act gave Democrats a chance to fund  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 . They didn't even try.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chris Jacobs \par \uc2 581 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 August 2022\par 17:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Before the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, 25 Democratic senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.warren.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/2022.06.07 Letter to POTUS on Abortion EO.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  to President Biden demanding "a whole-of-government response" to the prospect of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Two months later, there was an opportunity to enact such policies regardless of Republican opposition, but Democrats in Congress didn't even bother bringing them up for a vote.\par \par \uc2 The narrow Democratic majorities and the Senate filibuster had seemed to preclude legislation to counteract the effect of Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization. The Senate failed to overcome a filibuster on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation in February, and Sens. \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  (D., Ariz.) and Joe Manchin (D., W.Va.) oppose overturning the filibuster rule, meaning that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related legislation would need 60 votes.\par \par \uc2 But the budget reconciliation bill that Congress just passed was different. It could\u8212\'20\'14and did\u8212\'20\'14pass the Senate with only Democratic votes, including Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's tie-breaker. The bill also provided an opportunity to get around the Hyde Amendment, which prohibits most federal funding of abortions. The amendment applies only to appropriations through the annual spending bill that funds the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senate rules require all provisions of a reconciliation bill to have a primary nexus to the federal budget. Democrats couldn't have used this bill to make policy changes like "codifying" Roe v. Wade or repealing the Hyde Amendment. But they could have allocated federal funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in any number of ways, from creating grants to fund out-of-state travel to a tax credit reimbursing patients for the procedure itself.\par \par \uc2 Yet of the nearly 500 amendments that lawmakers filed on the budget reconciliation bill, the only ones touching on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  came from Republicans. Not only did the issue not receive a vote on the Senate floor; it barely received a word of debate, belying the Democratic senators' June push for "a whole-of-government response." In the House, no Democrat attempted to offer an amendment to the bill\u8212\'20\'14on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or anything else.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the senators knew that several of their Democratic colleagues\u8212\'20\'14notably Mr. Manchin, Bob Casey of Pennsylvania and Tim Kaine of Virginia\u8212\'20\'14had previously supported the Hyde Amendment. But the prospect of a failed vote didn't dissuade Sen. Bernie Sanders of Vermont from demanding votes on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1172/vote_117_2_00292.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding Medicare}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1172/vote_117_2_00292.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other social programs}}}\uc2 , or Sen. \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  of Georgia from demanding a vote on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1172/vote_117_2_00310.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Medicaid expansion}}}\uc2 , all of which went down to defeat during the reconciliation process. Nor did the certainty of failure dissuade Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  from demanding a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1172/vote_117_2_00170.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second unsuccessful vote}}}\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation in May, after a similar bill had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1172/vote_117_2_00065.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed}}}\uc2  to overcome a filibuster in February.\par \par \uc2 As a pro-life conservative, I view the Democrats' inaction as a positive development. I know from my experience as a Senate staffer that budget reconciliation presents a unique procedural opening, and so am struck by the contrast between the left's call for action and Democratic lawmakers' insouciance. Between now and November, Democratic candidates will seek to juice turnout by denouncing the Supreme Court and promising to restore access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They've given voters good reason to doubt they're serious.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Jacobs is founder and CEO of Juniper Research Group and author of "The Case Against Single Payer."\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/schumer-shrugs-as-roe-falls-democrats-reconciliation-abortion-hyde-amendment-filibuster-midterms-medicare-dobbs-supreme-court-11660651920"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Schumer Shrugs as Roe v. Wade Falls}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220816ei8g004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
