\par\par \uc2 Commentary (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Laws Demand Fair Enforcement; Indiana's \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2  baselessly attacks the physician who treated an Ohio 10-year-old.\b0\par\par\uc2 By John Tinder and Susan Brooks \par \uc2 527 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 August 2022\par 17:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 We are confident of Americans' ability to work through the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  now that the Supreme Court has returned it to the democratic process. But it's crucial for law enforcement to stay above the partisan fray. A case in Indiana leaves us deeply concerned on that score.\par \par \uc2 Initially, some doubted news reports that a 10-year-old Ohio rape victim had traveled to Indiana for a legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There were also unsubstantiated claims that the physician who performed the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  had failed to report the abuse of a child and the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  performed on a girl under 16, as Indiana law requires.\par \par \uc2 Indiana Attorney General \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2  rushed precipitously into this fray. He told Fox News he was investigating the physician and "was looking at her licensure." This, after admitting he hadn't examined evidence that she complied with reporting requirements. Even worse was his inflammatory rhetoric: "We have this \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist acting as a doctor," he said.\par \par \uc2 Despite the arrest and confession of a defendant in the rape, and news accounts documenting the physician's timely reporting, Mr. Rokita continues to say publicly that he is investigating her.\par \par \uc2 The justice system's legitimacy requires that law enforcement be fair, deliberative and ethical. Government investigations should remain confidential unless and until a defendant is charged, with respect for the presumption of innocence and government's burden of proof. A baseless investigation, if disclosed publicly, causes the target reputational damage, humiliation and loss.\par \par \uc2 We are appalled that, by his own admission, Mr. Rokita announced his investigation before gathering the most basic facts. Every attorney, as an officer of the court, has a solemn duty not to make false, misleading or groundless statements of law or fact. Mr. Rokita's position heightens that duty. His client, the state of Indiana, has the power to deprive its residents of liberty and property.\par \par \uc2 Indiana prosecutors are required to "refrain from making extrajudicial comments that have a substantial likelihood of heightening public condemnation of the accused." Mr. Rokita has disregarded that obligation.\par \par \uc2 A functioning democracy requires that citizens trust the state to enforce the law fairly. A prosecutor should never wield the government's extraordinary authority for political or ideological aims. That smacks of McCarthyism and is especially pernicious at a sensitive political moment.\par \par \uc2 Our nation remains deeply divided over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That won't change soon. One of us (Ms. Brooks) had a consistent pro-life record in Congress; the other (Mr. Tinder), a retired judge, has taken no public position on the issue. Wherever public officials stand, they are obligated to follow time-tested principles that promote the rule of law. We hope Mr. Rokita will rethink his actions and law-enforcement officials across the country will reject his example.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tinder served as a federal judge, 1987-2015. Ms. Brooks, a Republican, represented Indiana's Fifth Congressional District, 2013-21. Each served as U.S. attorney for Indiana's Southern District, respectively from 1984-87 and 2001-07.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-laws-demand-fair-enforcement-indiana-ten-year-old-victim-ohio-todd-rokita-prosecutor-investigation-11660140484"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Laws Demand Fair Enforcement}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220810ei8a004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
