\par\par \uc2 World News\par \uc2 World\par \b \uc2 How  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Access Has Changed Around the World; With Roe v. Wade overturned, the U.S. is one of a small number of countries where  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  laws are being tightened\b0\par\par\uc2 By Josh Ulick, James Benedict and Carl Churchill \par \uc2 1,037 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 August 2022\par 17:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Over the past 25 years, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  has risen globally. Around 50 countries have expanded the legal grounds under which women can seek the procedure, according to the Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which advocates for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The center categorizes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws into five levels of stringency, ranging from outright prohibition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -on-request. In between are countries that allow abortions when the life or health of the woman is at risk. Other countries go beyond health, taking broad social and economic factors into account when considering the impact of pregnancy and childbearing. These factors can include being unable to take care of a child because of work, housing or financial strains.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/supreme-court-decision-roe-v-wade-6-24-2022/card/europeans-react-on-roe-v-wade-YQY9SVjtWc4K7DIfB0R8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Countries that allow \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  may have gestational limits in place, after which procedures are no longer permitted, as well as parental or spousal approval requirements.\par \par \uc2 Since 1994, 18 countries that previously prohibited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  loosened their restrictions.\par \par \uc2 An additional seven countries that allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the life of the woman was at risk relaxed their laws as well. These include Ireland, where a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/irelands-vote-to-legalize-abortion-reflects-a-nation-in-transition-1527337110"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2018 referendum }}}\uc2  overturned one of the strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Twelve countries that limited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cases where the health of the woman was at risk, including Spain, South Africa and Argentina, loosened their laws to either allow abortions for social and economic reasons or upon request.\par \par \uc2 Other countries have relaxed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in more incremental ways, by adding exceptions for rape, incest or fetal impairment, for instance.\par \par \uc2 Before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade was overturned }}}\uc2 , the U.S. had relatively liberal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, allowing the procedure up until the viability of the fetus. The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 's decision in June ending the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves states to regulate access. Many are now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/doctors-struggle-with-state-abortion-restrictions-at-odds-with-federal-law-11657445400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to enact restrictions }}}\uc2 , with 16 states limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  primarily to cases where a woman's life or health is at risk.\par \par \uc2 While some states are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-prepare-to-quickly-implement-abortion-trigger-laws-11655385028"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tightening their laws }}}\uc2 , others are seeking to strengthen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access after Roe v. Wade. Vermont and California are moving forward with November ballot measures that would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-york-lawmakers-firm-up-gun-abortion-rules-following-supreme-court-decisions-11656706664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 codify the right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in their constitutions. New York state is seeking a similar amendment, though it may not go before voters until 2024.\par \par \uc2 With the Supreme Court decision, the U.S. is one of a small number of countries where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws are being tightened. These include Poland, which in 2020 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/polands-top-court-tightens-strict-abortion-laws-11603397449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared the procedure unconstitutional }}}\uc2  when conducted because of fetal abnormalities.\par \par \uc2 In 1998, El Salvador changed its law to remove all exceptions to its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prohibition. Previously, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was permitted to save a woman's life, and in cases of rape and fetal impairment. Nicaragua eliminated all exceptions to its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in 2006.\par \par \uc2 How \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws compare around the world\par \par \uc2 Of the 195 countries for which data is available, 12% prohibit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  outright. About 21% primarily restrict it to instances where the woman's life is at risk. Another 24% limit it to instances where the woman's health is at risk, which depending on the laws, can include mental as well as physical health.\par \par \uc2 An additional 6% of countries allow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for broad social and economic reasons. About 37% of locations permit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on request, often with gestational limits.\par \par \uc2 Countries in more lenient categories allow the exceptions available in less lenient ones. So countries that permit abortions for health reasons also permit them when the life of the mother is at risk. And countries that allow abortions on socioeconomic grounds also allow them in cases of risk to health or life.\par \par \uc2 Many of the countries with more restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws are in Africa, Latin America or the Middle East. Those with less restrictive laws tend to be clustered in Europe and Asia.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the Supreme Court decision, Ohio, Georgia, South Carolina and Tennessee now ban abortions at six weeks of pregnancy, with Iowa possibly following suit. Tennessee is expected to remove its gestational period soon, restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in all stages of pregnancy. In other nations with gestational limits, 12 weeks into pregnancy is the most common cutoff. Turkey, Portugal, Croatia and Guyana are among those with less than 12-week bans.\par \par \uc2 In some states, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is limited even where the law allows it, such as in Arizona, where all clinics are closed pending state law clarification.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Kansas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters on Tuesday rejected }}}\uc2  a proposed state constitutional amendment that would have ended protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Indiana's legislature on Friday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/indiana-legislature-is-first-to-approve-abortion-bans-since-supreme-court-overturned-roe-v-wade-11659755538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed a ban }}}\uc2  with exceptions limited to cases of rape and incest, and to protect the life and physical health of the mother.\par \par \uc2 How \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates have changed\par \par \uc2 Globally, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates have more or less held steady over the past 30 years. There were an estimated 40 abortions per 1,000 women ages 15\u8211\'20\'1349 from 1990 to 1994. From 2015 to 2019, there were 39, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/langlo/article/PIIS2214-109X(20)30315-6/fulltext"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a study }}}\uc2  by researchers at the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Regionally, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates have fallen in Europe and North America, while rising in much of Asia as well as sub-Saharan Africa.\par \par \uc2 Determining precise \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates can be challenging in some countries, particularly those with restrictive laws.\par \par \uc2 That \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates haven't risen more in the past three decades, despite increasingly liberal laws, is due in part to an overall drop in unintended pregnancies worldwide, according to Jonathan Bearak of the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , lead author of the study.\par \par \uc2 The study also found that, on average, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become more common in countries that restrict it. Some of the rise may be because of the increased {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-pill-orders-increase-even-in-restrictive-states-11658136602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 use of misoprostol }}}\uc2 . The medication, which can terminate pregnancies, may be available on the black market in countries that restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This likely contributes to more of unintended pregnancies ending in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in places where it is restricted, Dr. Bearak said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Josh Ulick at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:josh.ulick@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 josh.ulick@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , James Benedict at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:james.benedict@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 james.benedict@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Carl Churchill at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:carl.churchill@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 carl.churchill@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/how-abortion-access-has-changed-around-the-world-11659764119"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Access Has Changed Around the World }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220806ei860012x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
