\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  Suspends Florida Prosecutor Over Pledge to Not Prosecute  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 , Gender-Transition Cases; State attorney Andrew Warren had signed joint statements with other elected prosecutors around country\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joseph De Avila \par \uc2 857 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2022\par 23:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 Florida doesn't have a law criminalizing gender-affirming procedures. An earlier version of this article incorrectly implied the state did. (Corrected on Aug. 4)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://asset.wsj.net/wsjnewsgraphics/projects/narrator/780e0415-ca0e-4db6-986c-f3891ec9f11d.json"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://asset.wsj.net/wsjnewsgraphics/projects/narrator/780e0415-ca0e-4db6-986c-f3891ec9f11d.json }}}\par \par \uc2 Florida Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  suspended a state prosecutor Thursday for pledges he made to decline prosecuting cases involving violations related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender-transition treatments.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis said he suspended Andrew Warren, a Democrat who served as the top prosecutor for the state's 13th judicial circuit in Hillsborough County, which includes Tampa, for neglect of duty. The Republican governor tapped state judge Susan Lopez to serve as state attorney during the suspension. The state has 20 state attorneys.\par \par \uc2 "State Attorneys have a duty to prosecute crimes as defined in Florida law, not to pick and choose which laws to enforce based on his personal agenda," Mr. DeSantis said. "It is my duty to hold Florida's elected officials to the highest standards for the people of Florida."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warren, who was first elected in 2016 and was re-elected in 2020, said his suspension was a political stunt.\par \par \uc2 The governor's move is an "illegal overreach that continues a dangerous pattern by \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of using his office to further his own political ambition," Mr. Warren {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewWarrenFL/status/1555266171422887937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a statement }}}\uc2 . "It spits in the face of the voters of Hillsborough County who have twice elected me to serve them, not \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warren's office didn't immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis said the state constitution gave him authority to suspend state officials for reasons of misfeasance, malfeasance, neglect of duty, drunkenness, incompetence, permanent inability to perform official duties, or commission of a felony.\par \par \uc2 Florida's constitution gives broad powers to the governor to suspend officers such as state attorneys or county sheriffs for almost any reason, said Robert Jarvis, a professor who teaches Florida constitutional law at Nova Southeastern University's Shepard Broad College of Law. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-desantis-expected-to-suspend-sheriff-over-parkland-shooting-11547225013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. DeSantis suspended }}}\uc2  former Broward County Sheriff \uc2 Scott Israel\uc2  in 2019 because of his department's handling of the Parkland school shooting.\par \par \uc2 That authority has been challenged many times, but the courts have routinely ruled in favor of the governor, Dr. Jarvis said.\par \par \uc2 "The Florida Supreme Court has always said the governor has tremendous leeway, and there is almost nothing that wouldn't pass muster in terms of suspension," Dr. Jarvis said.\par \par \uc2 The governor's executive order Thursday said prosecutors have some discretion over whether to prosecute defendants. But it added that Mr. Warren's "blanket refusal" to enforce criminal law amounted to a veto on state law.\par \par \uc2 The order cites joint statements signed by Mr. Warren regarding potential crimes related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender-affirming procedures.\par \par \uc2 Weeks after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2 , Mr. Warren signed a statement, along with other elected prosecutors, regarding the enforcement of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/FJP-Post-Dobbs-Abortion-Joint-Statement.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The statement said }}}\uc2  the prosecutors wouldn't prosecute people who perform abortions.\par \par \uc2 "Enforcing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans runs counter to the obligations and interests we are sworn to uphold," the joint statement said.\par \par \uc2 Florida passed a law that went into effect in July {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-gov-ron-desantis-signs-15-week-abortion-ban-into-law-11649961049"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banning abortions after 15 weeks of pregnancy }}}\uc2 . The law includes exceptions for medical emergencies or "fatal fetal abnormalities." It doesn't include exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis's order said Mr. Warren's refusal to prosecute \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases is sufficient to justify his suspension.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warren also signed a statement in June 2021 alongside more than 70 state prosecutors and attorneys generals that said they wouldn't prosecute crimes related to gender-affirming procedures.\par \par \uc2 "Bills that criminalize safe and crucial medical treatments or the mere public existence of trans people do not promote public safety, community trust, or fiscal responsibility," the letter said. "They serve no legitimate purpose."\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis, in his executive order, noted that Florida has no such law, but said the statements show that Mr. Warren is willing to defy the state legislature.\par \par \uc2 Manny Diaz, chairman of the Florida Democratic Party, said Mr. Warren's suspension was an offensive power grab.\par \par \uc2 "Andrew Warren is an exceptional public servant, duly elected twice by the people of Hillsborough County, who was protecting the freedoms that are supposed to be afforded to Floridians under our constitution," said Mr. Diaz.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warren could choose to appeal his suspension to the state Senate, which then would have six months to conduct a trial, said Dr. Jarvis, the law professor. The Republican-controlled state Senate, however, is unlikely to reverse Mr. DeSantis's decision, he said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Warren could also still run for office again in 2024, Dr. Jarvis said. If he chooses to have a trial in the state Senate, the body could bar him from running again if it ruled against him.\par \par \uc2 Write to Joseph De Avila at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:joseph.deavila@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joseph.deavila@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/florida-ron-desantis-suspends-prosecutor-andrew-warren-abortion-gender-transition-cases-11659629739"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ron DeSantis Suspends Florida Prosecutor Over Pledge to Not Prosecute \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 , Gender-Transition Cases }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220804ei84004ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
