\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2  Wins Missouri GOP Senate Primary as Five States Cast Ballots; Contests settle some high-profile intraparty battles\b0\par\par\uc2 By Aaron Zitner \par \uc2 1,348 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 11:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Missouri Republicans selected \uc2 Eric Schmitt\uc2 , the state's attorney general, as their nominee for a \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  seat on Tuesday, ending a political comeback effort by \uc2 Eric Greitens\uc2 , a former governor who had resigned his office amid sexual-assault allegations.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Schmitt's victory in the Republican-leaning state, projected by the Associated Press, leaves his party in a strong position in the race to replace GOP Sen. \uc2 Roy Blunt\uc2 , who is retiring, and to help the GOP effort to build a majority in what is now a 50-50 Senate.\par \par \uc2 In Kansas, voters surged to the polls and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-voters-weigh-proposed-amendment-on-abortion-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a referendum }}}\uc2  that would have allowed new restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first test of voter sentiment toward \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  limits since the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  in June. With many other states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considering \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions, }}}\uc2  the referendum was closely watched for whether supporters or opponents were motivated the most.\par \par \uc2 The results came as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/primary-election-results-august-2-az-ks-mo-mi-wa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 five states held primary elections }}}\uc2  for federal and statewide office Tuesday. In Michigan, Republicans nominated Tudor Dixon, a political newcomer and conservative commentator, to challenge Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  in what is expected to be one of the most competitive races for governor this November.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, \uc2 Blake Masters\uc2 , who was backed by former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and venture capitalist \uc2 Peter Thiel\uc2 , won the Republican Party's nomination for the \uc2 U.S. Senate\uc2  race, according to the Associated Press. Republicans this year are aiming to defeat Democratic Sen. Mark Kelly, one of the most vulnerable senators seeking re-election, and to reassert their strength in a state that was once a GOP stronghold but which has trended Democratic in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The Republican primary in Missouri had drawn wide attention due to a surge in public opinion polls by Mr. Greitens, which some in the GOP feared would put their hold on the Senate seat at risk. In addition to the allegations of sexual assault and campaign-finance improprieties, which prompted his resignation as governor in 2018, he was accused this year by his ex-wife in court papers of physical abuse. He denied all of those allegations.\par \par \uc2 In an unusual statement Monday evening, Mr. Trump appeared to endorse both Messrs. Schmitt and Greitens, saying he backed "Eric,'' without designating which candidate.\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee will face Trudy Busch Valentine, an \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  beer heir, who won the Democratic primary.\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, Republicans have made Ms. Whitmer a top target among Democratic governors this year. Ms. Dixon, who worked in industrial-equipment sales before starting a conservative news service and becoming an on-air personality on a conservative TV network, said she was prompted to run out of opposition to Ms. Whitmer's business lockdowns and other anti-Covid measures.\par \par \uc2 Her promise to ban mask mandates at schools, oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fight racial and sexual "indoctrination'' in the classroom united Michigan's Republican establishment, and Friday she had won a late endorsement from Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Dixon, according to the Associated Press, defeated former auto dealer Kevin Rinke, who had put $8 million of his own money in the race.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in Michigan, GOP Rep. Peter Meijer narrowly lost the primary for his Grand Rapids-area seat, after he voted to impeach Mr. Trump over the Jan. 6, 2021, attack on the U.S. Capitol. Mr. Meijer was defeated by John Gibbs, a former Trump administration official who had won the former president's endorsement.\par \par \uc2 Democrats ran ads to promote Mr. Gibbs, believing he would be easier to beat in November in a district that tilts slightly Democratic. Mr. Gibbs will face Democrat Hillary Scholten, an attorney.\par \par \uc2 Outside Detroit, Democratic Rep. Haley Stevens defeated a fellow Democratic House member, Rep. \uc2 Andy Levin\uc2 , AP said, in one of the handful of congressional member-against-member primaries created by the new political boundaries drawn with results of the 2020 census.\par \par \uc2 The two lawmakers hold similar stances on most issues, but Mr. Levin, who is from a prominent Jewish family, has been more vocal in criticizing Israel's treatment of Palestinians. That posture drew millions of dollars in spending against him by a super PAC affiliated with the \uc2 American Israel Public Affairs Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The winner will face Mark Ambrose, an Army veteran and chartered financial analyst, who won the Republican primary, the AP projected.\par \par \uc2 In Kansas, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum generated unusually large turnout for a midterm primary election. It had been placed on the ballot by the Republican-led legislature after the state Supreme Court ruled in 2019 that the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is protected under the state constitution. It would affirm that there is no constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and allow state lawmakers to pass laws to regulate the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Kansas voters also set general-election matchups for two of the nation's most vulnerable Democratic political leaders: Kansas Gov. \uc2 Laura Kelly\uc2  and Rep. \uc2 Sharice Davids\uc2 , whose Eastern Kansas district includes Overland Park.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Who do you think will win in the primaries and why? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Kelly will face Republican Derek Schmidt, the state attorney general. Ms. Davids will face Amanda Adkins, a former leader of the state Republican Party, in a rematch of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump's false claims that he won the 2020 election have played a prominent role in Arizona, where many Republicans are critical of the state's top GOP leader, Gov. \uc2 Doug Ducey\uc2 , for certifying President Biden's election win.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Ducey can't run again because of term limits and is backing Karrin Taylor Robson, a property developer, who was also endorsed by former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump has endorsed former television journalist Kari Lake, who has focused much of her campaign on false claims that Mr. Biden's victory in Arizona was fraudulent. Election officials have found no widespread evidence of fraud, and a state GOP-backed audit confirmed Mr. Biden's win.\par \par \uc2 The Republican primary for governor wasn't the only one to divide prominent GOP officials. In the race to replace Ms. Hobbs as secretary of state, Rep. Mark Finchem, who was endorsed by Mr. Trump, beat Beau Lane, an advertising executive backed by Mr. Ducey, and two other Republican candidates. Mr. Finchem has been a leader in the effort to decertify some of the 2020 presidential election results in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 The winner will face either Reginald Bolding, the Democratic leader in the state House of Representatives, or \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2 , formerly the top elections official in Maricopa County, which includes Phoenix. Mr. Fontes narrowly led the Democratic primary Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 In Washington state, the Senate primary will give an early read on the strength of support both for Democratic Sen. \uc2 Patty Murray\uc2 , who is seeking re-election, and her leading challenger, Republican Tiffany Smiley, a nurse and advocate for veterans, including her husband, who was wounded while serving in Iraq.\par \par \uc2 There were 18 candidates on the ballot, but both women easily advanced to the November election under Washington state's primary system, which places contenders from all parties on a single ballot and elevates the top two finishers. Ms. Murray held a substantial lead over Ms. Smiley, but the tally was incomplete.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Smiley, who calls herself a "political outsider'' and "farm girl from rural Washington,'' has posted strong fundraising numbers and generated excitement within the party.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Murray's campaign has run negative ads targeting Ms. Smiley and highlighting her opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Ms. Smiley says that Ms. Murray's votes against banning late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  make her out of step with the views of most Americans.\par \par \uc2 Two Republican House members who voted to impeach Mr. Trump in 2021\u8212\'20\'14Reps. \uc2 Jaime Herrera Beutler\uc2  and \uc2 Dan Newhouse\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14are facing opponents endorsed by Mr. Trump. Both incumbents are expected to advance to the November election under the state's "top two finisher'' system.\par \par \uc2 Write to Aaron Zitner at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:aaron.zitner@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aaron.zitner@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/primary-elections-tuesday-august-2-2022-11659416514"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eric Schmitt Wins Missouri GOP Senate Primary as Five States Cast Ballots }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220802ei82000up\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
