\par\par \uc2 Midterm Election 2022\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Kansas Votes to Protect  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights in State Constitution;  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  now expected to remain legal and accessible in the state\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto and Joe Barrett \par \uc2 1,155 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 05:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 OLATHE, Kan.\u8212\'20\'14Kansas voters soundly rejected a proposed state constitutional amendment that would have ended protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in the first statewide referendum on the issue since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court eliminated \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  at the federal level.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-amendment-is-closely-watched-ahead-of-other-state-referendums-11658579068"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closely watched vote, }}}\uc2  in a conservative-leaning state where Republicans outnumber Democrats, means \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to remain legal and accessible in Kansas. The result, projected by the Associated Press, also provides an early political victory to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters weeks after their resounding defeat at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Where \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Is Legal and Where It Loses Protections Without Roe v. Wade\par \par \uc2 With 90% of the votes counted, about 60% of Kansas voters rejected the amendment, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 The referendum was planned months before the Supreme Court's June 24 ruling that the U.S. Constitution doesn't protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The decision, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/dobbs-v-jackson-womens-health-organization-6-24-2022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\uc2 , upheld \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions in Mississippi and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-does-overturning-roe-v-wade-mean-explained-11656081705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overruled the 1973 decision in Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  that recognized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 The dynamic of the Kansas race changed after the ruling, with the state seeing a wave of national attention and political fundraising. The Kansas primary, normally a sleepy affair, became the focus of intense campaigning, with supporters and opponents of the amendment each spending millions and making emotional appeals to voters through television ads, billboards and door-knocking efforts.\par \par \uc2 About a dozen states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have implemented new curbs on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  since Dobbs and more are expected, while other states are moving to add new protections for the procedure. Kansas was one of a handful of states where the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was uncertain, and both sides looked to Tuesday's primary for clues about voter attitudes on the issue after Dobbs. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
