\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Kansas Vote Signals  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Could Emerge as Top Political Issue in November; Both parties weigh surprise result rejecting constitutional amendment that would have eliminated  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights in the state\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kusisto, Aaron Zitner and Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,454 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 August 2022\par 21:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kansas voters across the political spectrum contributed to Tuesday's strong rejection of a proposed state constitutional amendment that would have eliminated \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state, an outcome that had politicians across the nation assessing the potential impact of the issue in this fall's elections.\par \par \uc2 Some 60% of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-vote-results-11659440554"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas voters rejected }}}\uc2  an amendment that would have explicitly stated there is no right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state's constitution. The ballot measure lost by 18 percentage points in a state that former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a Republican, carried by nearly 15 points two years ago.\par \par \uc2 Many Republican analysts saw a flashing yellow warning sign for their party from the first statewide test of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment since the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-overturns-roe-v-wade-eliminates-constitutional-right-to-abortion-11656080124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade }}}\uc2  in June. With voters agitated by inflation and unsatisfied with President Biden's job performance, most analysts say the election environment favors GOP candidates. But the high turnout for the referendum\u8212\'20\'14which drew about twice the number of votes as in the state's 2018 primaries\u8212\'20\'14suggested to some that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  fight could energize Democrats and sway independent voters.\par \par \uc2 "I think this will alter traditional turnout models, mostly likely in the Democrats' favor,'' said John Truscott, who served as communications chief for former GOP Gov. John Engler in Michigan, where an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  referendum is also likely to be on the ballot this fall. In some close races, he said, renewed attention to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  could tip the balance toward Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's ruling said the U.S. Constitution doesn't guarantee the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that states can determine its legal parameters. Since then, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/where-abortion-is-legal-and-where-it-loses-protections-without-roe-v-wade-11656080346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 number of states }}}\uc2 , especially in parts of the South and Midwest, have moved to ban or heavily restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while others have looked to widen access or enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their constitutions. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents said the result in Kansas was a significant defeat in their efforts to further limit it.\par \par \uc2 The Kansas amendment was rejected or received a mixed reception in several rural counties that had given Mr. Trump 60% and even 70% of their vote in 2020, suggesting that a substantial number of Republicans opposed the measure. Independents also turned out in large numbers, and about a fifth of those voting on the referendum\u8212\'20\'14more than 180,000 people\u8212\'20\'14didn't vote in the day's Republican or Democratic primaries for governor.\par \par \uc2 The results were parsed for their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-courts-abortion-ruling-puts-states-in-spotlight-11656082938"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 implications in states }}}\uc2 such as Michigan, one of the nation's most closely contested battlegrounds. A proposed constitutional amendment enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is likely to be on the ballot there\u8212\'20\'14if approved by elections officials\u8212\'20\'14while voters are also choosing between Democratic Gov. \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and her new Republican opponent, Tudor Dixon, who doesn't.\par \par \uc2 California and Vermont will vote on similar amendments in November. In Kentucky, which has enforced an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, voters will weigh an amendment stating there isn't a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protected in the state's constitution.\par \par \uc2 Coming gubernatorial and legislative races in states such as Georgia, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin could determine the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-abortion-amendment-is-closely-watched-ahead-of-other-state-referendums-11658579068"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 future of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access }}}\uc2  in those states. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  also could be an issue in U.S. House races in suburban districts, poised to be some of the most competitive in the country. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
