\par \par \uc2 People went to the polls on Tuesday in Johnson County, Kan. PHOTO: Fruhlein Chrys Econar/The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 The Kansas results showed a wariness of changing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law but didn't test whether that will motivate voters to choose Democratic candidates, said nonpartisan pollster Bernie Porn, president of EPIC-MRA in Michigan. Still, the GOP "may have miscalculated the intensity of the support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, not only nationwide but in Republican areas,'' Mr. Porn said.\par \par \uc2 Others argued that it wasn't clear that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  would weigh more heavily on voter decisions than other issues. "I still think the biggest issue is going to be the economy," said Sen. \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  (R., Fla.).\par \par \uc2 Micah Roberts, a Republican pollster, said that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights "is an issue that can certainly fire up the left\u8230\'20\'26But at the end of the day, if you can't pay your bills because inflation is at a 40-year high, there's just another force within the conversation."\par \par \uc2 Still, many Democrats say the issue will play to their advantage in races.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 What will be the future for a woman's access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kansas? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "If it's going to happen in Kansas, it's going to happen in a whole lot of states," said Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.). "The strong pro-choice turnout we saw last night in Kansas will continue well into the fall, and Republicans who side with these extremist MAGA policies that attack women's rights do so at their own political risk."\par \par \uc2 State election records show that women accounted for 70% of Kansans who registered to vote after the Supreme Court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling, according to \uc2 Tom Bonier\uc2 , a Democratic voter-data analyst.\par \par \uc2 The referendum was soundly rejected in the state's suburban and metropolitan areas, losing by 16 percentage points in the Wichita area and by 36 points in the area around the Kansas City suburb of Overland Park.\par \par \uc2 Support for the amendment was stronger in the state's rural communities. Still, the results suggested that some Republicans opposed it. In Cowley County, on the southern border with Oklahoma, Mr. Trump drew 68% support in 2020, but voters there narrowly rejected the referendum on Tuesday, 52% to 48%. Mr. Trump had won 72% support in rural Allen County, but voters split evenly on the referendum, with 50% for and against it.\par \par \uc2 Some Republican legislatures around the country have been enacting laws that curb or ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, sometimes with an exception only if the patient's life is in danger. Political analysts said Tuesday's result in Kansas suggests voters may be wary of having such far-reaching laws in their state.\par \par \uc2 "We've found that many voters who would define themselves as pro-life still embrace several exceptions," said Tony Fabrizio, lead pollster for Mr. Trump's two presidential campaigns. "Conversely, many voters who would define themselves as pro-choice would embrace certain time limits.''\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents cautioned against reading too much into Tuesday night's results, which they said were influenced by millions of dollars that poured into the campaign from large donors and wall-to-wall media coverage of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue since the Supreme Court's decision.\par \par \uc2 At least $12 million in advertising poured in to sway voters, split roughly equally between supporters and opponents.\par \par \uc2 The Kansas vote could motivate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters to try to take the issue to voters directly in more states in future years, said Mary Ziegler, a professor at the University of California, Davis School of Law. "It's going to make ballot initiatives seem like a promising tool for Democrats, and especially \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters, who are not sure how this is going to translate into Democratic victories at the polls," she said.\par \par \uc2 The Kansas referendum came in response to a 2019 state Supreme Court ruling that the state's constitution protects the right of personal autonomy, including access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mike Kuckelman, chairman of the Kansas Republican Party, said he was surprised by the wide margins of Tuesday's defeat, which he said will limit what the GOP-led legislature can accomplish in terms of placing limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Without this, it makes it very difficult for them to do much of anything," he said.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, Kansas clinics reported an uptick in patients from states like Oklahoma and Texas after bans on the procedure took effect there.\par \par \uc2 Trust Women, an organization that operates an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Wichita, said providing abortions for people in Kansas and throughout the region will be a priority. The clinic will soon finish construction that will allow two doctors instead of one to work at the same time, making room for more appointments each day, said Zachary Gingrich-Gaylord, a spokesman for the organization.\par \par \uc2 The outcome Tuesday "makes us very optimistic about our opportunities going forward\u8212\'20\'14including working to expand access," he said.\par \par \uc2 Teresa Mettela contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Laura Kusisto at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:laura.kusisto@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laura.kusisto@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Aaron Zitner at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:aaron.zitner@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aaron.zitner@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jennifer Calfas at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jennifer.Calfas@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kansas-vote-signals-abortion-could-emerge-as-top-political-issue-in-november-11659555741"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kansas Vote Signals \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Could Emerge as Top Political Issue in November  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020220803ei83004jx\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 rst=wsjo AND (abortion OR "reproductive rights" OR "reproductive health") AND (atleast5(abortion) OR atleast3("reproductive rights"))\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\c